1
00:00:03,847 --> 00:00:06,446
Hey, why do you keep starting
matches like that?

2
00:00:06,447 --> 00:00:08,813
Why do you always come out so flat?

3
00:00:10,147 --> 00:00:11,513
What's the deal?

4
00:00:13,813 --> 00:00:17,346
Honestly, today's match was
way more straightforward...

5
00:00:17,347 --> 00:00:18,946
than the one against Shujitsu.

6
00:00:18,947 --> 00:00:20,721
Everything they were running
was predictable.

7
00:00:21,039 --> 00:00:24,272
Couldn't you read
what they were going to do?

8
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,979
They only had two hitters,

9
00:00:30,004 --> 00:00:33,801
yet our left-side blockers, Enkhsoyol
and Ye Eun, were all over the place.

10
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:38,246
I told you to lock down that side,
and you couldn't even do that.

11
00:00:38,247 --> 00:00:39,213
(The players were scrambling.)

12
00:00:39,938 --> 00:00:42,071
We drilled defending
against tips and off-speed shots,

13
00:00:42,072 --> 00:00:43,543
and you let every single one drop.

14
00:00:44,038 --> 00:00:46,137
We barely scraped by today.
It was a total mess.

15
00:00:46,138 --> 00:00:47,347
Right down to the final points.

16
00:00:47,548 --> 00:00:49,180
You kept giving them free points
we shouldn't have.

17
00:00:49,205 --> 00:00:51,137
What are you going to do about that?

18
00:00:51,138 --> 00:00:54,372
(They failed to execute
the game plan they'd prepared.)

19
00:00:55,038 --> 00:00:58,071
You need to start thinking
about these things in practice.

20
00:00:58,072 --> 00:01:00,972
Because you treat practice
and real matches so differently,

21
00:01:01,338 --> 00:01:02,204
everything falls apart.

22
00:01:02,205 --> 00:01:05,004
You must bring the same intensity
and focus during practice to the match.

23
00:01:05,005 --> 00:01:07,371
Instead, you tense up when it's game time,

24
00:01:07,372 --> 00:01:08,768
and coast through practice.

25
00:01:10,172 --> 00:01:12,204
I'm telling you to lock in
during practice too.

26
00:01:12,205 --> 00:01:13,937
How do you expect
to perform under pressure...

27
00:01:13,938 --> 00:01:15,842
when you treat practice and matches
like two different worlds?

28
00:01:16,538 --> 00:01:17,537
Do you understand or not?

29
00:01:17,538 --> 00:01:18,578
- We understand.
- Yes, Coach.

30
00:01:24,672 --> 00:01:26,504
This isn't about whether you had
a good or bad day.

31
00:01:26,505 --> 00:01:29,737
It's about executing
the fundamentals we went over.

32
00:01:29,738 --> 00:01:31,347
Because if we can't even do that,
nothing else works.

33
00:01:31,372 --> 00:01:32,605
- Got it?
- Yes, Coach.

34
00:01:33,438 --> 00:01:34,405
Good work today.

35
00:01:35,405 --> 00:01:36,338
Thank you, Coach.

36
00:01:37,438 --> 00:01:39,605
(Current record: 2 wins in 2 matches)

37
00:01:40,405 --> 00:01:42,972
(100 percent win rate)

38
00:01:44,272 --> 00:01:46,805
(Their next opponent is revealed.)

39
00:01:47,672 --> 00:01:51,005
How would you size her up
as a fellow coach?

40
00:01:52,505 --> 00:01:54,205
(Coach Kang Min Sik, Suwon Special City)

41
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:58,672
First, their training volume is no joke.

42
00:01:59,405 --> 00:02:00,917
They're a team built
on solid fundamentals,

43
00:02:00,941 --> 00:02:01,771
so they rarely crumble.

44
00:02:01,772 --> 00:02:05,138
I'd call them pretty relentless.

45
00:02:05,972 --> 00:02:07,894
They went undefeated to win...

46
00:02:07,919 --> 00:02:10,772
the 2024 Danyang Korea
Business Volleyball Tournament,

47
00:02:11,346 --> 00:02:13,979
cementing their spot
as the nation's top team.

48
00:02:14,444 --> 00:02:19,043
I've been leading this team for 22 years,
ever since it was founded.

49
00:02:19,044 --> 00:02:20,378
I'm Head Coach Kim Yun Hye.

50
00:02:20,430 --> 00:02:22,563
And I was also the first
female head coach.

51
00:02:25,396 --> 00:02:27,695
For the past 20 years, volleyball has been
my entire life, year-round.

52
00:02:27,696 --> 00:02:29,529
Earlier this year, I injured my arm
and ended up in a cast.

53
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:31,929
Even then, I drove to matches one-handed.

54
00:02:31,930 --> 00:02:34,729
I've even shown up
to training camps on crutches.

55
00:02:34,730 --> 00:02:36,829
If we can squeeze in practice
even once a week,

56
00:02:36,830 --> 00:02:38,262
we make it happen.

57
00:02:38,263 --> 00:02:39,626
No matter what it takes.

58
00:02:43,896 --> 00:02:46,130
She was here earlier.
I spotted her sitting over there.

59
00:02:48,196 --> 00:02:51,430
(An unwelcome visitor
at the Pink Spiders match)

60
00:02:53,132 --> 00:02:54,726
(Se Yeon, Coach Yun Hye, Gyeong Hyeon
from Pohang Sports Council)

61
00:02:54,751 --> 00:02:57,310
The Pohang Sports Council coach
has her notebook out.

62
00:02:58,236 --> 00:03:00,136
(Logging every rally played
by the Wonder Dogs)

63
00:03:00,936 --> 00:03:03,803
(Scribbling scouting notes furiously,
like Beethoven composing a symphony)

64
00:03:04,036 --> 00:03:08,068
The reason we've won
so many five-set thrillers is...

65
00:03:08,069 --> 00:03:11,403
that we keep grinding
and refuse to let go.

66
00:03:12,103 --> 00:03:14,235
We tell ourselves never to quit
until the final whistle.

67
00:03:14,236 --> 00:03:16,269
We're basically bulldogs.

68
00:03:16,294 --> 00:03:17,969
(Bulldog style?)

69
00:03:18,136 --> 00:03:20,099
You can't just go through the motions!

70
00:03:20,436 --> 00:03:21,835
Hey, Oh Na Young!

71
00:03:23,303 --> 00:03:26,702
(Match Three: Underdogs...)

72
00:03:26,703 --> 00:03:31,069
(vs. Bulldogs)

73
00:03:32,636 --> 00:03:34,136
You have to cover that!

74
00:03:37,763 --> 00:03:41,055
(What's her take
on the Season 2 Wonder Dogs?)

75
00:03:43,603 --> 00:03:47,802
First off, I think this season's
Wonder Dogs might be...

76
00:03:47,803 --> 00:03:49,903
a bit thin in the middle.

77
00:03:54,636 --> 00:03:57,735
And Yeon Joo is playing
opposite now, right?

78
00:03:57,736 --> 00:03:59,069
Well...

79
00:04:02,803 --> 00:04:04,169
I think we can take them.

80
00:04:07,403 --> 00:04:09,603
It's the team unit that's dangerous,
not any single player.

81
00:04:10,503 --> 00:04:13,702
The Wonder Dogs haven't fully gelled yet,

82
00:04:13,703 --> 00:04:15,255
so they're bound to have weak spots.

83
00:04:18,203 --> 00:04:22,003
We spend nearly 300 days
together each year.

84
00:04:22,736 --> 00:04:24,831
There's no way
they can match our chemistry.

85
00:04:26,936 --> 00:04:29,269
(So what's Pohang Sports Council's
lineup?)

86
00:04:29,403 --> 00:04:31,871
That's a secret.
Why would I give that away?

87
00:04:32,203 --> 00:04:33,573
There is one thing I can tell you, though.

88
00:04:34,103 --> 00:04:35,769
Seon Ah, Ho Bin.

89
00:04:36,803 --> 00:04:38,044
You're watching, right?

90
00:04:41,669 --> 00:04:44,269
(Chae Seon Ah, Libero,
Pohang Sports Council)

91
00:04:46,979 --> 00:04:49,545
(Lee Ho Bin, Middle blocker,
Pohang Sports Council)

92
00:04:50,403 --> 00:04:52,835
(In this match,)

93
00:04:52,836 --> 00:04:55,403
(Seon Ah and Ho Bin...)

94
00:04:56,036 --> 00:04:58,836
(will suit up for Pohang Sports Council.)

95
00:05:09,836 --> 00:05:10,869
I honestly feel...

96
00:05:11,669 --> 00:05:16,736
Seon Ah has played a huge role as captain.

97
00:05:17,595 --> 00:05:19,903
We've decided...

98
00:05:20,103 --> 00:05:21,768
that Seon Ah will serve
as our team captain.

99
00:05:21,769 --> 00:05:24,168
We're counting on you
to lead the squad well.

100
00:05:24,169 --> 00:05:27,068
Chae Rim, watch the back-row attack
when you're blocking on the left.

101
00:05:27,069 --> 00:05:28,168
You let one slip by earlier.

102
00:05:28,169 --> 00:05:29,035
Don't let that happen again.

103
00:05:29,036 --> 00:05:30,335
It's alright. You're doing great.

104
00:05:30,336 --> 00:05:31,664
I love the aggression, Chae Rim.

105
00:05:32,169 --> 00:05:34,636
(Captain Chae, who has always been
the heart and soul of the team)

106
00:05:37,269 --> 00:05:39,436
(Libero Seon Ah: Out)

107
00:05:40,503 --> 00:05:42,936
(Middle blocker Ho Bin: Out)

108
00:05:45,036 --> 00:05:48,735
(They're forced to compete
without two core players.)

109
00:05:48,736 --> 00:05:50,868
With those two back on our side,

110
00:05:50,869 --> 00:05:52,485
there's no way our squad loses.

111
00:05:52,969 --> 00:05:56,369
(One Team)

112
00:05:58,136 --> 00:06:00,402
As everyone knows, nothing beats family.

113
00:06:00,403 --> 00:06:01,803
(Pohang Sports Council at full strength)

114
00:06:02,369 --> 00:06:06,335
Coach Kim was a world-class superstar,
and she still is.

115
00:06:06,336 --> 00:06:09,502
But for better or worse,
I've spent 22 years on this sideline...

116
00:06:09,503 --> 00:06:11,268
and built up a wealth of experience.

117
00:06:11,269 --> 00:06:14,669
And the competitive fire forged
over those 22 years will prevail.

118
00:06:17,636 --> 00:06:21,369
Coach Yun Hye may have
22 years of experience,

119
00:06:21,803 --> 00:06:23,336
but at the end of the day,
skill decides it.

120
00:06:23,936 --> 00:06:25,868
Yeon Koung is fiercely competitive too.

121
00:06:25,893 --> 00:06:27,244
And I hate losing
just as much as she does.

122
00:06:28,041 --> 00:06:30,148
We can't lose to her team.

123
00:06:30,682 --> 00:06:31,715
I'm sorry.

124
00:06:33,148 --> 00:06:34,615
But I think we've got this.

125
00:06:35,257 --> 00:06:37,290
I don't care if it goes to five sets,
as long as we win.

126
00:06:37,657 --> 00:06:39,741
A 3 to 0 sweep wouldn't be
much of a contest.

127
00:06:39,766 --> 00:06:40,667
It would be ideal.

128
00:06:41,024 --> 00:06:42,457
A clean sweep, right?

129
00:06:42,524 --> 00:06:44,023
Watch the tip!

130
00:06:44,024 --> 00:06:47,889
(Two years...)

131
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:52,657
(vs. 22 years)

132
00:06:53,490 --> 00:06:54,923
Let's go all out.

133
00:06:54,924 --> 00:06:56,990
(The Wonder Dogs' guts)

134
00:06:57,190 --> 00:06:59,489
We want to show them our grit.

135
00:06:59,490 --> 00:07:00,956
(Pohang Sports Council's grit)

136
00:07:00,957 --> 00:07:02,690
Hurry, get in!

137
00:07:02,890 --> 00:07:05,423
(A fierce showdown)

138
00:07:05,424 --> 00:07:06,490
Can I have this?

139
00:07:06,519 --> 00:07:07,779
(Wonder Dogs' roster)

140
00:07:14,057 --> 00:07:17,057
I know those players inside and out.

141
00:07:17,190 --> 00:07:18,424
I think that'll make things
more interesting.

142
00:07:18,890 --> 00:07:22,523
I believe players should give their all
wherever they play.

143
00:07:22,524 --> 00:07:26,123
As captain of Pohang Sports Council,
I'll lead my squad...

144
00:07:26,124 --> 00:07:28,024
and try to take down the Wonder Dogs.

145
00:07:28,590 --> 00:07:31,690
I want to show them
what I'm really capable of.

146
00:07:32,090 --> 00:07:34,724
I hope they realize
what they're missing out on.

147
00:07:35,457 --> 00:07:37,924
(And another player
from Pohang Sports Council)

148
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:43,756
I'm gutted and frustrated
that I can't play.

149
00:07:43,757 --> 00:07:47,857
Words can't describe how I feel.

150
00:07:50,357 --> 00:07:51,389
Everyone, gather around.

151
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:52,423
(A few days ago, after practice)

152
00:07:52,424 --> 00:07:53,457
You too, Song Hee.

153
00:07:57,124 --> 00:07:58,324
I don't know if you've heard,

154
00:07:58,690 --> 00:08:01,957
but Song Hee went to the hospital today.

155
00:08:02,324 --> 00:08:05,524
Her knee is in pretty bad shape,
so she's going to need surgery.

156
00:08:08,490 --> 00:08:09,489
Free ball!

157
00:08:09,490 --> 00:08:12,024
(During practice for the Shujitsu match)

158
00:08:14,690 --> 00:08:15,723
Hold on!

159
00:08:15,724 --> 00:08:17,524
- She's down!
- What happened?

160
00:08:17,690 --> 00:08:18,723
I'm sorry.

161
00:08:18,724 --> 00:08:21,057
(Song Hee injured her knee
during practice.)

162
00:08:23,057 --> 00:08:24,157
Does it still hurt?

163
00:08:24,990 --> 00:08:25,990
Not as much.

164
00:08:26,157 --> 00:08:27,589
- What?
- Not as bad as earlier.

165
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,556
(Her knee is badly swollen.)

166
00:08:29,557 --> 00:08:32,789
We'll apply some ointment for now,
but we need to check your ligaments.

167
00:08:32,790 --> 00:08:34,857
Let us know when the pain subsides.

168
00:08:36,124 --> 00:08:38,518
We'll have to get it examined
once the swelling goes down.

169
00:08:38,543 --> 00:08:40,209
It's going to take some time.

170
00:08:40,690 --> 00:08:43,089
If the pain doesn't ease up
in about five minutes,

171
00:08:43,090 --> 00:08:44,457
we'll have to take this wrap off.

172
00:08:45,324 --> 00:08:47,390
(She watched the matches
from the sidelines.)

173
00:08:48,890 --> 00:08:54,057
(She seemed to be on the mend.)

174
00:08:54,724 --> 00:08:55,723
Hello.

175
00:08:55,724 --> 00:08:57,056
Right this way. You came in person.

176
00:08:57,057 --> 00:08:58,056
Yes.

177
00:08:58,057 --> 00:08:59,323
(She visited the hospital
after the swelling went down.)

178
00:08:59,324 --> 00:09:00,323
- Hello.
- Hello.

179
00:09:00,324 --> 00:09:02,023
- Hi.
- Hello.

180
00:09:02,024 --> 00:09:03,690
Let's take a look at your knee.

181
00:09:04,290 --> 00:09:05,823
She got hurt on the landing.

182
00:09:05,824 --> 00:09:06,824
Okay.

183
00:09:07,324 --> 00:09:09,690
We kept checking both of her knees.

184
00:09:10,524 --> 00:09:11,824
- That spot was sticking out a bit.
- Right.

185
00:09:12,224 --> 00:09:14,824
- So the doctors were concerned.
- I see.

186
00:09:17,090 --> 00:09:19,990
- Well, first off,
- Give us the main takeaway.

187
00:09:20,457 --> 00:09:24,757
the meniscus is
a crucial part of your knee.

188
00:09:24,957 --> 00:09:26,589
Fortunately, it looks intact.

189
00:09:26,590 --> 00:09:27,589
- Okay.
- All right.

190
00:09:27,590 --> 00:09:28,824
However,

191
00:09:31,357 --> 00:09:33,506
you've torn
your anterior cruciate ligament.

192
00:09:34,390 --> 00:09:35,690
Your ACL.

193
00:09:35,890 --> 00:09:37,177
- Okay.
- As far as recovery goes,

194
00:09:37,224 --> 00:09:40,356
you'd be back in four months
if you were just jogging.

195
00:09:40,357 --> 00:09:44,156
But volleyball-specific training
takes seven to eight months.

196
00:09:44,157 --> 00:09:47,257
I'm afraid it'll take nine to ten months
to make a full recovery.

197
00:09:47,724 --> 00:09:49,356
You'll need to work
on regaining flexion...

198
00:09:49,357 --> 00:09:50,625
and extension in your knee.

199
00:09:50,649 --> 00:09:52,358
It'll also take a month
just to walk normally again.

200
00:09:57,933 --> 00:09:59,633
To reconstruct the ligament,

201
00:09:59,823 --> 00:10:02,590
we can use an autograft
from your own tissue...

202
00:10:02,783 --> 00:10:05,038
or a donor graft, though using
your own tissue is better.

203
00:10:05,883 --> 00:10:08,183
The silver lining is
that your meniscus is undamaged,

204
00:10:08,383 --> 00:10:10,017
so with proper surgery and rehab,

205
00:10:10,183 --> 00:10:12,849
you'll be able to make a smooth comeback.

206
00:10:12,850 --> 00:10:13,850
- Okay?
- Yes.

207
00:10:16,117 --> 00:10:17,383
Thank you.

208
00:10:31,317 --> 00:10:32,550
It's okay.

209
00:10:33,950 --> 00:10:37,250
This is my first serious injury.

210
00:10:38,283 --> 00:10:39,539
I guess that's why it hits so hard.

211
00:10:46,883 --> 00:10:47,917
You're tearing up.

212
00:10:50,483 --> 00:10:52,650
Here. It's okay.

213
00:10:53,150 --> 00:10:55,083
Injuries happen to everyone.

214
00:10:55,983 --> 00:10:59,117
Things have gone smoothly so far,
so you'll be fine.

215
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:01,961
Just focus on getting healthy.

216
00:11:02,917 --> 00:11:06,783
(Song Hee's unexpected
season-ending injury)

217
00:11:07,417 --> 00:11:08,583
Don't cry. It's okay.

218
00:11:14,417 --> 00:11:18,116
I wanted to learn so much...

219
00:11:18,117 --> 00:11:20,513
and play alongside you guys...

220
00:11:21,217 --> 00:11:23,117
for the full two months.

221
00:11:24,683 --> 00:11:26,550
I hate that it had to end like this.

222
00:11:29,317 --> 00:11:33,650
I'll be rooting for all of you
to stay healthy...

223
00:11:36,050 --> 00:11:39,683
and finish the season strong.

224
00:11:40,550 --> 00:11:41,650
Thank you.

225
00:11:49,783 --> 00:11:54,117
Song Hee and I had been teammates
since Season One.

226
00:11:54,683 --> 00:11:55,683
So I was...

227
00:11:56,617 --> 00:11:57,683
really heartbroken.

228
00:12:01,583 --> 00:12:02,583
Don't cry.

229
00:12:05,250 --> 00:12:06,750
Don't cry, Song Hee.

230
00:12:08,050 --> 00:12:09,050
It's okay.

231
00:12:11,650 --> 00:12:12,650
Song Hee.

232
00:12:13,583 --> 00:12:15,550
- Thank you, Min Kyeong.
- I cried too.

233
00:12:16,217 --> 00:12:19,205
Song Hee, you've got strong leg muscles,
so you'll bounce back in no time.

234
00:12:21,112 --> 00:12:22,949
Even Yeon Joo came back
from four surgeries.

235
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:24,017
- Yes.
- Exactly.

236
00:12:25,317 --> 00:12:27,283
- Keep your chin up.
- You've got this.

237
00:12:29,350 --> 00:12:31,384
I knew all too well
what she was going through,

238
00:12:32,650 --> 00:12:35,150
so I just had to reassure her like that.

239
00:12:37,017 --> 00:12:42,117
(Knowing the toll of a knee injury,)

240
00:12:42,817 --> 00:12:46,349
Nobody is hurting more
than she is right now.

241
00:12:46,350 --> 00:12:47,383
(she struggles to walk away.)

242
00:12:47,817 --> 00:12:48,850
So it broke my heart.

243
00:12:50,850 --> 00:12:52,782
(Patting)

244
00:12:52,783 --> 00:12:54,783
I wanted to keep the speech light,

245
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:57,083
but I got too choked up.

246
00:12:59,083 --> 00:13:00,117
Best of luck.

247
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:02,682
We'll play our hearts out for you.

248
00:13:02,683 --> 00:13:03,717
Song Hee.

249
00:13:04,350 --> 00:13:05,417
Good luck, Young In.

250
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:07,716
Come on!

251
00:13:07,717 --> 00:13:09,382
(They comfort her in their own ways.)

252
00:13:09,383 --> 00:13:11,883
- Go get warmed up.
- Okay.

253
00:13:14,683 --> 00:13:16,150
"I was completely fine."

254
00:13:16,917 --> 00:13:18,417
"I could've done so well."

255
00:13:19,017 --> 00:13:21,217
Thoughts like that stung even more.

256
00:13:21,483 --> 00:13:23,917
Other players are in the pro league now,

257
00:13:24,117 --> 00:13:25,483
and Enkhsoyol made it too.

258
00:13:25,983 --> 00:13:29,409
So I thought I might actually have a shot.

259
00:13:30,896 --> 00:13:34,229
(The second tryout, full of hope)

260
00:13:35,196 --> 00:13:38,661
(A dream right within her reach)

261
00:13:38,662 --> 00:13:40,295
It was my ultimate goal.

262
00:13:40,296 --> 00:13:41,395
(The dream she clung to until surgery day)

263
00:13:41,396 --> 00:13:43,895
I believed going pro would be
the best path for me.

264
00:13:43,896 --> 00:13:45,029
(Song Hee, a pro player)

265
00:13:46,262 --> 00:13:49,895
(To keep her pro dreams alive,)

266
00:13:49,896 --> 00:13:50,928
We'll be right back.

267
00:13:50,929 --> 00:13:52,695
- I'll be back soon.
- You've got this.

268
00:13:52,696 --> 00:13:53,896
(Song Hee opted for surgery.)

269
00:13:55,062 --> 00:13:58,861
(Post-op, she's pouring everything
into her rehab.)

270
00:13:58,862 --> 00:14:01,062
(Song Hee's run with the Wonder Dogs
may be over for now,)

271
00:14:01,929 --> 00:14:05,896
(but her dream of turning pro lives on.)

272
00:14:06,462 --> 00:14:09,729
She was a reliable hitter,

273
00:14:09,862 --> 00:14:12,462
so it's definitely a concern.

274
00:14:12,829 --> 00:14:14,628
It's been weighing on my mind.

275
00:14:14,629 --> 00:14:18,362
The match against Pohang Sports Council
is right around the corner.

276
00:14:18,896 --> 00:14:21,228
I'm trying to figure out
how to configure our lineup.

277
00:14:21,229 --> 00:14:22,461
(A sudden gap at outside hitter)

278
00:14:22,462 --> 00:14:25,696
I suppose we'll need
another outside hitter.

279
00:14:25,796 --> 00:14:26,862
- Yes.
- Right.

280
00:14:27,996 --> 00:14:30,362
Who else was at the tryouts?

281
00:14:30,762 --> 00:14:31,829
The girl from Yangsan?

282
00:14:32,162 --> 00:14:33,461
- She looked pretty solid.
- Right?

283
00:14:33,462 --> 00:14:35,642
- I think she handled some serve receive.
- Her passing was decent.

284
00:14:36,896 --> 00:14:39,595
(That night)

285
00:14:39,596 --> 00:14:40,796
(Knocking)

286
00:14:41,162 --> 00:14:43,328
Yeon Joo, I'm heading out.

287
00:14:43,329 --> 00:14:44,796
(Yeon Joo)

288
00:14:44,929 --> 00:14:46,661
- Safe travels.
- Sure.

289
00:14:46,662 --> 00:14:48,296
See you on the court.

290
00:14:48,362 --> 00:14:51,329
- You're our rival now. Get going.
- See you soon, Yeon Joo.

291
00:14:52,529 --> 00:14:53,596
Bye.

292
00:14:54,262 --> 00:14:57,395
(Ho Bin, Seon Ah, and Song Hee)

293
00:14:57,396 --> 00:14:59,796
(The Pohang Sports Council players
return to their squad.)

294
00:15:00,596 --> 00:15:01,595
(Six days left)

295
00:15:01,596 --> 00:15:02,735
Open up your vision.

296
00:15:02,829 --> 00:15:04,871
I don't need much of a warm-up.

297
00:15:05,229 --> 00:15:08,007
- It takes me a while to get warmed up.
- What time should we kick things off?

298
00:15:08,654 --> 00:15:11,788
(Approaching)

299
00:15:15,429 --> 00:15:16,429
Welcome.

300
00:15:19,362 --> 00:15:20,362
You scared me!

301
00:15:21,862 --> 00:15:24,216
(A familiar face to the players as well?)

302
00:15:29,502 --> 00:15:33,502
(In Season 1's match
against Geunyoung Girls' High,)

303
00:15:34,142 --> 00:15:36,909
(Yoon Ha stood out as the ace.)

304
00:15:38,942 --> 00:15:42,642
(She entered the 2025-2026 rookie draft,)

305
00:15:45,409 --> 00:15:48,275
(but went undrafted.)

306
00:15:48,889 --> 00:15:50,323
(She then tried out for Season Two.)

307
00:15:56,756 --> 00:15:58,923
Yoon Ha has serious hops.

308
00:16:01,323 --> 00:16:02,923
(From deft tips...)

309
00:16:03,523 --> 00:16:05,889
(to sharp line shots)

310
00:16:06,456 --> 00:16:08,256
Nice swing. Clean hit.

311
00:16:09,123 --> 00:16:11,323
- Yoon Ha's looking sharp.
- Yeah, she really is.

312
00:16:11,714 --> 00:16:13,113
How have I never noticed her before?

313
00:16:13,114 --> 00:16:14,680
She gets way up there too.

314
00:16:14,681 --> 00:16:16,314
(Outside hitter Yoon Ha turned heads.)

315
00:16:16,914 --> 00:16:19,081
When I didn't make the cut last time,

316
00:16:19,229 --> 00:16:22,581
I thought that was it for me.

317
00:16:22,848 --> 00:16:26,248
It feels like I've been given
a second chance.

318
00:16:26,914 --> 00:16:31,647
Yoon Ha impressed us at the tryout,

319
00:16:31,648 --> 00:16:36,114
and we felt she could fill the void
left by Song Hee,

320
00:16:36,381 --> 00:16:38,448
so we decided to bring her on board.

321
00:16:39,281 --> 00:16:41,380
I'll give it everything I've got.

322
00:16:41,381 --> 00:16:43,414
- Thanks for having me.
- Welcome to the squad.

323
00:16:46,314 --> 00:16:50,181
(Welcome, Kim Yoon Ha!)

324
00:16:50,881 --> 00:16:54,081
Now there's someone younger
I can look out for.

325
00:16:54,814 --> 00:16:56,381
It's a new feeling for me.

326
00:16:57,148 --> 00:16:58,581
(A quick glance)

327
00:17:00,481 --> 00:17:03,181
(And another glance)

328
00:17:04,448 --> 00:17:06,914
(She kept sneaking glances...)

329
00:17:07,748 --> 00:17:10,748
(at Yoon Ha, two years her junior.)

330
00:17:11,314 --> 00:17:12,981
She's still young,

331
00:17:13,414 --> 00:17:17,214
so I feel like I should take her
under my wing.

332
00:17:17,914 --> 00:17:22,014
I've always been the youngest,
with everyone looking out for me.

333
00:17:23,214 --> 00:17:24,848
So now I want to...

334
00:17:25,214 --> 00:17:29,081
pass on the warmth I've received.

335
00:17:30,348 --> 00:17:31,584
How does the rotation go?

336
00:17:31,714 --> 00:17:34,241
(At 21, Enkhsoyol steps
into a big-sister role...)

337
00:17:34,265 --> 00:17:35,614
(for 19-year-old Yoon Ha.)

338
00:17:36,581 --> 00:17:40,514
(And now Tsubaki's here too.)

339
00:17:40,948 --> 00:17:43,880
(Enkhsoyol takes on a new role.)

340
00:17:43,881 --> 00:17:44,947
Are you worn out?

341
00:17:44,948 --> 00:17:45,932
Was practice rough today?

342
00:17:46,340 --> 00:17:49,393
(Someone else dotes
on the youngest players too.)

343
00:17:51,581 --> 00:17:53,172
- How's the workout going?
- Hello, Coach.

344
00:17:53,481 --> 00:17:55,308
- Did you get a solid session in?
- Yes.

345
00:17:55,581 --> 00:17:58,713
For athletes, staying in peak condition
is everything.

346
00:17:58,714 --> 00:17:59,913
- Right?
- Yes.

347
00:17:59,914 --> 00:18:03,714
You need to know your probiotics
to keep your gut in check.

348
00:18:04,214 --> 00:18:05,813
- You know that, Tsubaki?
- Yes.

349
00:18:05,814 --> 00:18:07,448
So I brought you these.

350
00:18:07,681 --> 00:18:09,613
- Here you go, Tsubaki.
- Thank you.

351
00:18:09,614 --> 00:18:11,248
- Enkhsoyol.
- Thank you.

352
00:18:11,481 --> 00:18:12,313
(Thrilled)

353
00:18:12,314 --> 00:18:14,714
This is the strain number.

354
00:18:19,381 --> 00:18:21,547
You always want to check
the strain number.

355
00:18:21,548 --> 00:18:23,980
That way, you know
what each strain actually does,

356
00:18:23,981 --> 00:18:26,014
so check before you buy. Got it?

357
00:18:28,581 --> 00:18:31,148
- Thank you.
- Thank you!

358
00:18:32,748 --> 00:18:34,981
(Meanwhile, at Pohang Sports Council)

359
00:18:35,448 --> 00:18:36,548
Take it square on.

360
00:18:36,983 --> 00:18:41,383
(Seon Ah and Ho Bin train
with their home club.)

361
00:18:42,283 --> 00:18:46,083
(The Wonder Dogs' coaching staff
looks concerned.)

362
00:18:46,683 --> 00:18:47,727
Are we going to be okay?

363
00:18:48,349 --> 00:18:49,496
That's definitely a concern.

364
00:18:57,883 --> 00:19:00,082
We desperately need Young In to step up.

365
00:19:00,083 --> 00:19:01,215
We need her back in form.

366
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:04,315
This was never the plan for Yeon Joo.

367
00:19:04,849 --> 00:19:07,034
She was supposed to sub in,

368
00:19:07,058 --> 00:19:08,848
help stabilize things,
and sub right back out.

369
00:19:08,849 --> 00:19:10,616
Instead, we've had her out there nonstop.

370
00:19:12,016 --> 00:19:15,083
(Yeon Joo filled in for Young In.)

371
00:19:16,249 --> 00:19:19,916
(Flame Deer played every single set.)

372
00:19:21,516 --> 00:19:23,815
I could feel my energy draining
faster and faster.

373
00:19:23,816 --> 00:19:25,849
It was really grueling.

374
00:19:26,383 --> 00:19:28,215
We have some tough matches coming up,

375
00:19:28,216 --> 00:19:30,349
and I don't think Yeon Joo
can sustain this pace.

376
00:19:30,716 --> 00:19:33,948
We need more firepower on offense too.

377
00:19:33,949 --> 00:19:35,649
Young In has to produce. If she doesn't,

378
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:37,610
we're going to struggle to win.

379
00:19:37,849 --> 00:19:40,915
We need another scoring option,
and right now we don't have one.

380
00:19:40,916 --> 00:19:42,383
(A plan to get Young In back on track)

381
00:19:43,883 --> 00:19:45,758
If Young In could just get
her back-row attack going...

382
00:19:45,783 --> 00:19:47,220
She's been drilling her back-row attack.

383
00:19:47,649 --> 00:19:49,648
(A weapon Coach Kim has been
eager to deploy)

384
00:19:49,649 --> 00:19:51,849
(Back-row attacks)

385
00:19:53,483 --> 00:19:55,649
(A back-row hitter joins the offense,)

386
00:19:56,083 --> 00:19:57,849
(catching the defense off guard.)

387
00:19:58,116 --> 00:20:00,048
For our back-row attack,

388
00:20:00,049 --> 00:20:02,583
I pulled some game tape for us to study.

389
00:20:04,616 --> 00:20:07,182
Sharing files is
so much easier these days.

390
00:20:07,183 --> 00:20:09,115
It used to only work
between phones of the same brand,

391
00:20:09,116 --> 00:20:11,611
but now you can send them
across different brands too.

392
00:20:13,049 --> 00:20:17,149
A few D-balls here,
and we'd be in great shape.

393
00:20:18,359 --> 00:20:19,524
(D-ball, aka zero)

394
00:20:19,549 --> 00:20:22,249
(Right-side back-row attack)

395
00:20:23,349 --> 00:20:25,483
As for the zero,

396
00:20:26,449 --> 00:20:27,583
who can run it?

397
00:20:29,049 --> 00:20:30,216
Young In, right?

398
00:20:30,516 --> 00:20:31,548
Either Yeon Joo or Young In.

399
00:20:31,549 --> 00:20:33,415
But Young In packs more power,

400
00:20:33,416 --> 00:20:34,801
so it really needs to be her.

401
00:20:37,816 --> 00:20:39,583
That's the crux of the issue.

402
00:20:40,149 --> 00:20:45,115
If Young In can't establish
her right-side offense,

403
00:20:45,116 --> 00:20:51,216
we'll end up forcing everything
to the left again,

404
00:20:52,316 --> 00:20:56,648
and our attack becomes
completely one-dimensional.

405
00:20:56,649 --> 00:21:00,282
So we desperately need
Young In to deliver.

406
00:21:00,283 --> 00:21:02,048
That's the only way we win...

407
00:21:02,049 --> 00:21:04,149
and grow as a team.

408
00:21:04,516 --> 00:21:08,416
Here's our game plan for this matchup.

409
00:21:08,783 --> 00:21:10,770
We're going to run
more back-row attacks...

410
00:21:10,983 --> 00:21:15,982
and generate more offense
from the right pin.

411
00:21:15,983 --> 00:21:17,682
If our back-row attack stalls out,

412
00:21:17,683 --> 00:21:20,748
our offensive options shrink fast.

413
00:21:20,749 --> 00:21:22,615
That's why it's so critical for us.

414
00:21:22,616 --> 00:21:26,185
We have to get it clicking
for the rest of the season too.

415
00:21:26,359 --> 00:21:27,824
And who needs to step up?

416
00:21:27,849 --> 00:21:30,382
Her. If she doesn't step up,

417
00:21:30,383 --> 00:21:32,948
we're out of options.

418
00:21:32,949 --> 00:21:35,361
Otherwise, we'll have to waive her
and bring someone else in.

419
00:21:37,749 --> 00:21:39,615
If she can't produce, we'll make a trade.

420
00:21:39,616 --> 00:21:43,716
Anyway, we'll dial in your timing
with the setter. Alright?

421
00:21:44,149 --> 00:21:45,905
The rest of you are dismissed for dinner.

422
00:21:46,783 --> 00:21:47,949
Young In, stay behind.

423
00:21:56,616 --> 00:21:57,884
Everyone else, clear out. Let's go.

424
00:21:58,983 --> 00:22:01,215
- Good work today.
- Yes.

425
00:22:01,216 --> 00:22:03,749
(The players file out one by one.)

426
00:22:09,183 --> 00:22:11,349
(Young In stays behind with the coaches.)

427
00:22:12,716 --> 00:22:13,649
Alright.

428
00:22:15,383 --> 00:22:18,549
Time for a 1-on-1 film session
with Young In.

429
00:22:19,216 --> 00:22:20,349
Let's get into it.

430
00:22:21,316 --> 00:22:22,716
(Gulping)

431
00:22:24,716 --> 00:22:29,216
How do you prepare mentally for a match?

432
00:22:29,749 --> 00:22:31,701
What was your mindset
heading into the Shujitsu match?

433
00:22:34,483 --> 00:22:35,483
Well...

434
00:22:39,383 --> 00:22:42,016
Mostly, I just wanted to apply
what I'd worked on in practice.

435
00:22:43,349 --> 00:22:44,931
Don't give me that nonsense.

436
00:22:45,549 --> 00:22:47,133
Quit talking in vague generalities.

437
00:22:49,749 --> 00:22:51,615
So you walk into today's match thinking,

438
00:22:51,616 --> 00:22:52,448
"Today,"

439
00:22:52,449 --> 00:22:53,582
(Eyes shut)

440
00:22:53,583 --> 00:22:58,982
"I hope I can execute what I practiced."

441
00:22:58,983 --> 00:23:00,915
"I'll go out there and try my best."

442
00:23:00,916 --> 00:23:02,148
Is that what was in your head?

443
00:23:02,283 --> 00:23:03,682
Maybe in a sports manga.

444
00:23:03,683 --> 00:23:06,248
You can get away with that
in a comic book,

445
00:23:06,249 --> 00:23:07,983
but this is the real world.

446
00:23:10,416 --> 00:23:12,348
You need a concrete game plan.

447
00:23:12,349 --> 00:23:13,315
Map it out before first serve.

448
00:23:13,316 --> 00:23:15,315
"If they give me this look,
I'll take that shot."

449
00:23:15,316 --> 00:23:17,682
Even if you walk in
with a counter for every scenario,

450
00:23:17,683 --> 00:23:19,716
there's no guarantee it'll pan out.

451
00:23:23,349 --> 00:23:24,548
Look at what you're doing right here.

452
00:23:24,549 --> 00:23:25,483
Roll the clip.

453
00:23:27,149 --> 00:23:31,049
(Young In needs to put this ball away.)

454
00:23:33,349 --> 00:23:35,282
When you're swinging,

455
00:23:35,283 --> 00:23:38,848
I don't mind an error as long as I can see
the intent behind your shot.

456
00:23:38,849 --> 00:23:39,649
Yes, Coach.

457
00:23:40,392 --> 00:23:42,815
Say the block is only this high,
or there's a seam open.

458
00:23:42,816 --> 00:23:44,616
Or you can tool the block
off the outside hand.

459
00:23:44,883 --> 00:23:49,249
Or if she sets a high ball,
you can target the deep corner.

460
00:23:49,583 --> 00:23:51,227
The block is low,
yet you bury it in the net.

461
00:23:51,251 --> 00:23:52,082
Where were you even aiming?

462
00:23:52,083 --> 00:23:54,148
I can't tell at all
what you were trying to hit.

463
00:23:54,149 --> 00:23:55,749
You're just swinging blindly. Look.

464
00:23:56,249 --> 00:23:57,816
(Swinging without a clear target...)

465
00:23:58,383 --> 00:24:00,683
(and coming up empty every time)

466
00:24:00,983 --> 00:24:02,682
You just keep hammering the ball.

467
00:24:02,683 --> 00:24:04,148
A hundred swings,
every single one identical.

468
00:24:04,149 --> 00:24:07,115
You keep hitting the same spot,
and they keep digging it up.

469
00:24:07,116 --> 00:24:10,748
What's the point of hitting into the teeth
of the defense over and over?

470
00:24:10,749 --> 00:24:12,582
Picture a glass door.

471
00:24:12,583 --> 00:24:15,482
You keep sprinting straight into it.

472
00:24:15,483 --> 00:24:16,916
Is that going to open the door?

473
00:24:17,249 --> 00:24:18,982
Will slamming into it again make it budge?

474
00:24:18,983 --> 00:24:22,248
- No, it still won't open.
- No.

475
00:24:22,249 --> 00:24:23,729
That's literally what you're doing.

476
00:24:24,349 --> 00:24:25,552
Watching this tape,

477
00:24:25,576 --> 00:24:27,516
we have zero clue
what you were trying to do.

478
00:24:29,716 --> 00:24:30,683
What's your take?

479
00:24:31,349 --> 00:24:34,783
How do you assess your performance
through these first two matches?

480
00:24:38,049 --> 00:24:39,249
Well...

481
00:24:40,283 --> 00:24:42,248
After I missed my first swing,

482
00:24:42,249 --> 00:24:44,049
nerves got the best of me.

483
00:24:47,749 --> 00:24:49,015
Was that the first time that's happened?

484
00:24:49,016 --> 00:24:52,448
No, I just kept telling myself
I couldn't afford another error,

485
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:54,749
so I started playing it safe
and tipping instead of swinging.

486
00:25:11,749 --> 00:25:15,749
You haven't watched tape
of your own attacks yet, have you?

487
00:25:16,949 --> 00:25:18,117
You haven't seen this, right?

488
00:25:20,495 --> 00:25:22,421
It was too painful to watch, so I didn't.

489
00:25:23,821 --> 00:25:25,422
(Sighing)

490
00:25:28,407 --> 00:25:29,407
That sounds a bit...

491
00:25:29,875 --> 00:25:33,265
defeatist, to be honest.

492
00:25:38,817 --> 00:25:41,051
You really need to...

493
00:25:41,654 --> 00:25:43,421
- watch your game tape more.
- Yes.

494
00:25:43,689 --> 00:25:44,922
You have to do it on your own...

495
00:25:44,923 --> 00:25:47,158
and look at it objectively.

496
00:25:48,761 --> 00:25:50,795
You have great physical tools.

497
00:25:51,563 --> 00:25:53,697
You have a lot going for you.

498
00:25:53,966 --> 00:25:57,134
It's just the mechanics
that aren't clicking yet.

499
00:25:57,269 --> 00:26:01,004
You can become a much better player
if you iron out those issues.

500
00:26:01,005 --> 00:26:03,173
That's the effort
I'm not seeing right now.

501
00:26:04,176 --> 00:26:05,443
You really have to think the game.

502
00:26:05,444 --> 00:26:07,166
Keep volleyball on your mind more.

503
00:26:07,880 --> 00:26:09,780
Let's put in the work
to improve, Young In.

504
00:26:10,149 --> 00:26:11,683
You're capable of much more.

505
00:26:13,452 --> 00:26:18,056
(Episode 6: The Key to Improvement)

506
00:26:18,357 --> 00:26:21,526
Looking back on it now,
it really does sound like an excuse.

507
00:26:22,394 --> 00:26:25,896
I was just disappointed in myself.

508
00:26:27,099 --> 00:26:30,301
My mom used to play volleyball.

509
00:26:31,370 --> 00:26:33,671
She never made it to a pro team either.

510
00:26:34,540 --> 00:26:37,342
If I could give my parents one gift,

511
00:26:37,609 --> 00:26:39,877
it would be making a pro roster.

512
00:26:40,245 --> 00:26:42,401
So when I went undrafted
in the first draft...

513
00:26:42,982 --> 00:26:46,484
and the second draft,

514
00:26:46,485 --> 00:26:47,485
(Young In experienced two defeats.)

515
00:26:47,486 --> 00:26:50,154
I thought about walking away
from volleyball.

516
00:26:50,155 --> 00:26:51,589
(She considered giving up.)

517
00:26:52,357 --> 00:26:54,892
(But even as Young In considered
giving up...)

518
00:26:54,893 --> 00:26:56,126
Keep your eyes locked ahead.

519
00:26:56,127 --> 00:26:56,961
(She practiced attacks.)

520
00:26:56,962 --> 00:26:58,763
Keep your focus forward, alright?

521
00:26:58,788 --> 00:27:00,128
I have another question.

522
00:27:00,152 --> 00:27:00,941
(She sought advice from veterans.)

523
00:27:00,966 --> 00:27:02,667
Whenever there's a high set,

524
00:27:02,668 --> 00:27:04,523
I get this urge just to tool it off.

525
00:27:05,704 --> 00:27:08,439
(She reviewed recorded matches.)

526
00:27:08,941 --> 00:27:12,677
Whenever I talked to Coach
after watching tape,

527
00:27:13,445 --> 00:27:16,848
it felt like anything I said
would sound like an excuse.

528
00:27:18,083 --> 00:27:20,884
When she asked,
"Why did you hit the ball like that?"

529
00:27:21,220 --> 00:27:22,820
I didn't know how to respond.

530
00:27:22,921 --> 00:27:24,789
That's what frustrated me the most.

531
00:27:24,790 --> 00:27:26,157
(Tears flowing helplessly)

532
00:27:26,158 --> 00:27:28,747
Still, running away from it
won't make me any better.

533
00:27:29,194 --> 00:27:30,928
I have to confront it if I want to grow.

534
00:27:30,929 --> 00:27:32,463
It's as simple as that.

535
00:27:33,031 --> 00:27:35,867
I feel like Coach showed me
the way forward.

536
00:27:37,269 --> 00:27:39,337
(Training after discussing the recording)

537
00:27:40,105 --> 00:27:42,073
(Young In preparing herself)

538
00:27:42,841 --> 00:27:44,508
(Walking over)

539
00:27:46,112 --> 00:27:47,233
Whose is this?

540
00:27:50,573 --> 00:27:51,771
So you've been taking notes.

541
00:27:51,803 --> 00:27:52,882
(As if talking to herself)

542
00:27:56,822 --> 00:27:59,324
(Feeling determined)

543
00:28:00,325 --> 00:28:04,662
Coach Kim, this might sound
like a really stupid question.

544
00:28:04,663 --> 00:28:05,863
Stupid?

545
00:28:06,498 --> 00:28:08,265
When I'm hitting
a fast tempo ball cross-court,

546
00:28:08,266 --> 00:28:10,834
I usually swing this way...

547
00:28:10,835 --> 00:28:13,070
to get around the block.

548
00:28:13,071 --> 00:28:14,438
- When the set comes in,
- Yes.

549
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:17,408
how do I drive it deep?

550
00:28:18,011 --> 00:28:18,942
Just swing deep.

551
00:28:19,077 --> 00:28:21,412
No, what I mean is...

552
00:28:22,014 --> 00:28:23,602
Just angle your cross-court shots deep.

553
00:28:23,982 --> 00:28:27,184
Right now, I'm cutting it
at a sharp angle like this,

554
00:28:27,185 --> 00:28:28,552
trying to split the blockers.

555
00:28:28,553 --> 00:28:30,888
You don't need to force that.
Just open up your body like this.

556
00:28:31,523 --> 00:28:32,666
(The body angle matters.)

557
00:28:32,691 --> 00:28:34,325
Or you can contact the ball
from right here.

558
00:28:34,326 --> 00:28:35,193
(Nodding)

559
00:28:35,194 --> 00:28:36,026
Or you can drop it short.

560
00:28:36,027 --> 00:28:39,430
I've been wanting to ask,
but I was worried it'd sound dumb.

561
00:28:39,831 --> 00:28:41,899
No, that's not a dumb question at all.

562
00:28:43,068 --> 00:28:44,735
(Smiling)

563
00:28:45,837 --> 00:28:47,471
(Next day)

564
00:28:48,840 --> 00:28:52,843
(Wonder Dogs hard at training,
practicing back-row attacks)

565
00:28:56,048 --> 00:28:57,248
Right away!

566
00:28:57,249 --> 00:28:59,117
(Young In's turn)

567
00:29:00,885 --> 00:29:02,220
- Young In,
- My fault.

568
00:29:02,488 --> 00:29:03,855
Young In,

569
00:29:04,923 --> 00:29:06,991
- keep it out of the net.
- Yes, Coach.

570
00:29:07,714 --> 00:29:08,969
What did I just tell you?

571
00:29:08,994 --> 00:29:11,528
Drive it deep like this.

572
00:29:12,798 --> 00:29:13,719
Toss it to me.

573
00:29:14,266 --> 00:29:15,099
Go deep.

574
00:29:15,601 --> 00:29:17,001
Go deep, go deep!

575
00:29:17,703 --> 00:29:18,770
There you go!

576
00:29:18,771 --> 00:29:21,071
(Wonder Coach's
special back-row attack training)

577
00:29:21,440 --> 00:29:23,708
Young In, that was a great swing.

578
00:29:23,709 --> 00:29:24,697
Nice job right there.

579
00:29:28,547 --> 00:29:30,080
Stop being so tense.

580
00:29:30,081 --> 00:29:31,725
This is Season Two. You're a veteran now.

581
00:29:31,749 --> 00:29:32,773
No need to be so anxious.

582
00:29:32,798 --> 00:29:34,573
Why are you so nervous?

583
00:29:34,779 --> 00:29:37,447
You're way too wound up.

584
00:29:37,856 --> 00:29:40,012
What's with the gold necklace?

585
00:29:40,092 --> 00:29:42,894
I've always worn this,
so I'm glad you finally noticed.

586
00:29:42,895 --> 00:29:45,284
If you want to buy yourself another one,
you'd better play well.

587
00:29:46,098 --> 00:29:48,966
(Wonder Coach's special care mode on)

588
00:29:49,269 --> 00:29:52,704
Personally, I think
Young In has real upside.

589
00:29:52,705 --> 00:29:57,941
If I didn't see any potential
or upside in her,

590
00:29:57,942 --> 00:30:00,445
I wouldn't have picked her for the roster.

591
00:30:00,879 --> 00:30:05,883
There's a reason
she made the cut at tryouts.

592
00:30:06,151 --> 00:30:08,519
It's Young In's job to put in the work...

593
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:11,889
and our job to help her unlock it.

594
00:30:12,925 --> 00:30:14,458
To get Young In back on track,

595
00:30:14,859 --> 00:30:17,661
we're going to put
our stellar coaching staff to work.

596
00:30:20,198 --> 00:30:22,988
Young In, focus on your arm swing.

597
00:30:24,737 --> 00:30:27,471
Don't let your torso over-rotate.

598
00:30:27,496 --> 00:30:28,706
(Mini net just for Young In)

599
00:30:28,914 --> 00:30:31,308
(Special training
with coaches Bong Woo and Tae Young)

600
00:30:32,377 --> 00:30:33,744
- Okay.
- Now, let's focus on...

601
00:30:35,247 --> 00:30:35,980
keeping it error-free.

602
00:30:35,981 --> 00:30:36,881
(Special tutoring from two coaches)

603
00:30:37,315 --> 00:30:38,115
Okay.

604
00:30:38,717 --> 00:30:39,517
Alright.

605
00:30:39,542 --> 00:30:41,375
(Practicing intentional attacks)

606
00:30:41,953 --> 00:30:42,786
That's it.

607
00:30:46,558 --> 00:30:47,903
Young In, your approach was too slow.

608
00:30:47,928 --> 00:30:50,315
Start your approach
the moment the ball is set.

609
00:30:50,340 --> 00:30:51,774
Instead, you took off right away.

610
00:30:52,030 --> 00:30:53,430
Just key in on my voice.

611
00:30:54,299 --> 00:30:55,099
Go.

612
00:30:55,600 --> 00:30:57,167
That was too late.

613
00:30:57,202 --> 00:30:58,169
Go!

614
00:30:58,170 --> 00:30:59,003
(Yelling)

615
00:30:59,004 --> 00:30:59,870
Tool the block!

616
00:31:00,104 --> 00:31:01,038
Go, go!

617
00:31:01,640 --> 00:31:02,306
(Yelling)

618
00:31:03,474 --> 00:31:05,008
- There you go.
- Nice one.

619
00:31:05,009 --> 00:31:08,212
You need to nail that timing down
without me having to yell "go."

620
00:31:09,515 --> 00:31:12,083
(Close tutoring even after the training)

621
00:31:12,551 --> 00:31:14,451
What's the difference
between pushing it and...

622
00:31:14,452 --> 00:31:15,953
They're completely different.

623
00:31:16,188 --> 00:31:17,054
(Sighing)

624
00:31:17,257 --> 00:31:18,343
What you're seeing there...

625
00:31:18,457 --> 00:31:19,957
Before I knew it,

626
00:31:19,958 --> 00:31:22,448
I ended up handling the tough critiques
and mental conditioning.

627
00:31:23,321 --> 00:31:26,689
The younger coaches are the ones
rebuilding the players' confidence.

628
00:31:27,433 --> 00:31:30,601
If Young In can put it all together,

629
00:31:30,602 --> 00:31:33,170
she'll be a huge weapon
for the Wonder Dogs.

630
00:31:33,740 --> 00:31:34,605
That's it.

631
00:31:35,140 --> 00:31:36,006
Nice!

632
00:31:36,007 --> 00:31:36,841
(Everyone helps out.)

633
00:31:36,842 --> 00:31:38,442
That was solid.

634
00:31:38,443 --> 00:31:39,376
Rip it.

635
00:31:39,377 --> 00:31:41,679
(Young In's attacks improve day by day.)

636
00:31:42,247 --> 00:31:43,314
There you go.

637
00:31:43,482 --> 00:31:45,649
Young In, that looked great.

638
00:31:47,014 --> 00:31:48,918
Nice.

639
00:31:49,287 --> 00:31:49,920
(Clap)

640
00:31:49,921 --> 00:31:51,188
That was a smart play.

641
00:31:51,189 --> 00:31:53,090
Keep the momentum going, okay?

642
00:31:53,659 --> 00:31:57,028
Right now, the Wonder Dogs are
riding a winning streak.

643
00:31:58,164 --> 00:32:00,665
Today, they're gunning
for their third straight victory.

644
00:32:00,666 --> 00:32:01,566
(Aiming for the third victory)

645
00:32:01,567 --> 00:32:04,001
Joining me for today's matchup
against Pohang Sports Council is Hyo Jin.

646
00:32:04,002 --> 00:32:05,903
- Hello.
- Good afternoon.

647
00:32:06,955 --> 00:32:09,625
(Team manager Boo is on duty.)

648
00:32:10,008 --> 00:32:11,108
Hello!

649
00:32:12,077 --> 00:32:13,110
Great to see you.

650
00:32:13,245 --> 00:32:16,647
Lee Da Hyeon and Kim Da In
have also joined us.

651
00:32:16,648 --> 00:32:19,250
Looks like they came out
to catch the match on their day off.

652
00:32:19,251 --> 00:32:19,972
Right.

653
00:32:20,285 --> 00:32:22,086
Today's opponent is Pohang Sports Council.

654
00:32:22,087 --> 00:32:23,342
What kind of team are they?

655
00:32:23,522 --> 00:32:25,589
At the 2024 Danyang Championship,

656
00:32:25,590 --> 00:32:27,625
they swept the tournament undefeated
to take first place.

657
00:32:27,626 --> 00:32:29,248
So they're a seasoned,
battle-tested squad.

658
00:32:29,538 --> 00:32:31,004
They've even pushed pro teams...

659
00:32:31,029 --> 00:32:34,098
to five sets and come away
with multiple wins.

660
00:32:34,700 --> 00:32:38,502
They also swept the MVP, Best Setter,
and Best Coach awards.

661
00:32:38,503 --> 00:32:39,436
That's right.

662
00:32:39,437 --> 00:32:41,306
Not only are they one of the top
corporate teams in the country,

663
00:32:41,307 --> 00:32:43,441
their roster features
several former pro players.

664
00:32:43,442 --> 00:32:46,577
Yes, a few of my former teammates
are playing for them right now.

665
00:32:47,305 --> 00:32:49,206
(Lee Hyun Ji, outside hitter)

666
00:32:52,851 --> 00:32:54,285
She hits hard.

667
00:32:54,553 --> 00:32:55,387
Hyun Ji packs a punch.

668
00:32:55,388 --> 00:32:56,220
(Hyun Ji the Strong)

669
00:32:56,221 --> 00:32:59,557
Park Gyeong Hyun also brings
extensive pro league experience.

670
00:32:59,558 --> 00:33:01,125
She's a powerhouse attacker.

671
00:33:01,126 --> 00:33:03,594
On top of that, she's got a lethal serve.

672
00:33:03,595 --> 00:33:04,695
(Specializes in serves and attacks)

673
00:33:04,796 --> 00:33:07,498
Lee Chae Min, formerly
of the Pink Spiders,

674
00:33:07,499 --> 00:33:09,132
is another heavy hitter.

675
00:33:10,211 --> 00:33:12,256
Park Hyeon Ju is also
a former Rookie of the Year.

676
00:33:12,257 --> 00:33:12,913
Exactly.

677
00:33:12,938 --> 00:33:14,438
(Park Hyeon Ju: former Pink Spiders,
2019-2020 Best Rookie)

678
00:33:14,439 --> 00:33:16,874
In their last outing
against the Pink Spiders,

679
00:33:16,875 --> 00:33:20,845
the Wonder Dogs faced off
against Seung Ju and Na Yeon.

680
00:33:20,980 --> 00:33:23,748
I hear there are former Wonder Dogs...

681
00:33:23,749 --> 00:33:25,249
on Pohang Sports Council as well.

682
00:33:25,250 --> 00:33:29,721
With Ho Bin and Seon Ah
suiting up for Pohang Sports Council,

683
00:33:29,722 --> 00:33:32,790
the Wonder Dogs are down two key players.

684
00:33:32,791 --> 00:33:36,227
Two players who know
the Wonder Dogs' system inside and out...

685
00:33:36,228 --> 00:33:37,816
are now standing across the net.

686
00:33:37,939 --> 00:33:40,519
When you coach at the pro level,

687
00:33:40,544 --> 00:33:42,442
players inevitably
get sidelined by injuries,

688
00:33:42,466 --> 00:33:44,069
traded away, or called elsewhere.

689
00:33:44,070 --> 00:33:47,338
That's just part of the game.

690
00:33:47,339 --> 00:33:50,641
Right, it happens all the time.

691
00:33:51,109 --> 00:33:55,712
How you weather those absences is crucial.

692
00:33:55,713 --> 00:33:57,882
Exactly. For Coach Kim,

693
00:33:57,883 --> 00:34:01,819
this is a true test
of her coaching acumen...

694
00:34:02,054 --> 00:34:03,287
and a major challenge.

695
00:34:06,892 --> 00:34:08,392
Ho Bin is looking sharp.

696
00:34:09,894 --> 00:34:10,760
No way!

697
00:34:10,761 --> 00:34:12,929
(Smiling)

698
00:34:12,930 --> 00:34:13,864
She's sitting over there.

699
00:34:13,865 --> 00:34:15,465
(Smiling widely)

700
00:34:15,967 --> 00:34:17,990
They look even happier
than when they were with us.

701
00:34:19,471 --> 00:34:20,403
That was fun.

702
00:34:21,072 --> 00:34:23,574
They both looked so upbeat.

703
00:34:23,675 --> 00:34:24,408
(Breathing in)

704
00:34:24,409 --> 00:34:26,176
I felt a little bittersweet.

705
00:34:26,544 --> 00:34:27,411
(Chuckling)

706
00:34:27,646 --> 00:34:29,280
We're on opposite sides now.

707
00:34:29,281 --> 00:34:31,648
So I'll have to give it my all...

708
00:34:31,649 --> 00:34:32,750
and beat Yu Kyung.

709
00:34:34,753 --> 00:34:37,489
On the flip side,
this is a great chance...

710
00:34:37,490 --> 00:34:39,857
- to see what Yu Kyung can do.
- Right.

711
00:34:40,358 --> 00:34:44,194
This is Yu Kyung's first match
anchoring the defense as the sole libero.

712
00:34:44,496 --> 00:34:47,989
I'm really curious to see
how she steps up.

713
00:34:48,014 --> 00:34:48,754
Sure.

714
00:34:49,200 --> 00:34:51,535
(Another nervous player)

715
00:34:56,174 --> 00:34:58,809
I keep glancing over at Hyeon Ju.

716
00:34:59,578 --> 00:35:02,145
Once again, we're in for a clash...

717
00:35:02,314 --> 00:35:04,448
- between two opposite hitters.
- That's right.

718
00:35:05,116 --> 00:35:08,785
(Two faced off during the tryout.)

719
00:35:09,220 --> 00:35:13,323
(A showdown between two opposite spikers)

720
00:35:14,121 --> 00:35:16,070
(They meet again.)

721
00:35:16,095 --> 00:35:20,006
Young In and Hyeon Ju
go head-to-head today.

722
00:35:20,031 --> 00:35:20,531
Yes.

723
00:35:20,531 --> 00:35:23,731
Today, the outcome of the match
may come down to...

724
00:35:23,731 --> 00:35:26,831
how well she fulfills her role.

725
00:35:26,831 --> 00:35:27,931
(The opposite showdown begins again.)

726
00:35:28,765 --> 00:35:30,498
Hands up.

727
00:35:31,498 --> 00:35:33,231
(Coach Kim Yun Hye)

728
00:35:33,231 --> 00:35:34,931
Don't look to the right.

729
00:35:35,331 --> 00:35:36,298
Take this one, Na Young.

730
00:35:36,298 --> 00:35:37,731
(Across the court)

731
00:35:39,898 --> 00:35:42,498
(Glasses off)

732
00:35:42,865 --> 00:35:45,465
Coach Kim Yun Hye just took off
her glasses.

733
00:35:46,165 --> 00:35:47,631
Try blocking this.

734
00:35:47,631 --> 00:35:49,631
(She spikes it herself.)

735
00:35:51,565 --> 00:35:52,765
(A surprise tip)

736
00:35:53,098 --> 00:35:53,965
(Shaking her head)

737
00:35:53,965 --> 00:35:55,331
Too slow.

738
00:35:55,798 --> 00:35:59,031
(Watching in awe)

739
00:35:59,231 --> 00:36:01,598
Don't set it too tight.

740
00:36:01,598 --> 00:36:03,965
(Bringing the intensity
even during warm-ups)

741
00:36:03,965 --> 00:36:05,765
Jump quicker.

742
00:36:06,031 --> 00:36:07,098
That's it.

743
00:36:07,098 --> 00:36:10,131
(Who is shouting alongside Coach Yun Hye?)

744
00:36:10,298 --> 00:36:12,731
Coach Yun Hui is there
as an assistant coach.

745
00:36:12,731 --> 00:36:13,665
She used to be a player.

746
00:36:13,665 --> 00:36:15,431
Until last year, she was a player-coach.

747
00:36:15,431 --> 00:36:17,823
But this year, she's stepped
into the coaching role full-time.

748
00:36:18,065 --> 00:36:21,331
Coach Yun Hye is a veteran
with 22 years of experience,

749
00:36:21,331 --> 00:36:23,962
but the coach assisting her is
also a legend in her own right.

750
00:36:23,966 --> 00:36:24,740
Absolutely.

751
00:36:25,471 --> 00:36:27,171
Today's matchup is between...

752
00:36:27,171 --> 00:36:29,437
Kim Yeon Koung, a second-year coach,

753
00:36:29,437 --> 00:36:32,371
and Kim Yun Hye,
a coach with 22 years of experience.

754
00:36:32,371 --> 00:36:34,371
- That's a 20-year gap in experience.
- True.

755
00:36:34,371 --> 00:36:37,871
Both Coach Kims have a similar style.

756
00:36:37,871 --> 00:36:41,704
So whose voice will carry louder
across the court today?

757
00:36:41,704 --> 00:36:43,104
I'm really curious.

758
00:36:44,005 --> 00:36:46,037
Let's check
the Wonder Dogs' starting lineup.

759
00:36:46,037 --> 00:36:48,137
Starting from Zone One,
middle blocker Kim Bo Been.

760
00:36:48,637 --> 00:36:50,004
Setter Kim Da Sol.

761
00:36:50,004 --> 00:36:51,737
Outside hitter Enkhsoyol.

762
00:36:52,171 --> 00:36:53,671
Middle blocker Lee Ye Dam.

763
00:36:54,171 --> 00:36:55,771
Opposite spiker Yoon Young In.

764
00:36:56,271 --> 00:36:57,971
Outside hitter Back Chae Rim.

765
00:36:57,971 --> 00:36:59,437
And libero Seo Yu Kyung.

766
00:37:01,904 --> 00:37:04,004
Let's check
Pohang Sports Council's starting lineup.

767
00:37:04,004 --> 00:37:06,037
Starting from Zone One,
setter Choi Yeong Hye.

768
00:37:06,037 --> 00:37:07,471
Outside hitter Park Gyeong Hyeon.

769
00:37:08,004 --> 00:37:09,471
Middle blocker Oh Na Young.

770
00:37:09,904 --> 00:37:11,604
Opposite spiker Park Hyeon Ju.

771
00:37:12,204 --> 00:37:14,071
Outside hitter Lee Hyun Ji.

772
00:37:14,671 --> 00:37:16,071
Middle blocker Lee Ho Bin.

773
00:37:16,071 --> 00:37:17,471
And libero Chae Seon Ah.

774
00:37:22,037 --> 00:37:25,237
Keep the rally alive with your defense.

775
00:37:25,237 --> 00:37:26,871
(Starting setter, Kim Da Sol)

776
00:37:26,871 --> 00:37:31,304
I wanted to make use
of every player in this match.

777
00:37:31,604 --> 00:37:35,637
And since Da Sol excels
at that kind of play,

778
00:37:36,104 --> 00:37:39,171
I decided to put her
in the starting lineup.

779
00:37:40,471 --> 00:37:43,671
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 0
: Wonder Dogs 0)

780
00:37:43,837 --> 00:37:45,971
With the Wonder Dogs' Kim Bo Been serving,

781
00:37:45,971 --> 00:37:47,804
the third match is underway.

782
00:37:50,104 --> 00:37:50,871
Are you ready?

783
00:37:52,837 --> 00:37:53,637
Yes.

784
00:37:54,804 --> 00:37:55,604
Can you drop it short?

785
00:37:56,271 --> 00:37:57,871
(Short serve to Zone 1)

786
00:38:00,904 --> 00:38:01,837
(Flicking)

787
00:38:02,171 --> 00:38:04,037
(Got it.)

788
00:38:04,237 --> 00:38:06,037
She says she can pull it off.

789
00:38:06,037 --> 00:38:07,504
- It's her first serve.
- Bo Been can do it.

790
00:38:07,504 --> 00:38:08,804
If it's Bo Been, she can make it happen.

791
00:38:08,804 --> 00:38:09,604
She gives the nod.

792
00:38:10,437 --> 00:38:11,237
Let's see.

793
00:38:11,637 --> 00:38:12,571
Serve.

794
00:38:14,037 --> 00:38:15,137
Set One is underway.

795
00:38:20,037 --> 00:38:21,837
Hyeon Ju. The set is tight to the net.

796
00:38:21,837 --> 00:38:22,971
That's it.

797
00:38:24,171 --> 00:38:25,004
Up the middle.

798
00:38:25,337 --> 00:38:26,237
Blocked!

799
00:38:28,404 --> 00:38:29,337
It goes to Hyeon Ju.

800
00:38:29,337 --> 00:38:30,237
Spike.

801
00:38:30,737 --> 00:38:32,104
What a dig!

802
00:38:32,904 --> 00:38:34,004
To the left.

803
00:38:34,004 --> 00:38:34,771
A tip.

804
00:38:35,804 --> 00:38:37,537
Enkhsoyol.

805
00:38:39,871 --> 00:38:42,737
(The Wonder Dogs take the first point
of the set.)

806
00:38:42,904 --> 00:38:43,737
Na Young.

807
00:38:44,437 --> 00:38:46,437
Don't pull your hands back. Keep them up.

808
00:38:46,437 --> 00:38:47,237
Okay.

809
00:38:47,904 --> 00:38:49,937
The Wonder Dogs scored first
in two straight matches.

810
00:38:49,937 --> 00:38:53,071
They've taken the opening point
in both of their previous games.

811
00:38:53,071 --> 00:38:56,304
We'll have to see
if they can keep that streak alive.

812
00:38:56,304 --> 00:38:57,471
Let's watch.

813
00:38:58,004 --> 00:38:59,704
And Bo Been's serve is sharp.

814
00:38:59,704 --> 00:39:01,404
Right, it's really solid.

815
00:39:01,671 --> 00:39:02,571
Nice serve.

816
00:39:04,404 --> 00:39:07,237
I figured targeting their serve receive
would be the key.

817
00:39:08,104 --> 00:39:10,004
And when we serve,

818
00:39:10,004 --> 00:39:12,871
we're planning to mix in short serves.

819
00:39:12,871 --> 00:39:15,671
Short serves seriously disrupt
their passing efficiency.

820
00:39:16,104 --> 00:39:18,537
Our second option is
to target Seon Ah's right side.

821
00:39:18,537 --> 00:39:19,871
The right side is a good target too.

822
00:39:19,871 --> 00:39:21,904
You know that's her weak spot.

823
00:39:22,604 --> 00:39:25,871
We know their strengths and weaknesses,

824
00:39:25,871 --> 00:39:27,337
and we've game-planned accordingly.

825
00:39:29,537 --> 00:39:32,571
(This time, Zone 1.)

826
00:39:33,371 --> 00:39:38,904
(Target Seon Ah's right side)

827
00:39:39,337 --> 00:39:40,171
Bo Been again.

828
00:39:44,337 --> 00:39:45,571
Seon Ah's pass is shaky.

829
00:39:45,571 --> 00:39:46,337
That's right.

830
00:39:49,937 --> 00:39:51,337
Gyeong Hyeon. Up and swing.

831
00:39:51,737 --> 00:39:54,671
(A clean free ball)

832
00:39:54,671 --> 00:39:56,437
Once again. Enkhsoyol.

833
00:39:56,437 --> 00:39:57,486
Point!

834
00:39:57,486 --> 00:39:58,871
(A powerful line shot scores)

835
00:39:58,871 --> 00:40:00,204
Let's go.

836
00:40:00,204 --> 00:40:02,537
(The game plan works again.)

837
00:40:02,771 --> 00:40:04,637
I should've caught that.

838
00:40:05,437 --> 00:40:06,504
You're late.

839
00:40:07,071 --> 00:40:08,304
You're too late.

840
00:40:08,304 --> 00:40:10,637
If you don't put it away,
don't cover her on defense.

841
00:40:10,637 --> 00:40:11,704
Just transition early.

842
00:40:11,704 --> 00:40:13,237
- You're late.
- Got it.

843
00:40:16,904 --> 00:40:18,902
You can usually tell,

844
00:40:18,902 --> 00:40:20,304
after one or two points.

845
00:40:21,171 --> 00:40:23,404
I could feel they were targeting me.

846
00:40:24,704 --> 00:40:25,837
They're relentless.

847
00:40:26,904 --> 00:40:29,071
Help me out with the coverage.

848
00:40:29,271 --> 00:40:30,637
- Okay.
- Got it.

849
00:40:30,847 --> 00:40:31,987
I'll give you a signal.

850
00:40:32,012 --> 00:40:34,379
(Briefly rattled,
but quick to give direction)

851
00:40:34,404 --> 00:40:35,704
- Let's go.
- Come on.

852
00:40:40,271 --> 00:40:41,137
Bo Been.

853
00:40:41,137 --> 00:40:43,437
(Another short serve to Zone 1)

854
00:40:43,437 --> 00:40:45,071
Bo Been steps up to serve again.

855
00:40:46,511 --> 00:40:47,584
In 2, 1.

856
00:40:49,104 --> 00:40:50,746
Take it. Right in front of Hyeon Ju.

857
00:40:50,771 --> 00:40:52,237
(Rushing)

858
00:40:53,604 --> 00:40:54,471
Serve receive.

859
00:40:54,471 --> 00:40:55,404
(This time, they handle it.)

860
00:40:56,537 --> 00:40:57,371
Pin.

861
00:40:58,604 --> 00:41:00,037
(Startled)

862
00:41:01,271 --> 00:41:05,437
Gyeong Hyeon played professionally
until last season,

863
00:41:05,437 --> 00:41:07,237
- so we need to keep a close eye on her.
- Definitely.

864
00:41:07,971 --> 00:41:11,404
- Great dig, Hyeon Ju.
- Nice job.

865
00:41:12,204 --> 00:41:13,271
Cover the line.

866
00:41:13,671 --> 00:41:16,209
(Still barking out instructions
even after scoring)

867
00:41:16,571 --> 00:41:17,737
(Strong early serves from Bo Been)

868
00:41:17,737 --> 00:41:18,971
- Great serve.
- Nice serve.

869
00:41:19,897 --> 00:41:22,064
Great serve.

870
00:41:23,537 --> 00:41:24,504
Enkhsoyol.

871
00:41:24,504 --> 00:41:25,804
Push it or tip it to Zone Three.

872
00:41:25,804 --> 00:41:26,704
No soft swings.

873
00:41:26,937 --> 00:41:27,737
Got it.

874
00:41:29,871 --> 00:41:31,404
Gyeong Hyeon is a tough server too.

875
00:41:34,737 --> 00:41:36,104
Chae Rim passes it.

876
00:41:36,737 --> 00:41:38,297
Push it or tip it to Zone Three.

877
00:41:39,171 --> 00:41:40,671
A tip.

878
00:41:40,671 --> 00:41:41,504
To Zone Three.

879
00:41:41,504 --> 00:41:42,537
(Executed right away)

880
00:41:42,904 --> 00:41:43,971
Well done.

881
00:41:44,304 --> 00:41:48,404
(Boiling with frustration)

882
00:41:48,737 --> 00:41:49,871
A tip to Zone Three

883
00:41:50,671 --> 00:41:52,671
They're settling into a rhythm now.

884
00:41:52,671 --> 00:41:54,404
She's been mixing in...

885
00:41:54,404 --> 00:41:57,837
both attacks and tips to Zone Three.

886
00:41:58,204 --> 00:42:01,437
Enkhsoyol is showing some real composure
out there.

887
00:42:01,437 --> 00:42:02,337
(She's become a scoring machine.)

888
00:42:06,471 --> 00:42:07,971
Yeong Hye, set it to the left.

889
00:42:08,024 --> 00:42:08,998
Okay.

890
00:42:09,137 --> 00:42:10,337
Hyun Ji, you have to swing.

891
00:42:11,837 --> 00:42:14,737
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 2
: Wonder Dogs 4)

892
00:42:15,237 --> 00:42:17,004
(Play continues.)

893
00:42:17,004 --> 00:42:17,804
Set the C!

894
00:42:18,638 --> 00:42:20,072
(Hyun Ji charges in.)

895
00:42:20,072 --> 00:42:20,972
Hit it quick.

896
00:42:21,704 --> 00:42:23,304
A tip. Dug up.

897
00:42:23,304 --> 00:42:24,571
No, I told you to swing.

898
00:42:24,871 --> 00:42:26,004
Back-row attack.

899
00:42:26,371 --> 00:42:27,371
Da Sol.

900
00:42:27,371 --> 00:42:28,271
Down the middle.

901
00:42:29,171 --> 00:42:30,071
Defense.

902
00:42:30,837 --> 00:42:31,771
Hyeon Ju.

903
00:42:31,771 --> 00:42:32,904
The spike is blocked.

904
00:42:33,871 --> 00:42:36,004
- To the left.
- Go deep!

905
00:42:36,004 --> 00:42:37,071
Hey.

906
00:42:38,304 --> 00:42:39,104
She turns and swings.

907
00:42:39,104 --> 00:42:41,037
Enkhsoyol dives for the dig.

908
00:42:42,371 --> 00:42:44,137
A heavy swing from the left.

909
00:42:44,137 --> 00:42:44,971
Chae Rim.

910
00:42:46,271 --> 00:42:48,037
- Nice set.
- Nice set.

911
00:42:48,380 --> 00:42:49,967
(Wowing)

912
00:42:50,004 --> 00:42:51,637
Oh, no.

913
00:42:52,637 --> 00:42:54,037
No, Hyun Ji.

914
00:42:54,037 --> 00:42:55,737
Why are you tipping it?

915
00:42:55,737 --> 00:42:56,871
I told you to swing.

916
00:42:57,704 --> 00:42:59,271
Put it down right inside the court.

917
00:43:00,071 --> 00:43:01,137
She's giving feedback right away.

918
00:43:01,137 --> 00:43:02,271
(The tone is getting sharper.)

919
00:43:02,271 --> 00:43:03,502
She doesn't let anything slide.

920
00:43:04,471 --> 00:43:06,637
Do it again. Get ready for the next rally.

921
00:43:07,071 --> 00:43:08,137
Hyeon Ju.

922
00:43:09,804 --> 00:43:11,604
You're standing too far in.

923
00:43:11,604 --> 00:43:14,404
(Yun Hui steps in to help coach.)

924
00:43:14,404 --> 00:43:15,237
Serve.

925
00:43:15,237 --> 00:43:17,104
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 2
: Wonder Dogs 6)

926
00:43:18,904 --> 00:43:20,237
The pass is shaky.

927
00:43:20,237 --> 00:43:21,104
Take it.

928
00:43:21,837 --> 00:43:24,404
It deflects off the block.

929
00:43:24,404 --> 00:43:25,271
Where did it go?

930
00:43:25,571 --> 00:43:27,971
- That's it.
- Okay.

931
00:43:28,904 --> 00:43:31,071
(Hyeon Ju snaps the Wonder Dogs' run.)

932
00:43:31,071 --> 00:43:32,471
- Nice job.
- Well done.

933
00:43:32,971 --> 00:43:35,471
Once Hyeon Ju heats up,

934
00:43:35,471 --> 00:43:37,404
- the Wonder Dogs are in trouble.
- That's right.

935
00:43:39,837 --> 00:43:41,804
Da Sol,
they're already cheating over early.

936
00:43:41,837 --> 00:43:42,604
They're going to the left.

937
00:43:42,604 --> 00:43:43,871
We have Young In over here.

938
00:43:44,804 --> 00:43:50,037
(Countering by going to the right side)

939
00:43:50,037 --> 00:43:52,071
Hyeon Ju serves after the point.

940
00:43:52,804 --> 00:43:53,604
Enkhsoyol.

941
00:43:53,937 --> 00:43:55,004
Set a C, right away.

942
00:43:55,004 --> 00:43:55,904
To the right side.

943
00:43:56,271 --> 00:43:57,604
Da Sol drops back for a back set.

944
00:43:58,237 --> 00:43:59,104
Young In.

945
00:43:59,104 --> 00:44:00,371
(Stuffed by the block)

946
00:44:02,937 --> 00:44:03,737
Yeong Hye.

947
00:44:05,404 --> 00:44:06,804
Back-row tip.

948
00:44:06,804 --> 00:44:07,971
(A sneaky back-row tip)

949
00:44:08,371 --> 00:44:12,137
(Hyeon Ju scores back-to-back points.)

950
00:44:12,137 --> 00:44:16,304
She read the block cleanly
and dropped a tip to catch them off guard.

951
00:44:16,304 --> 00:44:20,442
It's tough to defend a back-row attack
when the timing gets thrown off like that.

952
00:44:20,442 --> 00:44:21,737
She placed it nicely.

953
00:44:22,571 --> 00:44:24,004
(Headache)

954
00:44:24,937 --> 00:44:26,304
Long.

955
00:44:26,304 --> 00:44:27,437
(I can't let her show me up.)

956
00:44:27,771 --> 00:44:29,371
It's 6 to 4, a two-point game.

957
00:44:31,471 --> 00:44:32,671
Do it now.

958
00:44:32,671 --> 00:44:33,504
Back set.

959
00:44:33,737 --> 00:44:34,671
Too low.

960
00:44:37,237 --> 00:44:38,504
Hyeon Ju out of the back row.

961
00:44:39,804 --> 00:44:41,437
Cross-court shot. Da Sol digs it.

962
00:44:41,437 --> 00:44:42,537
Yu Kyung puts it up again.

963
00:44:42,537 --> 00:44:44,037
Young In charges in.

964
00:44:45,004 --> 00:44:46,537
Covered. They send it over.

965
00:44:46,904 --> 00:44:48,671
Point.

966
00:44:48,671 --> 00:44:50,971
(Not to be outdone,
Young In answers back.)

967
00:44:51,504 --> 00:44:58,404
(Yoon Young In vs. Park Hyeon Ju)

968
00:44:58,804 --> 00:45:02,337
(The tug-of-war is fierce
right from the start.)

969
00:45:02,866 --> 00:45:04,066
The score is 7 to 4, a three-point lead.

970
00:45:04,067 --> 00:45:04,800
(Ye Dam serves.)

971
00:45:04,801 --> 00:45:05,634
Ye Dam.

972
00:45:07,070 --> 00:45:08,704
(Another mysterious signal)

973
00:45:08,705 --> 00:45:10,205
Send it over!

974
00:45:11,808 --> 00:45:12,841
(Everyone goes on alert.)

975
00:45:12,842 --> 00:45:14,109
I'll get the ball through the seam.

976
00:45:15,078 --> 00:45:15,878
Serve.

977
00:45:16,179 --> 00:45:17,079
Ye Dam serves.

978
00:45:19,749 --> 00:45:20,749
That's it. Great serve.

979
00:45:21,585 --> 00:45:22,952
Their pass is shaky!

980
00:45:23,053 --> 00:45:24,253
That's it. Go.

981
00:45:26,456 --> 00:45:28,657
And Ye Dam's service ace!

982
00:45:31,895 --> 00:45:33,729
(Ye Dam, nice!)

983
00:45:33,730 --> 00:45:34,597
Nice serve.

984
00:45:35,198 --> 00:45:36,398
I've never seen her get a service ace
before.

985
00:45:37,835 --> 00:45:41,137
Coach Yeon Koung's serving strategy
keeps paying off.

986
00:45:41,138 --> 00:45:43,005
What really matters is...

987
00:45:43,006 --> 00:45:45,175
that where the serve is received
affects...

988
00:45:45,176 --> 00:45:48,478
how often each player gets set on offense.

989
00:45:48,479 --> 00:45:51,214
So we're going to target number four
with our serves.

990
00:45:51,215 --> 00:45:52,882
She gets a lot of sets.

991
00:45:52,883 --> 00:45:53,751
(Hyun Ji gets a heavy share
of the team's attacks.)

992
00:45:53,752 --> 00:45:56,052
So we need to make things
as tough as possible for Hyun Ji.

993
00:45:56,077 --> 00:45:58,144
That'll make it easier for you
to read and react.

994
00:45:59,122 --> 00:46:02,825
The Wonder Dogs keep targeting
number four with their serves.

995
00:46:02,826 --> 00:46:04,526
And the game plan is working.

996
00:46:09,499 --> 00:46:11,032
(Strategy successful!)

997
00:46:11,033 --> 00:46:11,901
Great.

998
00:46:11,902 --> 00:46:13,368
My bad.

999
00:46:13,369 --> 00:46:14,837
- It's fine.
- Sorry.

1000
00:46:14,838 --> 00:46:15,838
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 5
: Wonder Dogs 9)

1001
00:46:20,010 --> 00:46:21,043
Da Sol.

1002
00:46:22,279 --> 00:46:24,380
See? That's how we get them moving.

1003
00:46:24,381 --> 00:46:25,413
Okay.

1004
00:46:25,414 --> 00:46:26,949
Let's keep them moving like that!

1005
00:46:26,950 --> 00:46:27,883
(She calls for a decoy play.)

1006
00:46:31,421 --> 00:46:32,321
(Power server Hyun Ji steps up to serve.)

1007
00:46:32,322 --> 00:46:33,289
Hyun Ji serves.

1008
00:46:34,424 --> 00:46:36,425
They handle the heavy serve cleanly.

1009
00:46:36,660 --> 00:46:37,593
Okay.

1010
00:46:37,594 --> 00:46:38,494
Enkhsoyol.

1011
00:46:38,663 --> 00:46:39,828
The pass goes to Da Sol.

1012
00:46:39,829 --> 00:46:40,996
Hey, back B!

1013
00:46:40,997 --> 00:46:42,230
Back B! They're shifting.

1014
00:46:44,300 --> 00:46:46,635
(See? That's how we get them moving.)

1015
00:46:47,537 --> 00:46:49,571
(The decoy works just as planned.)

1016
00:46:49,572 --> 00:46:50,873
(Flinching)

1017
00:46:51,041 --> 00:46:51,976
(A single-block look!)

1018
00:46:51,977 --> 00:46:53,009
That's it.

1019
00:46:53,010 --> 00:46:55,711
The set goes left, followed by a spike.

1020
00:46:55,712 --> 00:46:56,679
- And she puts it away.
- Nice.

1021
00:46:58,648 --> 00:46:59,682
Nice.

1022
00:46:59,916 --> 00:47:00,949
Great job, everyone.

1023
00:47:01,584 --> 00:47:03,118
Hey!

1024
00:47:03,453 --> 00:47:05,020
The swing came through so fast...

1025
00:47:05,021 --> 00:47:06,889
that Seon Ah couldn't get out of the way.

1026
00:47:06,890 --> 00:47:07,890
That's right.

1027
00:47:08,525 --> 00:47:09,926
(Young In is up to serve next.)

1028
00:47:09,927 --> 00:47:10,860
Young In.

1029
00:47:11,227 --> 00:47:12,093
Let's go with this.

1030
00:47:12,094 --> 00:47:13,728
(Another tactical call right away)

1031
00:47:13,729 --> 00:47:15,297
(Nodding)

1032
00:47:15,899 --> 00:47:19,034
(Hyun Ji is the target again.)

1033
00:47:19,436 --> 00:47:21,837
Watch for a low serve.
You know Young In serves low.

1034
00:47:23,908 --> 00:47:25,441
The score is now 10 to 5.

1035
00:47:28,612 --> 00:47:29,840
Their pass is shaky.

1036
00:47:30,580 --> 00:47:31,413
That's it.

1037
00:47:33,183 --> 00:47:34,450
And that's a point.

1038
00:47:34,751 --> 00:47:35,684
Young In!

1039
00:47:35,685 --> 00:47:36,685
(Young In scores a service ace.)

1040
00:47:36,686 --> 00:47:37,586
Nice job.

1041
00:47:40,590 --> 00:47:43,025
(They stretch their lead
and build momentum!)

1042
00:47:43,026 --> 00:47:44,259
- Unbelievable.
- Well done.

1043
00:47:44,394 --> 00:47:44,927
Yes!

1044
00:47:45,629 --> 00:47:49,031
Great serve! Nice serve!

1045
00:47:49,599 --> 00:47:51,767
The Wonder Dogs are playing...

1046
00:47:51,768 --> 00:47:53,468
much sharper than they did
in their first two matches.

1047
00:47:53,469 --> 00:47:55,971
They look like a completely
different squad right now.

1048
00:47:55,972 --> 00:47:56,939
Hey.

1049
00:47:56,940 --> 00:47:58,707
Chae Rim passes, and Da Sol sets.

1050
00:47:59,275 --> 00:48:00,775
A push shot from the middle
of the back row.

1051
00:48:00,776 --> 00:48:02,210
(A tip from number three)

1052
00:48:02,679 --> 00:48:03,946
The score is now 12 to 6.

1053
00:48:04,248 --> 00:48:06,415
Hey, you have to go for the ball,
even if you collide.

1054
00:48:06,416 --> 00:48:08,217
(Sharp glance)

1055
00:48:10,387 --> 00:48:12,822
The ball drops in.

1056
00:48:12,823 --> 00:48:13,923
A service ace for Chae Rim!

1057
00:48:13,924 --> 00:48:14,858
Keep it rolling.

1058
00:48:14,859 --> 00:48:16,993
They keep targeting the same receiver
with their serves,

1059
00:48:16,994 --> 00:48:19,462
and it's working like a charm.

1060
00:48:19,795 --> 00:48:21,629
They need to set up a play here.

1061
00:48:21,630 --> 00:48:22,464
Slide attack.

1062
00:48:22,899 --> 00:48:24,533
A push shot.

1063
00:48:25,101 --> 00:48:26,068
Bo Been scores.

1064
00:48:26,469 --> 00:48:28,170
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 6
: Wonder Dogs 15)

1065
00:48:28,171 --> 00:48:29,703
When we faced the Wonder Dogs earlier,

1066
00:48:29,704 --> 00:48:32,240
they felt like a really tough team.

1067
00:48:33,044 --> 00:48:34,477
Hey, swing!

1068
00:48:35,512 --> 00:48:37,179
And a push shot!

1069
00:48:37,180 --> 00:48:39,882
They score! It's 17 to 7.

1070
00:48:39,883 --> 00:48:41,951
The lead has grown to ten points!

1071
00:48:42,052 --> 00:48:43,319
Zero!

1072
00:48:43,320 --> 00:48:46,255
And they put it away.

1073
00:48:46,256 --> 00:48:48,658
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 7
: Wonder Dogs 18)

1074
00:48:48,659 --> 00:48:51,260
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 7
: Wonder Dogs 19)

1075
00:48:51,261 --> 00:48:52,194
That's it.

1076
00:48:52,195 --> 00:48:53,295
(A 12-point lead!)

1077
00:48:53,963 --> 00:48:57,566
The players are executing
so well right now...

1078
00:48:57,567 --> 00:48:59,635
that Coach Yeon Koung barely
has anything to say.

1079
00:48:59,636 --> 00:49:01,923
It's 19 to 7, a 12-point lead.

1080
00:49:02,306 --> 00:49:04,374
The Wonder Dogs are on fire!

1081
00:49:04,375 --> 00:49:05,407
That's right.

1082
00:49:06,209 --> 00:49:07,943
I can't believe we're seeing
a score like this.

1083
00:49:07,944 --> 00:49:09,644
Look deep into the court and swing away.

1084
00:49:09,645 --> 00:49:12,781
I think we're seeing the payoff
from their video session.

1085
00:49:13,316 --> 00:49:16,418
You can see the Pohang players
getting rattled every time they swing.

1086
00:49:18,054 --> 00:49:18,854
(The perfect serving strategy)

1087
00:49:18,855 --> 00:49:19,888
Their serves are dialed in.

1088
00:49:20,957 --> 00:49:22,257
Zero!

1089
00:49:23,160 --> 00:49:24,560
Their blocks are dialed in too.

1090
00:49:24,861 --> 00:49:27,864
The Wonder Dogs have built a 12-point lead
with a game plan tailored to Pohang.

1091
00:49:27,865 --> 00:49:28,764
That's right.

1092
00:49:28,765 --> 00:49:30,666
I think they've done a great job...

1093
00:49:30,667 --> 00:49:33,969
executing every strategy...

1094
00:49:33,970 --> 00:49:36,438
and the play we went over in our meeting.

1095
00:49:37,674 --> 00:49:40,476
(The lead has grown to 12 points.)

1096
00:49:42,713 --> 00:49:44,013
What are you doing?

1097
00:49:49,486 --> 00:49:52,522
You need to step up and play responsibly,
Gyeong Hyeon!

1098
00:49:52,523 --> 00:49:53,387
Yes!

1099
00:49:56,359 --> 00:49:58,427
Go for another one!

1100
00:50:03,233 --> 00:50:06,068
(She snaps her head up.)

1101
00:50:07,204 --> 00:50:08,837
Hey, Hyeon Ju!

1102
00:50:09,205 --> 00:50:10,071
Hyeon Ju!

1103
00:50:11,508 --> 00:50:13,575
It's fine if you make an error.
Just swing away!

1104
00:50:13,943 --> 00:50:14,776
Okay.

1105
00:50:15,612 --> 00:50:18,247
Don't wait.
Don't wait for someone else to take it.

1106
00:50:18,915 --> 00:50:19,882
The score is 19 to 7.

1107
00:50:19,883 --> 00:50:20,782
(Min Kyeong serves.)

1108
00:50:22,252 --> 00:50:23,419
Jump!

1109
00:50:23,820 --> 00:50:24,953
(A fake jump)

1110
00:50:24,954 --> 00:50:26,121
(An open spot)

1111
00:50:26,356 --> 00:50:27,456
A push shot!

1112
00:50:27,590 --> 00:50:28,390
A tip!

1113
00:50:28,892 --> 00:50:30,759
Hyeon Ju drops it
into the open spot for a point.

1114
00:50:30,760 --> 00:50:32,695
(Hyeon Ju scores with a well-placed tip!)

1115
00:50:33,797 --> 00:50:34,764
My bad.

1116
00:50:36,065 --> 00:50:38,166
Hyeon Ju did a great job...

1117
00:50:38,167 --> 00:50:40,201
finding the open space in the defense.

1118
00:50:40,637 --> 00:50:42,871
Nice touch on that tip, Hyeon Ju!

1119
00:50:45,358 --> 00:50:47,076
(She gets low again.)

1120
00:50:48,311 --> 00:50:49,444
(Glaring)

1121
00:50:49,612 --> 00:50:50,545
Nice.

1122
00:50:51,281 --> 00:50:52,514
Let's get one here, everyone!

1123
00:50:53,082 --> 00:50:54,082
Nice.

1124
00:50:54,083 --> 00:50:54,849
Hyun Ji.

1125
00:50:55,151 --> 00:50:56,118
The block is high.

1126
00:50:56,119 --> 00:50:57,753
Push it deep off your high contact point.

1127
00:50:58,054 --> 00:50:59,154
I'll clear out of the way.

1128
00:50:59,656 --> 00:51:00,655
Give me C!

1129
00:51:02,826 --> 00:51:04,160
Zero!

1130
00:51:04,527 --> 00:51:05,927
- A back set!
- Go!

1131
00:51:05,928 --> 00:51:07,996
- You have to swing.
- Go. There's no block.

1132
00:51:08,531 --> 00:51:09,564
A back-row attack from the right.

1133
00:51:10,034 --> 00:51:11,600
Dug up.

1134
00:51:12,035 --> 00:51:13,636
(Pohang battles back!)

1135
00:51:13,937 --> 00:51:15,471
- Push it.
- Let it go.

1136
00:51:16,306 --> 00:51:18,540
A push shot. Off the block and out.

1137
00:51:18,541 --> 00:51:19,541
Okay!

1138
00:51:19,542 --> 00:51:21,744
Hyun Ji packs so much power
into her swings.

1139
00:51:21,745 --> 00:51:22,977
- Great.
- Good.

1140
00:51:22,978 --> 00:51:23,812
Young In.

1141
00:51:24,114 --> 00:51:27,015
Don't hit straight into the block.
Aim for the seams!

1142
00:51:28,218 --> 00:51:29,251
(She watches intently again.)

1143
00:51:30,286 --> 00:51:31,152
Hyeon Ju!

1144
00:51:31,788 --> 00:51:34,122
There are seams between the blockers,
so aim for those gaps.

1145
00:51:36,993 --> 00:51:38,493
Hit it deep...

1146
00:51:38,695 --> 00:51:39,828
Gyeong Hyeon serves again.

1147
00:51:40,597 --> 00:51:41,964
Zero! I've got it!

1148
00:51:42,465 --> 00:51:43,532
Another back set!

1149
00:51:44,234 --> 00:51:45,100
Swing!

1150
00:51:46,637 --> 00:51:48,537
So close!

1151
00:51:48,538 --> 00:51:49,605
Keep it up!

1152
00:51:49,672 --> 00:51:50,572
Hit it!

1153
00:51:51,774 --> 00:51:52,807
Hyeon Ju.

1154
00:51:54,510 --> 00:51:55,510
(Hyeon Ju unleashes a thunderous spike.)

1155
00:51:56,079 --> 00:51:57,046
They keep it alive!

1156
00:51:57,047 --> 00:51:57,746
(Young In comes up with the dig.)

1157
00:51:57,914 --> 00:51:58,714
Coming back over.

1158
00:51:59,849 --> 00:52:00,415
(Whoosh!)

1159
00:52:01,184 --> 00:52:03,252
- Off the block and out!
- My bad.

1160
00:52:03,586 --> 00:52:04,553
It's fine.

1161
00:52:05,221 --> 00:52:06,188
Sorry.

1162
00:52:07,190 --> 00:52:09,424
(Three straight points for Pohang!)

1163
00:52:09,425 --> 00:52:12,060
The Wonder Dogs can't afford
to let their guard down...

1164
00:52:12,061 --> 00:52:13,529
just because they're up big.

1165
00:52:13,530 --> 00:52:15,764
That's right. Pohang is a gritty team,

1166
00:52:15,765 --> 00:52:18,200
so this is still a lead
they can chip away at.

1167
00:52:18,768 --> 00:52:21,003
(We fight to the very end,
no matter who we're facing.)

1168
00:52:21,604 --> 00:52:24,439
(The bulldog mentality?)

1169
00:52:25,743 --> 00:52:27,443
When you have the momentum,
you have to ride it!

1170
00:52:27,444 --> 00:52:28,477
(The Bulldogs are building
dangerous momentum.)

1171
00:52:28,478 --> 00:52:30,079
Young In, take a little off it!

1172
00:52:30,080 --> 00:52:31,880
How hard are you trying to swing?

1173
00:52:31,881 --> 00:52:32,915
Hitting harder doesn't
automatically score points!

1174
00:52:32,916 --> 00:52:34,950
- You have to aim between the blockers!
- Okay.

1175
00:52:36,886 --> 00:52:39,255
(The back-row attack,
one of their key challenges in this match)

1176
00:52:39,756 --> 00:52:40,588
(And it ends in a push shot.)

1177
00:52:40,589 --> 00:52:42,191
Da Sol keeps...

1178
00:52:42,192 --> 00:52:44,226
setting up back-row attacks,

1179
00:52:44,227 --> 00:52:45,694
but they still haven't found their groove.

1180
00:52:45,695 --> 00:52:48,030
(A problem they still haven't cracked)

1181
00:52:48,097 --> 00:52:49,130
(Peeking)

1182
00:52:50,400 --> 00:52:53,401
Hyeon Ju,
don't jump too early on the block!

1183
00:52:54,137 --> 00:52:55,137
(Nodding)

1184
00:52:55,471 --> 00:52:56,505
The lead is trimmed to nine points.

1185
00:52:56,506 --> 00:52:57,740
(Gyeong Hyeon's third straight serve)

1186
00:52:58,141 --> 00:52:58,974
Mine.

1187
00:52:58,975 --> 00:53:00,609
C! Hit it!

1188
00:53:00,610 --> 00:53:01,844
- She charges in!
- You have to swing!

1189
00:53:03,513 --> 00:53:05,280
And it's stuffed!

1190
00:53:06,649 --> 00:53:08,850
(Hyeon Ju scores with a stuff block!)

1191
00:53:09,920 --> 00:53:12,454
Great timing, Hyeon Ju!

1192
00:53:13,056 --> 00:53:14,256
Hyeon Ju jumps really late.

1193
00:53:14,257 --> 00:53:16,324
We need to hit it quickly
while the set is still high.

1194
00:53:16,325 --> 00:53:19,026
Hyeon Ju is delaying
her block timing a bit,

1195
00:53:19,027 --> 00:53:21,896
and Enkhsoyol keeps getting caught by it.

1196
00:53:21,897 --> 00:53:25,333
(During the previous match
against the Pink Spiders)

1197
00:53:27,437 --> 00:53:29,471
(Coach Yun Hye watched the game
and took notes.)

1198
00:53:30,606 --> 00:53:33,241
(Even when a point was scored,)

1199
00:53:34,110 --> 00:53:36,745
(she stayed locked in on her scouting.)

1200
00:53:38,881 --> 00:53:40,582
(Among her detailed notes on each player)

1201
00:53:41,818 --> 00:53:43,052
("Enkhsoyol:")

1202
00:53:43,053 --> 00:53:47,155
("Try delaying the block
and jumping later.")

1203
00:53:47,156 --> 00:53:48,223
(She lowers her stance.)

1204
00:53:48,224 --> 00:53:49,224
(Then jumps!)

1205
00:53:50,393 --> 00:53:52,995
(A game plan tailored specifically
to counter the Wonder Dogs pays off.)

1206
00:53:53,896 --> 00:53:56,065
(She checks her scouting notes
once again.)

1207
00:53:56,066 --> 00:53:57,232
Let's go.

1208
00:53:57,434 --> 00:53:58,500
One more.

1209
00:54:00,570 --> 00:54:02,371
Serve to Enkhsoyol.

1210
00:54:03,840 --> 00:54:07,023
("Enkhsoyol: Keep targeting her with
serves when she's the primary passer.")

1211
00:54:07,452 --> 00:54:08,586
A shaky reception.

1212
00:54:09,286 --> 00:54:10,319
Down the middle!

1213
00:54:10,819 --> 00:54:12,786
Another chance for Pohang Sports Council.

1214
00:54:13,219 --> 00:54:14,586
Tip!

1215
00:54:14,586 --> 00:54:15,586
(Getting ready to defend)

1216
00:54:17,052 --> 00:54:18,719
Hyeon Ju tips it!

1217
00:54:18,719 --> 00:54:19,886
(A well-placed tip)

1218
00:54:20,719 --> 00:54:22,119
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 12
: Wonder Dogs 19)

1219
00:54:22,119 --> 00:54:23,652
Nice, great play!

1220
00:54:23,886 --> 00:54:25,686
Way to go, Hyeon Ju!

1221
00:54:26,319 --> 00:54:28,919
Hyeon Ju is finding her groove.

1222
00:54:28,919 --> 00:54:29,919
She really is.

1223
00:54:30,619 --> 00:54:32,552
The gap is closing.

1224
00:54:32,552 --> 00:54:34,219
It's too early to let their guard down.

1225
00:54:34,652 --> 00:54:35,886
Low serve coming.

1226
00:54:35,886 --> 00:54:37,419
Hyeon Ju, watch the low serve.

1227
00:54:38,252 --> 00:54:39,752
The ball bounces. Da Sol.

1228
00:54:40,386 --> 00:54:41,386
To the left again.

1229
00:54:41,386 --> 00:54:42,486
Slow down!

1230
00:54:43,819 --> 00:54:45,786
Enkhsoyol gets blocked.

1231
00:54:45,786 --> 00:54:48,286
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 13
: Wonder Dogs 20)

1232
00:54:48,586 --> 00:54:49,986
All right!

1233
00:54:49,986 --> 00:54:51,719
("Time your block a bit later
against Enkhsoyol.")

1234
00:54:53,419 --> 00:54:55,086
(Let's see.)

1235
00:54:55,352 --> 00:54:57,486
Get the first touch!

1236
00:54:58,119 --> 00:54:59,786
Hyun Ji!

1237
00:55:00,286 --> 00:55:02,352
If there's a double block, push it.

1238
00:55:02,352 --> 00:55:03,652
Don't swing down on it.

1239
00:55:05,419 --> 00:55:06,752
Da Sol barely keeps it alive.

1240
00:55:07,519 --> 00:55:09,519
- Free ball for Pohang Sports Council.
- Push it!

1241
00:55:09,519 --> 00:55:11,452
Hyun Ji spikes!

1242
00:55:11,919 --> 00:55:13,121
- Nice!
- Good.

1243
00:55:13,122 --> 00:55:14,719
("Seo Yu Kyung: Slow to cover
the deep corners. Hit it deep.")

1244
00:55:14,719 --> 00:55:16,052
Why aren't you getting set?

1245
00:55:16,486 --> 00:55:18,286
(Her tailored strategy pays off
every time.)

1246
00:55:18,552 --> 00:55:20,752
They trailed by more than 10 points,

1247
00:55:21,052 --> 00:55:23,586
but they've already cut the lead to six.

1248
00:55:25,752 --> 00:55:26,786
- Quick set.
- Hit it!

1249
00:55:26,786 --> 00:55:28,586
Spike. They keep it alive again.

1250
00:55:29,386 --> 00:55:30,419
Hyeon Ju.

1251
00:55:30,419 --> 00:55:31,419
A standing tip.

1252
00:55:31,619 --> 00:55:32,986
("Slow to cover the deep corners.
Hit it deep.")

1253
00:55:32,986 --> 00:55:34,686
("Mix up short and deep shots.")

1254
00:55:34,686 --> 00:55:36,786
(That's it.)

1255
00:55:37,386 --> 00:55:39,886
Are you doing that again?

1256
00:55:40,952 --> 00:55:42,352
Why are you in there?

1257
00:55:42,819 --> 00:55:44,052
It's just her!

1258
00:55:46,286 --> 00:55:47,286
Da Sol.

1259
00:55:47,986 --> 00:55:48,986
Hyeon Ju digs it up.

1260
00:55:50,786 --> 00:55:51,698
(Rushing)

1261
00:55:51,699 --> 00:55:53,086
- A tip is coming.
- Tip!

1262
00:55:53,086 --> 00:55:54,352
Stay close!

1263
00:55:55,019 --> 00:55:56,219
It's out.

1264
00:55:57,019 --> 00:55:59,386
Did the Wonder Dogs let their guard down?

1265
00:55:59,386 --> 00:56:00,386
Nice!

1266
00:56:00,386 --> 00:56:01,486
Good!

1267
00:56:01,486 --> 00:56:03,119
What's wrong with you? That was a tip!

1268
00:56:06,486 --> 00:56:08,519
Seriously! So frustrating!

1269
00:56:08,519 --> 00:56:10,452
Step up fast if the dig goes wide.

1270
00:56:12,852 --> 00:56:14,719
Yu Kyung, that's three you've missed.

1271
00:56:15,586 --> 00:56:16,586
(Hesitating)

1272
00:56:16,586 --> 00:56:17,586
Geez.

1273
00:56:17,986 --> 00:56:19,186
Can't we sub out the libero?

1274
00:56:20,652 --> 00:56:23,552
Whether Yu Kyung is playing well or not,

1275
00:56:23,552 --> 00:56:25,452
- there's no one to sub in today.
- You're right.

1276
00:56:25,452 --> 00:56:27,819
Yu Kyung is the Wonder Dogs' only libero.

1277
00:56:29,786 --> 00:56:31,319
Back set. Hyeon Ju is wide open.

1278
00:56:31,319 --> 00:56:32,319
Put it away! Just one!

1279
00:56:35,552 --> 00:56:36,752
It's 21 to 17.

1280
00:56:36,752 --> 00:56:37,819
Down to a four-point gap.

1281
00:56:41,119 --> 00:56:44,152
(Hyeon Ju scored 7 of the 10 points
in this comeback.)

1282
00:56:44,319 --> 00:56:46,686
Once Hyeon Ju finds her rhythm,

1283
00:56:46,686 --> 00:56:48,552
Pohang Sports Council is unstoppable.

1284
00:56:53,652 --> 00:56:56,852
(Staring at the replay)

1285
00:56:57,219 --> 00:56:58,252
It's short!

1286
00:56:58,252 --> 00:57:02,119
I couldn't stop thinking about Hyeon Ju.

1287
00:57:02,719 --> 00:57:04,552
She kept scoring,

1288
00:57:05,286 --> 00:57:07,486
so I guess I got a little impatient.

1289
00:57:07,986 --> 00:57:09,419
C! Give it to me right away!

1290
00:57:09,919 --> 00:57:11,619
- Hit it!
- Attack from the right.

1291
00:57:11,619 --> 00:57:12,619
Get low!

1292
00:57:12,919 --> 00:57:14,086
Go!

1293
00:57:14,352 --> 00:57:15,519
(Young In spikes.)

1294
00:57:15,519 --> 00:57:16,552
Hyeon Ju digs it up.

1295
00:57:17,686 --> 00:57:19,919
Hyun Ji steps back.

1296
00:57:19,919 --> 00:57:21,352
Spike!

1297
00:57:21,819 --> 00:57:22,819
- She scores.
- Nice!

1298
00:57:22,819 --> 00:57:23,819
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 18
: Wonder Dogs 22)

1299
00:57:24,452 --> 00:57:25,519
Gyeong Hyeon!

1300
00:57:25,552 --> 00:57:27,186
- Down the line!
- Yes, Coach.

1301
00:57:27,186 --> 00:57:29,219
I'll cover the left.

1302
00:57:29,219 --> 00:57:30,786
(Power server Hyun Ji steps up next.)

1303
00:57:30,786 --> 00:57:31,786
Hyun Ji serves.

1304
00:57:32,386 --> 00:57:34,386
(Bracing for a tough serve)

1305
00:57:37,519 --> 00:57:38,519
A heavy serve.

1306
00:57:38,819 --> 00:57:40,052
Clean reception. B-quick.

1307
00:57:40,952 --> 00:57:41,952
That was rushed.

1308
00:57:42,352 --> 00:57:43,752
Free ball for Pohang Sports Council.

1309
00:57:43,752 --> 00:57:44,852
Down the line!

1310
00:57:45,286 --> 00:57:46,419
Gyeong Hyeon tips it!

1311
00:57:46,419 --> 00:57:47,452
She scores.

1312
00:57:49,286 --> 00:57:51,019
Awesome!

1313
00:57:51,419 --> 00:57:53,086
Nice, Gyeong Hyeon!

1314
00:57:54,719 --> 00:57:56,686
It's down to a three-point game.

1315
00:57:56,686 --> 00:57:59,319
They have to stay locked in right now.

1316
00:57:59,319 --> 00:58:01,819
Pohang Sports Council is the team
with all the momentum.

1317
00:58:02,186 --> 00:58:04,252
- Nice!
- All right!

1318
00:58:04,552 --> 00:58:05,752
Way to go!

1319
00:58:06,652 --> 00:58:08,286
Wasn't it 19 to 7 earlier?

1320
00:58:08,286 --> 00:58:09,286
Yes.

1321
00:58:09,286 --> 00:58:10,319
I can't believe this.

1322
00:58:12,452 --> 00:58:17,019
We gave away points in such sloppy ways...

1323
00:58:17,886 --> 00:58:21,252
that I was completely speechless.

1324
00:58:24,419 --> 00:58:26,486
- Let's get it back!
- One point!

1325
00:58:27,219 --> 00:58:28,586
- Just one!
- Great serve!

1326
00:58:28,586 --> 00:58:30,186
Great serve!

1327
00:58:30,819 --> 00:58:31,986
(Power server Hyun Ji serves.)

1328
00:58:31,986 --> 00:58:34,452
Hyun Ji has a nasty serve too.

1329
00:58:34,452 --> 00:58:35,452
Hyun Ji!

1330
00:58:35,886 --> 00:58:36,986
Serve it deep.

1331
00:58:37,286 --> 00:58:38,352
Receive!

1332
00:58:38,352 --> 00:58:40,286
Short one coming!

1333
00:58:41,352 --> 00:58:44,219
Watch the drop. Stay sharp.

1334
00:58:44,519 --> 00:58:46,619
Yu Kyung rushed that a bit.

1335
00:58:46,619 --> 00:58:48,719
- She has a lot on her mind.
- Yes.

1336
00:58:49,386 --> 00:58:52,119
They need to stay composed,
especially in moments like this.

1337
00:58:52,119 --> 00:58:53,952
The players are getting rattled...

1338
00:58:54,419 --> 00:58:56,019
with the other team closing in.

1339
00:58:59,019 --> 00:59:00,019
One, two!

1340
00:59:00,752 --> 00:59:02,219
(I'll take this one.)

1341
00:59:04,219 --> 00:59:05,619
It's out.

1342
00:59:05,619 --> 00:59:07,319
(Out)

1343
00:59:07,319 --> 00:59:09,686
- Nice!
- Keep pushing!

1344
00:59:09,686 --> 00:59:11,852
- What a massive relief.
- It really is.

1345
00:59:11,852 --> 00:59:13,219
Again.

1346
00:59:13,586 --> 00:59:15,852
Keep your hands relaxed!

1347
00:59:16,219 --> 00:59:17,386
(One more point gives them a set point.)

1348
00:59:17,386 --> 00:59:18,919
It's 23 to 19.

1349
00:59:18,919 --> 00:59:19,919
A four-point lead.

1350
00:59:20,619 --> 00:59:22,686
Chae Rim, aim deep.

1351
00:59:22,686 --> 00:59:23,852
- On it.
- You can place it deep.

1352
00:59:24,219 --> 00:59:25,252
Okay!

1353
00:59:25,586 --> 00:59:26,586
Serve!

1354
00:59:28,419 --> 00:59:29,486
(Shaky)

1355
00:59:29,486 --> 00:59:30,552
Short pass.

1356
00:59:30,619 --> 00:59:31,619
- Pushed to the left.
- Cover!

1357
00:59:31,619 --> 00:59:32,652
Gyeong Hyeon spikes.

1358
00:59:33,986 --> 00:59:35,019
Right there.

1359
00:59:35,386 --> 00:59:36,386
- Yu Kyung digs it up.
- Down!

1360
00:59:36,786 --> 00:59:37,786
Da Sol.

1361
00:59:38,986 --> 00:59:41,152
- Chae Rim spikes!
- Nice!

1362
00:59:41,152 --> 00:59:43,052
It drops right in.

1363
00:59:43,052 --> 00:59:45,086
- Great set!
- Great set.

1364
00:59:45,419 --> 00:59:47,619
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 19
: Wonder Dogs 24)

1365
00:59:47,619 --> 00:59:48,886
(Set point)

1366
00:59:48,886 --> 00:59:52,252
That came down at a really sharp angle.

1367
00:59:53,286 --> 00:59:57,386
Chae Rim got the better of Seon Ah
on that one.

1368
00:59:57,386 --> 00:59:58,386
She carved out...

1369
00:59:58,786 --> 00:59:59,952
a deep angle for the point.

1370
00:59:59,952 --> 01:00:01,352
Set point for the Wonder Dogs.

1371
01:00:03,052 --> 01:00:05,219
Let's shift one step in on the block.

1372
01:00:05,986 --> 01:00:08,119
Stuff it! Shut them down!

1373
01:00:10,919 --> 01:00:12,197
I was mad.

1374
01:00:12,198 --> 01:00:14,986
Honestly, it fired up my competitive side.

1375
01:00:14,986 --> 01:00:17,519
I want to win. I know we can.

1376
01:00:18,119 --> 01:00:20,052
- It's 24 to 19.
- Okay.

1377
01:00:20,052 --> 01:00:21,052
Overpass, mine!

1378
01:00:21,086 --> 01:00:23,352
It's the Wonder Dogs' first set point.

1379
01:00:26,086 --> 01:00:27,352
Cover.

1380
01:00:27,352 --> 01:00:28,952
- Over!
- Over!

1381
01:00:30,919 --> 01:00:32,886
It's deep. A push shot!

1382
01:00:32,886 --> 01:00:34,086
Chae Rim puts it away.

1383
01:00:34,086 --> 01:00:35,352
Great serve!

1384
01:00:35,352 --> 01:00:37,219
(Relieved)

1385
01:00:37,452 --> 01:00:40,052
(Whew, we barely pulled that off.)

1386
01:00:40,552 --> 01:00:43,586
(First set, Pohang Sports Council 19
: Wonder Dogs 25)

1387
01:00:46,986 --> 01:00:49,552
Come on, let's get the next point.

1388
01:00:49,952 --> 01:00:53,219
The Wonder Dogs take the first set
25 to 19.

1389
01:00:53,219 --> 01:00:54,786
(Second-set timeout)

1390
01:00:55,119 --> 01:00:57,819
Overall, you're not playing badly.

1391
01:00:58,186 --> 01:00:59,552
You're doing well, but...

1392
01:01:01,686 --> 01:01:04,119
- something's off.
- Yes.

1393
01:01:04,919 --> 01:01:06,019
Something is still missing.

1394
01:01:08,219 --> 01:01:09,786
We're changing the lineup before we start.

1395
01:01:10,686 --> 01:01:13,419
Min Kyeong and Ye Eun are going in.

1396
01:01:13,919 --> 01:01:15,852
You stay tight, and you play deep.

1397
01:01:15,852 --> 01:01:17,252
- Understood.
- Got it?

1398
01:01:17,252 --> 01:01:18,286
- Yes.
- Yes.

1399
01:01:19,052 --> 01:01:22,486
We're going to use
our lineup strategically.

1400
01:01:23,286 --> 01:01:27,252
Min Kyeong's serves were dialed in today.

1401
01:01:28,252 --> 01:01:29,452
Cover!

1402
01:01:30,186 --> 01:01:32,652
Ye Eun has improved a lot.

1403
01:01:34,319 --> 01:01:36,619
They're ready to step onto the court.

1404
01:01:36,619 --> 01:01:37,652
(Subbing both outside hitters)

1405
01:01:38,319 --> 01:01:39,319
Next...

1406
01:01:40,319 --> 01:01:43,452
(The remaining piece is
the opposite spiker.)

1407
01:01:43,652 --> 01:01:44,652
The rest of you stay put.

1408
01:01:44,652 --> 01:01:46,719
- We're just swapping the outside hitters.
- Understood.

1409
01:01:51,286 --> 01:01:52,352
Young In?

1410
01:01:52,786 --> 01:01:54,719
She's frustrating to watch.

1411
01:01:55,619 --> 01:01:56,652
Swing away!

1412
01:01:57,986 --> 01:02:00,419
Against both Shujitsu High School
and the Pink Spiders,

1413
01:02:02,852 --> 01:02:07,252
she struggled to fight
through adversity on her own.

1414
01:02:08,052 --> 01:02:10,052
So I wanted to put my trust in her.

1415
01:02:14,419 --> 01:02:16,752
(Glancing over)

1416
01:02:16,986 --> 01:02:18,152
Coach, is my footwork okay?

1417
01:02:18,152 --> 01:02:19,486
My steps are fine, right?

1418
01:02:21,386 --> 01:02:23,552
Your last step needs
to be quick and light.

1419
01:02:23,786 --> 01:02:26,619
I didn't like your footwork
on that back-row attack earlier,

1420
01:02:26,886 --> 01:02:29,186
but I liked your backstep
on that tight net ball.

1421
01:02:30,052 --> 01:02:32,319
I knew this was my last shot,

1422
01:02:32,319 --> 01:02:35,719
so I didn't want to leave any regrets
on the court.

1423
01:02:36,819 --> 01:02:39,152
(While Young In gets feedback...)

1424
01:02:39,686 --> 01:02:40,686
(Glancing over)

1425
01:02:40,686 --> 01:02:42,186
(Glancing over again)

1426
01:02:42,186 --> 01:02:44,319
If you don't load your legs,

1427
01:02:44,319 --> 01:02:45,319
you'll keep losing your balance.

1428
01:02:45,319 --> 01:02:48,386
You have to stay grounded
no matter how tough it gets...

1429
01:02:48,386 --> 01:02:49,952
- if you want to level up your game.
- Yes, Coach.

1430
01:02:49,952 --> 01:02:52,119
And if you can defend and dig,

1431
01:02:52,119 --> 01:02:53,719
we definitely have a shot.

1432
01:02:53,719 --> 01:02:55,252
When you're blocking, like I said,

1433
01:02:55,252 --> 01:02:57,086
you need to get set and wait
for the swing.

1434
01:02:57,086 --> 01:03:00,386
You can't all crash in to cover
once you've put up the block.

1435
01:03:00,386 --> 01:03:02,952
Even if the pass is deep,
set it to the opposite.

1436
01:03:02,952 --> 01:03:03,952
We have Hyeon Ju.

1437
01:03:03,952 --> 01:03:05,286
She can hit out of the back row too.

1438
01:03:05,286 --> 01:03:06,286
- Understood.
- Understood.

1439
01:03:06,286 --> 01:03:07,586
You need to hit it deep and fast.

1440
01:03:07,586 --> 01:03:08,852
- Go for it.
- Okay.

1441
01:03:08,852 --> 01:03:09,919
(Hyeon Ju is instructed to hit deep.)

1442
01:03:09,919 --> 01:03:12,486
- Pass it clean. We have to take this set.
- Let's go!

1443
01:03:12,952 --> 01:03:14,519
- Pohang!
- Hey!

1444
01:03:16,919 --> 01:03:18,552
- One, two, three. Hey!
- Hey!

1445
01:03:18,552 --> 01:03:19,652
Young In!

1446
01:03:19,652 --> 01:03:21,252
- Aim deep.
- Got it.

1447
01:03:22,052 --> 01:03:23,286
The Wonder Dogs,
after taking the first set,

1448
01:03:23,286 --> 01:03:25,152
have changed their lineup for the second.

1449
01:03:25,152 --> 01:03:28,752
Yes.
Min Kyeong and Ye Eun are on the court.

1450
01:03:28,752 --> 01:03:30,186
- Get it!
- Yes!

1451
01:03:32,386 --> 01:03:33,886
Min Kyeong's back-row attacks tend
to fall a little short.

1452
01:03:33,886 --> 01:03:35,519
- You might be in a good spot there.
- Okay.

1453
01:03:37,686 --> 01:03:39,486
Min Kyeong always goes cross-court
when she hits short.

1454
01:03:40,286 --> 01:03:43,886
I'm curious to see how Coach Kim's gamble
to swap both outside hitters...

1455
01:03:43,886 --> 01:03:45,852
will pay off.

1456
01:03:45,852 --> 01:03:46,886
Right.

1457
01:03:48,052 --> 01:03:50,919
The second set kicks off
with new outside hitters on the floor.

1458
01:03:50,919 --> 01:03:52,019
- Mine!
- Go!

1459
01:03:52,486 --> 01:03:54,186
(Rushing)

1460
01:03:56,086 --> 01:03:57,386
(Hesitating)

1461
01:03:58,286 --> 01:04:00,152
They're running a slide.
A single-block look!

1462
01:04:01,586 --> 01:04:02,619
Bo Been puts it away.

1463
01:04:03,119 --> 01:04:04,586
Right there! Bravo.

1464
01:04:05,106 --> 01:04:05,972
Nice!

1465
01:04:07,326 --> 01:04:09,542
(The substitute successfully draws
their focus.)

1466
01:04:09,543 --> 01:04:11,377
- Nice!
- Great play!

1467
01:04:11,378 --> 01:04:13,446
Bo Been scores on a slide. It's 1 to 0.

1468
01:04:14,215 --> 01:04:15,182
Bo Been serves.

1469
01:04:17,352 --> 01:04:18,651
Short!

1470
01:04:18,786 --> 01:04:20,520
- Na Young, watch the short one.
- Serve!

1471
01:04:22,790 --> 01:04:23,690
Mine!

1472
01:04:24,192 --> 01:04:25,425
Seon Ah digs it up.

1473
01:04:26,761 --> 01:04:28,162
(Will it clear the net?)

1474
01:04:28,163 --> 01:04:28,995
Over!

1475
01:04:30,564 --> 01:04:31,430
A set!

1476
01:04:32,466 --> 01:04:33,499
And they put it away.

1477
01:04:33,968 --> 01:04:35,268
(Point conceded)

1478
01:04:35,802 --> 01:04:36,769
Na Young gets the point.

1479
01:04:37,104 --> 01:04:39,439
- Where are you going? Get that ball.
- Yes.

1480
01:04:39,974 --> 01:04:40,874
Sorry, my fault.

1481
01:04:41,208 --> 01:04:42,041
Da Sol.

1482
01:04:43,277 --> 01:04:44,110
Two is good.

1483
01:04:48,983 --> 01:04:50,116
(Da Sol signals to Young In.)

1484
01:04:50,117 --> 01:04:51,351
Let's get that point right back!

1485
01:04:54,356 --> 01:04:56,123
Ready!

1486
01:04:56,623 --> 01:04:58,725
I was surprised, honestly.

1487
01:04:59,460 --> 01:05:01,928
I hadn't been scoring,

1488
01:05:01,929 --> 01:05:04,597
but Coach Kim told them to set me anyway.

1489
01:05:05,766 --> 01:05:07,634
I wondered
if I could actually put it away.

1490
01:05:08,602 --> 01:05:10,002
- Ready!
- Zero!

1491
01:05:10,305 --> 01:05:11,171
I'm going right away.

1492
01:05:11,906 --> 01:05:12,973
Gyeong Hyeon serves.

1493
01:05:13,374 --> 01:05:14,207
You take it!

1494
01:05:14,208 --> 01:05:15,308
Yu Kyung with the pass.

1495
01:05:16,144 --> 01:05:17,043
Here!

1496
01:05:17,378 --> 01:05:18,378
Nobody's there to cover!

1497
01:05:18,612 --> 01:05:19,812
There's an opening!

1498
01:05:19,813 --> 01:05:21,080
(A prime setup for a back-row attack)

1499
01:05:22,450 --> 01:05:24,384
A right-side back-row attack scores!

1500
01:05:24,418 --> 01:05:25,351
That's it!

1501
01:05:25,687 --> 01:05:27,487
- That's it!
- Nice job!

1502
01:05:29,790 --> 01:05:30,724
(First successful right-side attack)

1503
01:05:30,725 --> 01:05:33,459
Coach Kim has been calling for this.

1504
01:05:33,460 --> 01:05:35,395
- And we finally see it pay off.
- That's right.

1505
01:05:35,496 --> 01:05:37,663
The set was a little low,
but you were late too, Young In.

1506
01:05:37,664 --> 01:05:39,632
Stick to the timing we worked on.

1507
01:05:39,800 --> 01:05:41,134
I'll start my approach earlier.

1508
01:05:42,103 --> 01:05:44,036
It felt great.

1509
01:05:44,806 --> 01:05:47,274
Still, I don't think
it was quite the swing I wanted yet.

1510
01:05:48,476 --> 01:05:50,577
Her timing was slightly off,
but she powered through it.

1511
01:05:50,578 --> 01:05:51,611
(Proud)

1512
01:05:55,817 --> 01:05:57,383
- Watch for the overpass, Ye Dam.
- Yes.

1513
01:05:57,384 --> 01:05:58,318
(Min Kyeong in the front row)

1514
01:05:58,386 --> 01:06:00,987
Hyeon Ju, aim for the seam by Min Kyeong!

1515
01:06:01,722 --> 01:06:02,588
Yes.

1516
01:06:04,859 --> 01:06:05,826
Here!

1517
01:06:06,694 --> 01:06:07,493
(Pohang is caught off balance.)

1518
01:06:07,494 --> 01:06:08,328
The pass is off.

1519
01:06:08,696 --> 01:06:09,596
(Hyeon Ju can't swing now.)

1520
01:06:09,597 --> 01:06:10,463
Move up.

1521
01:06:10,464 --> 01:06:11,364
- Cover!
- Go!

1522
01:06:11,599 --> 01:06:12,933
Hyun Ji.

1523
01:06:13,401 --> 01:06:14,301
There we go.

1524
01:06:15,302 --> 01:06:16,602
- Again!
- Off the block, still alive.

1525
01:06:16,905 --> 01:06:19,272
- Yu Kyung sets it to Young In.
- Swing!

1526
01:06:19,273 --> 01:06:20,206
(Back to Young In)

1527
01:06:20,207 --> 01:06:21,341
That's it.

1528
01:06:22,943 --> 01:06:25,077
What a swing! Yeong Hye keeps it alive.

1529
01:06:27,782 --> 01:06:29,182
Hyeon Ju.

1530
01:06:30,584 --> 01:06:32,151
(Through the seam in the block)

1531
01:06:33,254 --> 01:06:34,354
She puts it away.

1532
01:06:34,355 --> 01:06:36,022
(Pohang's game plan pays off.)

1533
01:06:36,023 --> 01:06:37,324
Nice!

1534
01:06:38,259 --> 01:06:39,893
Watch the seam.

1535
01:06:39,894 --> 01:06:40,793
The seam!

1536
01:06:40,794 --> 01:06:42,195
- Nice!
- My bad.

1537
01:06:44,331 --> 01:06:45,164
(Stealing a glance)

1538
01:06:46,901 --> 01:06:47,767
Nice.

1539
01:06:48,669 --> 01:06:50,737
Hyeon Ju scored nine points
in the first set alone,

1540
01:06:50,738 --> 01:06:53,840
- hitting at a 54 percent clip.
- Right.

1541
01:06:53,841 --> 01:06:55,975
(Hyeon Ju is building momentum.)

1542
01:06:56,210 --> 01:06:58,311
And as Hyeon Ju keeps scoring,

1543
01:06:58,312 --> 01:07:00,413
Young In can't help but feel the pressure.

1544
01:07:00,714 --> 01:07:03,416
I couldn't take my eyes off Hyeon Ju.

1545
01:07:03,651 --> 01:07:05,585
I had to prove...

1546
01:07:05,586 --> 01:07:09,189
that I earned my spot
in a Wonder Dogs jersey.

1547
01:07:09,390 --> 01:07:10,724
Hyeon Ju, I'll take the deep balls.

1548
01:07:10,725 --> 01:07:11,858
(The positional rivalry heats up.)

1549
01:07:11,859 --> 01:07:13,360
- Help cover the short ones.
- Okay.

1550
01:07:13,361 --> 01:07:15,195
(Libero versus libero)

1551
01:07:15,196 --> 01:07:16,363
Get in position.

1552
01:07:16,598 --> 01:07:18,064
Let's catch it right away.

1553
01:07:19,401 --> 01:07:22,903
I wanted them to see us win.

1554
01:07:26,140 --> 01:07:30,944
(The serve targets Zone 4.)

1555
01:07:31,312 --> 01:07:33,213
(Min Kyeong serves.)

1556
01:07:35,015 --> 01:07:36,082
(Dead on target)

1557
01:07:36,083 --> 01:07:37,550
That's it! Great serve.

1558
01:07:37,985 --> 01:07:39,619
- Mine!
- Shaky reception.

1559
01:07:39,820 --> 01:07:40,887
Gyeong Hyeon puts it up.

1560
01:07:41,221 --> 01:07:42,488
(To Hyeon Ju)

1561
01:07:42,556 --> 01:07:43,756
Deep!

1562
01:07:45,192 --> 01:07:46,259
The Wonder Dogs keep it in play.

1563
01:07:46,527 --> 01:07:47,393
Right side!

1564
01:07:48,196 --> 01:07:50,063
Da Sol sets it to the right.

1565
01:07:50,197 --> 01:07:51,731
(Young In goes up for the swing.)

1566
01:07:51,899 --> 01:07:53,166
She's going to tip it!

1567
01:07:54,001 --> 01:07:55,635
Young In scores on a push shot!

1568
01:07:56,337 --> 01:07:57,170
(Diving to the floor)

1569
01:07:57,171 --> 01:07:58,205
Let's go again.

1570
01:07:58,206 --> 01:08:00,607
- Nice!
- Great play!

1571
01:08:01,408 --> 01:08:02,708
Hyeon Ju scores a point,

1572
01:08:02,709 --> 01:08:04,810
and Young In answers right back.

1573
01:08:05,847 --> 01:08:07,247
It's 5 to 3, a two-point lead.

1574
01:08:07,815 --> 01:08:08,983
(Min Kyeong serves again.)

1575
01:08:08,984 --> 01:08:09,816
Here it comes!

1576
01:08:10,484 --> 01:08:11,417
A heavy serve!

1577
01:08:11,586 --> 01:08:12,653
There you go. Great serve.

1578
01:08:12,654 --> 01:08:13,486
Mine!

1579
01:08:13,988 --> 01:08:15,255
(Seon Ah keeps it alive...)

1580
01:08:15,256 --> 01:08:16,389
(and sets it to Hyun Ji.)

1581
01:08:16,390 --> 01:08:17,624
Put it away!

1582
01:08:17,625 --> 01:08:19,893
Timing!

1583
01:08:21,695 --> 01:08:23,529
Ye Dam with the stuff!

1584
01:08:23,530 --> 01:08:24,330
(Ye Dam shuts her down.)

1585
01:08:24,331 --> 01:08:25,264
That's it!

1586
01:08:26,166 --> 01:08:27,300
(No getting past Ye Dam!)

1587
01:08:27,301 --> 01:08:28,434
Ye Dam!

1588
01:08:28,435 --> 01:08:30,402
Good job! Nice!

1589
01:08:32,440 --> 01:08:35,808
The Wonder Dogs stretch the lead again,
6 to 3.

1590
01:08:36,443 --> 01:08:38,844
(Min Kyeong's third straight serve)

1591
01:08:39,780 --> 01:08:41,814
(Taking aim)

1592
01:08:43,751 --> 01:08:44,951
It's headed toward Hyun Ji.

1593
01:08:45,252 --> 01:08:46,152
(Dead on target)

1594
01:08:46,320 --> 01:08:47,186
Great serve!

1595
01:08:48,088 --> 01:08:49,055
You have to swing!

1596
01:08:49,490 --> 01:08:50,723
Right side!

1597
01:08:51,591 --> 01:08:52,625
- A back set!
- Hit it.

1598
01:08:52,826 --> 01:08:53,893
(And it goes straight to Hyeon Ju.)

1599
01:08:53,894 --> 01:08:54,794
Drop back!

1600
01:08:56,997 --> 01:08:58,364
- Hyeon Ju hits it long.
- No touch!

1601
01:08:58,832 --> 01:08:59,965
Out!

1602
01:08:59,966 --> 01:09:01,066
You're good.

1603
01:09:01,067 --> 01:09:03,002
- Nice one!
- Great serve!

1604
01:09:03,370 --> 01:09:05,071
Hyeon Ju got a bit too eager there.

1605
01:09:05,072 --> 01:09:06,006
Sorry.

1606
01:09:06,607 --> 01:09:08,741
(A chance to pad the lead)

1607
01:09:08,742 --> 01:09:10,009
Nice serve, Min Kyeong.

1608
01:09:10,678 --> 01:09:11,645
Stay calm. Don't rush.

1609
01:09:11,646 --> 01:09:13,012
(Min Kyeong's fourth straight serve)

1610
01:09:13,013 --> 01:09:14,246
Nice serve, Min Kyeong!

1611
01:09:14,247 --> 01:09:15,281
Great serve!

1612
01:09:15,916 --> 01:09:17,550
The Wonder Dogs lead by four.

1613
01:09:17,551 --> 01:09:19,919
(Coach Kim's serving sub delivers.)

1614
01:09:21,722 --> 01:09:22,656
We have to block this!

1615
01:09:22,657 --> 01:09:25,058
(Pohang handles the serve cleanly.)

1616
01:09:26,460 --> 01:09:27,427
A back set.

1617
01:09:27,928 --> 01:09:28,895
Hyeon Ju.

1618
01:09:28,896 --> 01:09:29,829
(Hyeon Ju charges in.)

1619
01:09:29,830 --> 01:09:30,930
Just swing!

1620
01:09:31,031 --> 01:09:32,164
Cover!

1621
01:09:33,968 --> 01:09:35,335
Great dig by Yu Kyung!

1622
01:09:35,336 --> 01:09:36,436
- There you go!
- Nice dig!

1623
01:09:36,937 --> 01:09:37,871
Left!

1624
01:09:37,872 --> 01:09:38,771
Mine!

1625
01:09:38,839 --> 01:09:39,905
Cover!

1626
01:09:40,040 --> 01:09:41,540
(Set to the right!)

1627
01:09:42,276 --> 01:09:43,276
Good!

1628
01:09:43,510 --> 01:09:45,511
Close the seam! Put it down!

1629
01:09:45,512 --> 01:09:48,214
Young In splits the blockers. She scores!

1630
01:09:48,515 --> 01:09:50,116
- Nice hit!
- There you go.

1631
01:09:50,117 --> 01:09:51,450
(That's what we're talking about.)

1632
01:09:51,451 --> 01:09:52,918
- That's it!
- Way to go!

1633
01:09:52,919 --> 01:09:54,887
(Nice one, Young In!)

1634
01:09:55,355 --> 01:09:58,157
(One of Coach Hyo Hee's training drills)

1635
01:09:58,525 --> 01:10:01,027
(When two blockers are up,)

1636
01:10:01,461 --> 01:10:03,496
(aim for the seam.)

1637
01:10:04,364 --> 01:10:06,899
(Right between their hands!)

1638
01:10:07,568 --> 01:10:10,202
(Putting her training into practice)

1639
01:10:10,404 --> 01:10:12,572
(Proud)

1640
01:10:12,573 --> 01:10:14,741
Young In is hitting her stride in Set Two.

1641
01:10:15,243 --> 01:10:17,877
- Great job!
- Looking sharp, Young In!

1642
01:10:18,345 --> 01:10:21,314
(Hyeon Ju is losing her cool.)

1643
01:10:21,716 --> 01:10:22,816
Hey!

1644
01:10:24,118 --> 01:10:26,318
Don't hit it right at them.
Go for the middle!

1645
01:10:26,319 --> 01:10:28,588
That's why they're all closing in.

1646
01:10:28,589 --> 01:10:29,522
(And the Bulldog Coach is fuming.)

1647
01:10:29,923 --> 01:10:32,258
(Five straight serves and counting)

1648
01:10:32,593 --> 01:10:33,426
Hit it!

1649
01:10:33,460 --> 01:10:35,061
- The pass is off.
- Good!

1650
01:10:35,062 --> 01:10:35,961
Great serve!

1651
01:10:36,330 --> 01:10:37,196
Step in!

1652
01:10:40,300 --> 01:10:41,233
She just sends it over.

1653
01:10:41,234 --> 01:10:42,201
Pass!

1654
01:10:42,202 --> 01:10:43,035
Mine!

1655
01:10:43,904 --> 01:10:44,971
(Where's it going?)

1656
01:10:45,706 --> 01:10:46,539
Swing!

1657
01:10:46,540 --> 01:10:47,206
(Soaring in for the attack)

1658
01:10:48,509 --> 01:10:49,409
Seon Ah with the dig!

1659
01:10:51,578 --> 01:10:53,080
(Yu Kyung fires right back.)

1660
01:10:53,081 --> 01:10:54,046
There you go.

1661
01:10:54,348 --> 01:10:55,214
Left!

1662
01:10:56,316 --> 01:10:57,449
(Ye Eun unleashes a thunderous spike.)

1663
01:10:58,519 --> 01:10:59,352
(A frantic scramble for the ball)

1664
01:10:59,353 --> 01:11:00,253
Nice!

1665
01:11:00,254 --> 01:11:01,955
Easy! Go!

1666
01:11:04,458 --> 01:11:06,091
(She keeps it alive...)

1667
01:11:06,092 --> 01:11:07,160
(and sends it to Hyeon Ju.)

1668
01:11:07,161 --> 01:11:08,061
Hit it now!

1669
01:11:08,796 --> 01:11:10,296
(Past the Wonder Dogs' block)

1670
01:11:11,198 --> 01:11:12,064
Out!

1671
01:11:12,332 --> 01:11:13,332
One more!

1672
01:11:15,503 --> 01:11:17,069
Come on! Nice one!

1673
01:11:17,070 --> 01:11:19,172
(Another hitting error from Hyeon Ju)

1674
01:11:19,306 --> 01:11:20,907
(Second set, Pohang Sports Council 3
: Wonder Dogs 9)

1675
01:11:21,074 --> 01:11:22,308
(Keep the momentum rolling!)

1676
01:11:24,511 --> 01:11:25,644
- Pass!
- Pohang barely sends it over.

1677
01:11:25,645 --> 01:11:26,512
(Free ball for the Wonder Dogs)

1678
01:11:26,513 --> 01:11:27,313
Free ball!

1679
01:11:27,649 --> 01:11:28,581
Here on the left!

1680
01:11:29,450 --> 01:11:31,384
- Yu Kyung with the second touch!
- Cover!

1681
01:11:31,385 --> 01:11:32,352
(Ye Eun rises up to swing.)

1682
01:11:32,353 --> 01:11:33,720
Cover!

1683
01:11:35,789 --> 01:11:36,756
(Off Hyeon Ju's hands)

1684
01:11:37,124 --> 01:11:39,558
Ye Eun scores off the block!

1685
01:11:39,559 --> 01:11:41,494
Touched!

1686
01:11:41,929 --> 01:11:42,962
Off the block!

1687
01:11:44,865 --> 01:11:47,199
(Other hitters are stepping up too.)

1688
01:11:48,235 --> 01:11:49,102
(They keep the pressure on.)

1689
01:11:49,103 --> 01:11:50,303
Get ready!

1690
01:11:51,105 --> 01:11:52,005
Watch Ye Eun.

1691
01:11:52,006 --> 01:11:54,007
Watch who's sending it over!

1692
01:11:54,274 --> 01:11:56,309
Coach Kim is making some sharp moves.

1693
01:11:56,477 --> 01:11:59,712
She's subbing in players
like Min Kyeong and Ye Eun,

1694
01:11:59,713 --> 01:12:01,815
along with a few others,

1695
01:12:01,983 --> 01:12:04,450
and it's really paying off today.

1696
01:12:04,451 --> 01:12:06,852
(The substitutions spark a scoring run.)

1697
01:12:07,488 --> 01:12:08,421
Ten to six.

1698
01:12:08,722 --> 01:12:10,389
(The momentum keeps rolling.)

1699
01:12:12,326 --> 01:12:13,527
Mine!

1700
01:12:13,528 --> 01:12:14,627
Yu Kyung with the pass.

1701
01:12:14,628 --> 01:12:15,862
Right away!

1702
01:12:16,163 --> 01:12:17,763
(Bracing for the swing)

1703
01:12:18,365 --> 01:12:19,298
Hit it!

1704
01:12:19,299 --> 01:12:20,700
(Young In takes a leap.)

1705
01:12:20,968 --> 01:12:22,169
(Young In, aim deep.)

1706
01:12:22,170 --> 01:12:22,969
Swing!

1707
01:12:23,771 --> 01:12:26,173
A powerful hit from the right!
Off the block and out.

1708
01:12:26,174 --> 01:12:27,640
That's it!

1709
01:12:28,308 --> 01:12:29,808
Yes!

1710
01:12:29,809 --> 01:12:30,576
Nice!

1711
01:12:30,577 --> 01:12:33,346
Young In's attack efficiency is up
in the second set.

1712
01:12:33,347 --> 01:12:36,181
Even the look in Young In's eyes
has changed.

1713
01:12:36,182 --> 01:12:40,052
You can tell she's determined
to do her part.

1714
01:12:40,053 --> 01:12:41,186
(A more aggressive swing)

1715
01:12:41,187 --> 01:12:42,690
All I'm thinking about is winning.

1716
01:12:42,691 --> 01:12:45,524
Coach Kim and the rest of the staff are
helping me,

1717
01:12:45,726 --> 01:12:48,194
so I'm confident I'll keep getting better.

1718
01:12:48,762 --> 01:12:49,795
Okay!

1719
01:12:49,796 --> 01:12:50,930
(Her confidence sends her soaring.)

1720
01:12:51,131 --> 01:12:52,431
That's it. Bravo!

1721
01:12:53,000 --> 01:12:53,933
Nice one!

1722
01:12:56,837 --> 01:12:58,605
Let's bring Yoon Ha in now, then.

1723
01:12:58,606 --> 01:13:00,072
- Another sub?
- Yes.

1724
01:13:00,674 --> 01:13:03,943
(One more sub to close it out)

1725
01:13:04,178 --> 01:13:05,044
Okay.

1726
01:13:08,116 --> 01:13:11,417
And now, a Wonder Dogs debut!

1727
01:13:11,418 --> 01:13:13,485
Yoon Ha checks in.

1728
01:13:15,188 --> 01:13:20,159
(Aim for Zone 3)

1729
01:13:21,028 --> 01:13:22,495
(Got it.)

1730
01:13:22,795 --> 01:13:24,897
- Yoon Ha might spark something.
- I think so too.

1731
01:13:26,166 --> 01:13:27,032
Serve.

1732
01:13:29,369 --> 01:13:30,969
- Mine!
- Great serve!

1733
01:13:30,970 --> 01:13:32,572
(A serve that disrupts the reception)

1734
01:13:32,573 --> 01:13:34,173
Nice serve!

1735
01:13:35,209 --> 01:13:36,043
Get it!

1736
01:13:36,044 --> 01:13:36,943
A push shot!

1737
01:13:37,311 --> 01:13:38,278
Hit it!

1738
01:13:39,513 --> 01:13:40,980
- Mine!
- Defense!

1739
01:13:40,981 --> 01:13:42,815
- Great defense!
- That's it.

1740
01:13:42,883 --> 01:13:43,883
- Get it!
- Free ball.

1741
01:13:44,284 --> 01:13:45,384
A quick hit up the middle!

1742
01:13:48,422 --> 01:13:50,656
And Pohang can't get it back over!

1743
01:13:53,227 --> 01:13:54,727
- Nice!
- Great job!

1744
01:13:54,728 --> 01:13:55,929
(A bold debut for the youngest)

1745
01:13:58,665 --> 01:14:02,068
Looks like we'll see Yoon Ha serve again.

1746
01:14:02,069 --> 01:14:05,971
Yes, her serve set up
a great attacking chance earlier.

1747
01:14:05,971 --> 01:14:06,708
That's right.

1748
01:14:07,410 --> 01:14:10,076
(Same target)

1749
01:14:10,876 --> 01:14:12,775
Her serves are quick.

1750
01:14:12,776 --> 01:14:14,975
Hyeon Ju, take care of the long shots.

1751
01:14:14,976 --> 01:14:16,875
Get ready for a short one.

1752
01:14:16,876 --> 01:14:19,676
(Alert mode on for Yoon Ha's serve)

1753
01:14:19,876 --> 01:14:20,776
Serve.

1754
01:14:25,010 --> 01:14:25,943
(Frustrated)

1755
01:14:25,944 --> 01:14:27,210
Another serve!

1756
01:14:29,810 --> 01:14:31,742
An ace!

1757
01:14:31,743 --> 01:14:33,110
Yoon Ha did it.

1758
01:14:33,710 --> 01:14:37,510
(A service ace right off her first sub in)

1759
01:14:38,243 --> 01:14:41,376
Coach Kim's tactical substitution
is paying off in the second set.

1760
01:14:42,776 --> 01:14:43,643
The current score is 7 to 13.

1761
01:14:44,810 --> 01:14:46,810
Now, a serve from Hyun Ji.

1762
01:14:47,176 --> 01:14:50,075
She actually has great serves.

1763
01:14:50,076 --> 01:14:51,142
Expect a tip.

1764
01:14:51,143 --> 01:14:53,043
(A serve for a serve)

1765
01:14:53,410 --> 01:14:55,009
Mind the gaps.

1766
01:14:55,010 --> 01:14:56,476
Bo Been, watch the net.

1767
01:14:56,710 --> 01:14:57,976
Leave the net to me.

1768
01:15:05,743 --> 01:15:07,210
(Caught in the net)

1769
01:15:07,610 --> 01:15:09,876
After hitting the net,
the ball hits the ground.

1770
01:15:12,543 --> 01:15:13,810
(Feeling relieved)

1771
01:15:16,176 --> 01:15:17,642
I'm sorry.

1772
01:15:17,643 --> 01:15:18,842
Sorry about that.

1773
01:15:18,843 --> 01:15:20,510
It's fine. Let's go again.

1774
01:15:23,543 --> 01:15:25,776
Get Yeon Joo and Tsubaki ready to sub in.

1775
01:15:26,643 --> 01:15:27,675
- Tsubaki, get ready.
- Got it.

1776
01:15:27,676 --> 01:15:28,810
(A back-to-back substitution?)

1777
01:15:30,210 --> 01:15:34,076
This strategy might determine
the outcome of the match.

1778
01:15:34,676 --> 01:15:35,443
Da Sol.

1779
01:15:35,876 --> 01:15:37,042
You can go to the left side.

1780
01:15:37,043 --> 01:15:38,442
- Do your best.
- Got it.

1781
01:15:38,443 --> 01:15:39,476
(Tactical instruction immediately)

1782
01:15:45,443 --> 01:15:46,842
- Nice!
- Hit it.

1783
01:15:46,843 --> 01:15:49,175
(The ball moves left.)

1784
01:15:49,176 --> 01:15:50,076
An open quick.

1785
01:15:50,643 --> 01:15:51,709
An out off the block for Ye Eun.

1786
01:15:51,710 --> 01:15:52,875
Nicely done!

1787
01:15:52,876 --> 01:15:54,475
(Ye Eun, another sub, hard at work)

1788
01:15:54,476 --> 01:15:55,410
(Cheering)

1789
01:15:58,110 --> 01:16:00,610
(This is our chance.)

1790
01:16:01,376 --> 01:16:02,776
(Running)

1791
01:16:05,776 --> 01:16:09,042
We have Tsubaki and Yeon Joo coming in.

1792
01:16:09,043 --> 01:16:13,476
With this, the Wonder Dogs have
three attackers.

1793
01:16:13,810 --> 01:16:16,542
We're going to make use of double subs.

1794
01:16:16,543 --> 01:16:18,242
Double subs are where...

1795
01:16:18,243 --> 01:16:20,875
we sub in to make three attackers...

1796
01:16:20,876 --> 01:16:23,243
when we're down to only two.

1797
01:16:24,410 --> 01:16:29,676
(The players rotate
when they win back the serve.)

1798
01:16:30,776 --> 01:16:33,943
(Da Sol was in the back
during the previous rally.)

1799
01:16:35,343 --> 01:16:38,210
(Upon winning back the serve,
players move to the front.)

1800
01:16:39,376 --> 01:16:42,176
(That leaves two attackers in the front.)

1801
01:16:42,943 --> 01:16:44,876
(Here, the setter in the front...)

1802
01:16:45,843 --> 01:16:47,843
(and the opposite hitters
in the back are subbed.)

1803
01:16:48,676 --> 01:16:51,143
(This leaves three attackers
in the front again.)

1804
01:16:51,476 --> 01:16:54,175
This is only possible when you have
two good opposite hitters...

1805
01:16:54,176 --> 01:16:57,410
and two good setters.

1806
01:16:58,243 --> 01:17:00,642
Having three attackers in the front...

1807
01:17:00,643 --> 01:17:02,642
will put more pressure on the opponent.

1808
01:17:02,643 --> 01:17:06,475
You leave them wondering
where the shot will come from.

1809
01:17:06,476 --> 01:17:10,843
We want to make it difficult
for them to block us.

1810
01:17:12,276 --> 01:17:14,776
(Feeling nervous)

1811
01:17:15,010 --> 01:17:16,109
Tsubaki serves.

1812
01:17:16,110 --> 01:17:17,975
Tsubaki will want to ace this serve.

1813
01:17:17,976 --> 01:17:20,410
Her friend scored with her serve just now.

1814
01:17:20,910 --> 01:17:22,243
Let's do this serve well!

1815
01:17:29,343 --> 01:17:30,243
Hyun Ji's reception.

1816
01:17:30,244 --> 01:17:31,343
(A sudden pass feint)

1817
01:17:31,443 --> 01:17:32,276
They saved it.

1818
01:17:34,010 --> 01:17:34,943
Spike.

1819
01:17:35,276 --> 01:17:36,410
Seon Ah's dig.

1820
01:17:37,210 --> 01:17:38,310
To Gyeong Hyeon!

1821
01:17:39,010 --> 01:17:40,010
The ball goes up.

1822
01:17:41,110 --> 01:17:43,342
(All attackers get ready.)

1823
