- Coach, six substitutions.
- Okay, thanks.

2098
01:28:00,846 --> 01:28:03,280
I'd already used
all my substitution cards,

2099
01:28:03,849 --> 01:28:06,184
so I had to think about
how to make the best use...

2100
01:28:06,351 --> 01:28:09,219
of the players left on the court
and still win.

2101
01:28:10,589 --> 01:28:11,656
Min Kyeong.

2102
01:28:11,857 --> 01:28:13,491
Push to the middle or tip to Zone Three.

2103
01:28:14,989 --> 01:28:15,793
You do it.

2104
01:28:18,363 --> 01:28:20,698
Se Yeon serves again.

2105
01:28:20,699 --> 01:28:22,499
It's going to be short.

2106
01:28:23,669 --> 01:28:25,068
It's short.

2107
01:28:25,337 --> 01:28:26,170
Set to C.

2108
01:28:26,972 --> 01:28:28,440
(The ball goes to Min Kyeong.)

2109
01:28:28,473 --> 01:28:29,306
The middle.

2110
01:28:29,307 --> 01:28:31,208
- Close the gap.
- Close the gap!

2111
01:28:31,209 --> 01:28:32,076
To the middle.

2112
01:28:33,178 --> 01:28:35,679
She takes the power off
and scores with a tip.

2113
01:28:35,680 --> 01:28:37,448
(Following instructions perfectly)

2114
01:28:37,449 --> 01:28:38,616
Nice.

2115
01:28:39,434 --> 01:28:40,985
- Nice job, Min Kyeong.
- Great!

2116
01:28:41,786 --> 01:28:45,088
(That completely kills their hopes
of a comeback.)

2117
01:28:46,825 --> 01:28:48,859
(And now she serves.)

2118
01:28:50,795 --> 01:28:53,697
(The star of the consecutive serves)

2119
01:28:55,267 --> 01:28:56,267
Ball to the middle.

2120
01:28:56,268 --> 01:28:56,967
(Min Kyeong serves)

2121
01:28:58,036 --> 01:28:59,770
(Target: Zone 4)

2122
01:29:00,405 --> 01:29:02,873
(The target remains the same.)

2123
01:29:06,745 --> 01:29:08,512
- There it is.
- Seriously?

2124
01:29:08,914 --> 01:29:09,947
That's long.

2125
01:29:10,282 --> 01:29:11,249
It's over.

2126
01:29:11,250 --> 01:29:13,251
Min Kyeong with an ace!

2127
01:29:13,252 --> 01:29:15,686
(A serve pays off from the coach's trust)

2128
01:29:16,154 --> 01:29:17,988
- Nice job, Min Kyeong.
- Great job.

2129
01:29:17,989 --> 01:29:20,390
- Nice serve.
- Nice serve.

2130
01:29:20,525 --> 01:29:21,892
Nice serve.

2131
01:29:22,361 --> 01:29:23,760
Let's get another point.

2132
01:29:23,761 --> 01:29:25,219
My bad.

2133
01:29:25,273 --> 01:29:27,898
It's okay. Let's get right back into it.

2134
01:29:28,566 --> 01:29:30,400
(Target Hyun Ji again.)

2135
01:29:31,102 --> 01:29:32,168
It's 22 to 16.

2136
01:29:34,873 --> 01:29:35,606
(Another shaky reception)

2137
01:29:35,607 --> 01:29:37,007
- Hey!
- Get it!

2138
01:29:39,945 --> 01:29:41,346
A chance.

2139
01:29:41,363 --> 01:29:41,922
(A high ball)

2140
01:29:41,946 --> 01:29:42,913
It goes over.

2141
01:29:43,448 --> 01:29:44,114
(A high ball)

2142
01:29:44,115 --> 01:29:45,519
- Over here.
- Set to C, right away.

2143
01:29:45,720 --> 01:29:47,077
Smash it.

2144
01:29:47,085 --> 01:29:47,951
It's a one-woman block!

2145
01:29:49,254 --> 01:29:50,855
- A back set for the spike.
- Mine!

2146
01:29:50,856 --> 01:29:52,056
Set to C again!

2147
01:29:52,057 --> 01:29:53,591
Yu Kyung sets it up again.

2148
01:29:53,592 --> 01:29:54,491
(Another chance...)

2149
01:29:54,492 --> 01:29:55,492
Young In.

2150
01:29:55,493 --> 01:29:56,259
(for Young In)

2151
01:29:56,795 --> 01:29:58,262
(The coach had told her to...)

2152
01:29:58,263 --> 01:29:59,397
(hit it deep.)

2153
01:30:01,400 --> 01:30:04,102
A powerful line hit to the right!

2154
01:30:04,103 --> 01:30:05,002
- Nice.
- That's right.

2155
01:30:05,003 --> 01:30:06,170
(A satisfying deep spike)

2156
01:30:06,171 --> 01:30:07,571
Nice job.

2157
01:30:07,639 --> 01:30:09,006
That was a great deep shot.

2158
01:30:09,507 --> 01:30:10,706
It's our serve.

2159
01:30:10,707 --> 01:30:14,077
Young In has really stepped up her game.

2160
01:30:15,580 --> 01:30:18,148
(A perfectly placed powerful attack)

2161
01:30:20,852 --> 01:30:23,587
(The opponent couldn't do
anything about it.)

2162
01:30:24,223 --> 01:30:25,522
Let's turn it back around.

2163
01:30:25,907 --> 01:30:26,957
Let's get right back into it.

2164
01:30:27,593 --> 01:30:29,693
- Give me a sign.
- Long ones are mine.

2165
01:30:32,047 --> 01:30:33,829
We can use the pipe attack
when Min Kyeong is up.

2166
01:30:34,822 --> 01:30:35,945
- Min Kyeong's pipe attack is good.
- Okay.

2167
01:30:35,946 --> 01:30:37,100
- Try it.
- Got it.

2168
01:30:37,101 --> 01:30:38,802
(A call for a middle back-row attack)

2169
01:30:42,674 --> 01:30:43,607
Front set.

2170
01:30:45,143 --> 01:30:45,976
- Hit it!
- Hit it!

2171
01:30:45,977 --> 01:30:46,843
Hit it!

2172
01:30:47,579 --> 01:30:48,646
Ho Bin to the middle.

2173
01:30:48,980 --> 01:30:50,814
- Yu Kyung receives it.
- Behind you.

2174
01:30:51,349 --> 01:30:52,459
(Back-row attack attempt)

2175
01:30:52,484 --> 01:30:53,384
That's it.

2176
01:30:53,385 --> 01:30:54,652
It's a tip.

2177
01:30:54,653 --> 01:30:55,754
(A surprise tip)

2178
01:30:56,055 --> 01:30:58,456
A tip down the middle. It drops.

2179
01:30:58,656 --> 01:31:00,828
(Min Kyeong scores
with a middle back-row attack.)

2180
01:31:00,829 --> 01:31:01,893
- Great job.
- Nice job.

2181
01:31:01,894 --> 01:31:03,759
- Well done.
- Nice finish.

2182
01:31:03,945 --> 01:31:05,048
Unbelievable.

2183
01:31:05,049 --> 01:31:06,060
The score is 16 to 24.

2184
01:31:06,084 --> 01:31:08,049
The Wonder Dogs are at set point
in the second set.

2185
01:31:08,284 --> 01:31:09,451
Young In, let's get this one.

2186
01:31:09,919 --> 01:31:10,785
Let's go.

2187
01:31:11,054 --> 01:31:12,120
Just one more point.

2188
01:31:12,555 --> 01:31:13,688
(Just one point to win)

2189
01:31:14,757 --> 01:31:17,459
Let's carry this momentum
into the next set.

2190
01:31:24,267 --> 01:31:25,234
Set to C.

2191
01:31:27,071 --> 01:31:28,337
You have to hit it!

2192
01:31:28,338 --> 01:31:29,438
Hit it!

2193
01:31:30,274 --> 01:31:31,206
Hyun Ji.

2194
01:31:31,307 --> 01:31:32,607
Smash it in!

2195
01:31:38,681 --> 01:31:39,481
It's out.

2196
01:31:40,383 --> 01:31:41,450
Out.

2197
01:31:41,451 --> 01:31:42,517
(Out)

2198
01:31:42,518 --> 01:31:43,352
That's it!

2199
01:31:44,320 --> 01:31:45,253
Nice.

2200
01:31:47,357 --> 01:31:48,559
(Second set, Pohang Sports Council 16
: Wonder Dogs 25)

2201
01:31:48,560 --> 01:31:49,959
Nice, Min Kyeong.

2202
01:31:50,260 --> 01:31:52,862
Even though they'd already used
all six of their substitutions,

2203
01:31:52,996 --> 01:31:54,763
with a variety of tactics,

2204
01:31:54,764 --> 01:31:57,733
Coach Kim took complete control
of the second set.

2205
01:31:57,734 --> 01:32:01,470
Also, Young In and Min Kyeong were
absolutely outstanding.

2206
01:32:01,471 --> 01:32:02,438
(New faces that stood out)

2207
01:32:03,039 --> 01:32:05,441
(The set score is 0 to 2.)

2208
01:32:05,976 --> 01:32:09,212
(A timeout before the third set)

2209
01:32:09,213 --> 01:32:11,179
Why aren't you saying anything, Ho Bin?

2210
01:32:11,180 --> 01:32:13,615
I told you to set the ball
if you're close enough.

2211
01:32:14,817 --> 01:32:15,750
My goodness.

2212
01:32:25,528 --> 01:32:27,329
You're not scoring
because you take easy shots.

2213
01:32:27,330 --> 01:32:29,465
Just commit to the attack, out or not.

2214
01:32:29,466 --> 01:32:31,333
You have to chase after it.

2215
01:32:31,334 --> 01:32:33,511
You have to put it away.

2216
01:32:33,536 --> 01:32:36,184
You have to give your teammates the sign.

2217
01:32:36,185 --> 01:32:37,116
Call for the ball first.

2218
01:32:37,140 --> 01:32:40,209
Don't just stay silent.
You need to communicate.

2219
01:32:40,210 --> 01:32:42,444
If we keep making mistakes,
when will we ever play?

2220
01:32:42,645 --> 01:32:44,446
They're making mistakes too.

2221
01:32:44,915 --> 01:32:46,580
You shouldn't move forward
while receiving.

2222
01:32:46,581 --> 01:32:49,250
For Min Kyeong's balls,
move inward as you receive.

2223
01:32:49,251 --> 01:32:50,652
Don't secure the ball first and then turn.

2224
01:32:50,653 --> 01:32:52,177
(She points out the biggest problem,
serve reception.)

2225
01:32:52,189 --> 01:32:54,300
Get close to the ball
and bring the reception up.

2226
01:32:54,324 --> 01:32:56,058
We can't make it 3 to 0.

2227
01:32:57,260 --> 01:33:00,362
(Meanwhile, Wonder Dogs have already
taken the first two sets.)

2228
01:33:00,363 --> 01:33:02,997
- Nice job, Min Kyeong.
- Nice call.

2229
01:33:02,998 --> 01:33:04,233
That call was intense.

2230
01:33:04,334 --> 01:33:05,367
- Yes.
- That really was.

2231
01:33:06,002 --> 01:33:07,570
I'll give you... Sorry.

2232
01:33:07,571 --> 01:33:09,080
When I signal you,
let's move out together.

2233
01:33:09,105 --> 01:33:10,773
I think it's fine now.

2234
01:33:10,774 --> 01:33:11,740
Okay, sorry.

2235
01:33:11,741 --> 01:33:12,741
(Coach Kim is the only silent one.)

2236
01:33:12,742 --> 01:33:14,243
Just signal in advance, and we're good.

2237
01:33:14,911 --> 01:33:15,744
I mean...

2238
01:33:16,346 --> 01:33:19,514
Winning the match isn't
the only thing that matters.

2239
01:33:23,453 --> 01:33:26,688
There are things we can take away
from the way we're playing,

2240
01:33:26,923 --> 01:33:29,291
but so many things aren't working at all.

2241
01:33:32,962 --> 01:33:35,696
We need to get better at the things
we can execute more perfectly.

2242
01:33:35,697 --> 01:33:37,165
There were those free balls coming over,

2243
01:33:37,166 --> 01:33:39,868
and those short attacks. Things like that.

2244
01:33:40,103 --> 01:33:42,871
There were things we could've done better.

2245
01:33:43,106 --> 01:33:46,707
We made too many mistakes
in terms of accuracy.

2246
01:33:46,708 --> 01:33:48,610
Even though we're way ahead right now,

2247
01:33:49,612 --> 01:33:51,380
this is a team that could still...

2248
01:33:51,381 --> 01:33:54,750
turn the game around.

2249
01:33:55,118 --> 01:33:56,618
That's how I see it.

2250
01:33:56,953 --> 01:33:58,721
They're the most basic fundamentals.

2251
01:33:58,722 --> 01:34:01,323
Why aren't you following
the things we discussed?

2252
01:34:01,324 --> 01:34:02,925
What's the score right now?

2253
01:34:03,360 --> 01:34:04,991
Watch your timing carefully
on high balls...

2254
01:34:04,993 --> 01:34:06,290
and mind the timing of the blocks too.

2255
01:34:06,291 --> 01:34:09,023
Your timing was off
on Hyeon Ju's attack earlier too.

2256
01:34:09,024 --> 01:34:10,456
And don't forget
to put the ball in the middle.

2257
01:34:10,457 --> 01:34:13,490
Make sure you're in the right position
and pay attention to all the details.

2258
01:34:13,491 --> 01:34:15,291
- Those things are really important.
- Yes, Coach.

2259
01:34:17,424 --> 01:34:19,590
Ye Dam, your timing is
consistently a little too early.

2260
01:34:19,591 --> 01:34:22,056
You're just reaching up to meet the ball,
so you're jumping too soon.

2261
01:34:22,057 --> 01:34:24,857
What did I tell you to do
when blocking a high ball?

2262
01:34:25,491 --> 01:34:27,056
I told you to plant your feet first.

2263
01:34:27,057 --> 01:34:28,956
You need to bend your knees
before you jump to get the timing right.

2264
01:34:28,957 --> 01:34:32,057
You're just jumping to reach the ball,
so you're too early.

2265
01:34:32,391 --> 01:34:34,457
- Bend your knees and then jump.
- Got it.

2266
01:34:35,791 --> 01:34:39,457
The lineup for Set 3 is the same as Set 2.

2267
01:34:40,224 --> 01:34:42,557
(Is it going to be a shutout...)

2268
01:34:43,024 --> 01:34:45,356
(or a comeback?)

2269
01:34:45,357 --> 01:34:46,824
Let's get right into it.
Watch for the tip.

2270
01:34:47,291 --> 01:34:48,015
I'll serve!

2271
01:34:48,016 --> 01:34:49,257
(The fate of the match rides
on the third set.)

2272
01:34:50,391 --> 01:34:51,557
The third set is underway.

2273
01:34:56,257 --> 01:34:57,124
You have to bend your knees.

2274
01:34:57,791 --> 01:34:59,456
(Bending)

2275
01:34:59,457 --> 01:35:00,524
There it is.

2276
01:35:02,424 --> 01:35:05,391
Hyun Ji spikes, and it's blocked!

2277
01:35:06,291 --> 01:35:07,157
Great.

2278
01:35:07,158 --> 01:35:08,957
(Clenching her fist)

2279
01:35:09,424 --> 01:35:10,324
(Good job.)

2280
01:35:10,691 --> 01:35:14,191
- A zero-tempo attack.
- Zero.

2281
01:35:15,324 --> 01:35:17,891
Ye Dam's been putting up quite a wall!

2282
01:35:19,257 --> 01:35:21,724
(Frustrated)

2283
01:35:22,424 --> 01:35:24,924
You were too early just now too.

2284
01:35:25,591 --> 01:35:27,482
You're hitting the ball on your way down.

2285
01:35:27,562 --> 01:35:28,690
- Right.
- You were on your way down.

2286
01:35:28,691 --> 01:35:30,124
You're still a bit too early.

2287
01:35:30,757 --> 01:35:32,291
- I'll serve.
- The score is 1 to 0.

2288
01:35:36,024 --> 01:35:36,717
Swing!

2289
01:35:36,757 --> 01:35:38,057
Go in!

2290
01:35:40,624 --> 01:35:41,457
To the middle.

2291
01:35:41,457 --> 01:35:42,324
It's out!

2292
01:35:42,325 --> 01:35:44,423
(Line out)

2293
01:35:44,424 --> 01:35:47,156
- Nice!
- Nice!

2294
01:35:47,157 --> 01:35:49,424
- That was a high block by Ye Dam.
- Right.

2295
01:35:50,257 --> 01:35:52,790
I think the opponent had to hit
the ball a little higher because of it.

2296
01:35:52,791 --> 01:35:55,557
She had no choice
but to be aware of Ye Dam.

2297
01:35:58,291 --> 01:36:01,291
Where's your confidence?
Just hit it. It's fine.

2298
01:36:02,624 --> 01:36:03,491
I'll serve.

2299
01:36:03,492 --> 01:36:05,357
(Bo Been goes
for her third consecutive serve.)

2300
01:36:06,791 --> 01:36:07,657
Block it.

2301
01:36:08,224 --> 01:36:08,991
It's dug up!

2302
01:36:08,992 --> 01:36:10,624
(Will it make it over the net?)

2303
01:36:12,324 --> 01:36:13,324
It doesn't make it over.

2304
01:36:15,291 --> 01:36:16,124
That's it.

2305
01:36:17,557 --> 01:36:20,457
She was wary of Ye Dam again just now.

2306
01:36:24,324 --> 01:36:26,957
Hyun Ji, why are you waiting?

2307
01:36:28,491 --> 01:36:29,391
(She's told to attack directly.)

2308
01:36:29,391 --> 01:36:30,357
The score is 3 to 0.

2309
01:36:31,091 --> 01:36:32,124
In 1, 2.

2310
01:36:33,791 --> 01:36:34,657
C!

2311
01:36:36,891 --> 01:36:38,824
Get up quickly and hit it!

2312
01:36:39,257 --> 01:36:40,157
Hyun Ji with a powerful hit!

2313
01:36:40,857 --> 01:36:41,857
And it's in.

2314
01:36:42,657 --> 01:36:43,823
Did that hit her face?

2315
01:36:43,824 --> 01:36:46,257
That was a really hard hit.

2316
01:36:47,424 --> 01:36:51,123
Bo Been didn't flinch,
even though the ball came at her...

2317
01:36:51,124 --> 01:36:52,791
with so much force.

2318
01:36:54,124 --> 01:36:56,691
I'm sorry. That was my defensive mistake.

2319
01:36:58,191 --> 01:36:59,790
You couldn't even make the dig,

2320
01:36:59,791 --> 01:37:01,624
- so don't act like it hurt.
- Yes, Coach.

2321
01:37:02,424 --> 01:37:03,490
The ball had already bounced.

2322
01:37:03,491 --> 01:37:04,924
(Strict feedback)

2323
01:37:06,091 --> 01:37:07,157
Hyun Ji, serve it.

2324
01:37:07,957 --> 01:37:08,824
Put some power into it.

2325
01:37:08,957 --> 01:37:10,491
(Nodding)

2326
01:37:10,724 --> 01:37:13,057
It's a short serve.

2327
01:37:13,324 --> 01:37:14,991
It's going to drop.

2328
01:37:15,357 --> 01:37:17,024
It's a drop serve aimed between us.

2329
01:37:17,291 --> 01:37:18,157
Let's get another!

2330
01:37:19,357 --> 01:37:20,357
(Back-row attack signal)

2331
01:37:20,358 --> 01:37:21,556
A zero-tempo attack.

2332
01:37:21,557 --> 01:37:23,624
(Signal received)

2333
01:37:24,724 --> 01:37:27,391
(Strong Hyun Ji gets ready
to unleash her serve.)

2334
01:37:30,424 --> 01:37:31,291
A powerful serve!

2335
01:37:31,491 --> 01:37:32,324
- The middle.
- Da Sol!

2336
01:37:32,457 --> 01:37:33,956
Da Sol digs it underhand.

2337
01:37:33,957 --> 01:37:35,190
They rush in for the spike!

2338
01:37:35,191 --> 01:37:36,024
(The left side is blocked.)

2339
01:37:37,824 --> 01:37:38,624
It's smashed down.

2340
01:37:39,691 --> 01:37:40,923
(Young In dives for the dig.)

2341
01:37:40,924 --> 01:37:41,724
Good.

2342
01:37:42,157 --> 01:37:42,957
They keep the rally going.

2343
01:37:42,958 --> 01:37:45,157
(The ball Young In kept alive)

2344
01:37:46,224 --> 01:37:47,490
Yeong Hye with a back set.

2345
01:37:47,491 --> 01:37:48,923
(Hyeon Ju tips it over.)

2346
01:37:48,924 --> 01:37:50,437
Right corner! Cover!

2347
01:37:50,438 --> 01:37:51,591
(Young In's chance for a back-row attack)

2348
01:37:52,051 --> 01:37:53,424
(Dashing backward)

2349
01:37:54,557 --> 01:37:55,357
Smash it.

2350
01:37:56,891 --> 01:37:57,757
That's it!

2351
01:37:59,491 --> 01:38:01,123
A back-row attack.

2352
01:38:01,124 --> 01:38:02,990
Young In puts it away!

2353
01:38:02,991 --> 01:38:05,190
(We did it!)

2354
01:38:05,191 --> 01:38:06,323
That's it!

2355
01:38:06,324 --> 01:38:07,556
(Their back-row attacks are paying off.)

2356
01:38:07,557 --> 01:38:09,457
Young In's playing really well today.

2357
01:38:10,091 --> 01:38:10,924
Too much float.

2358
01:38:11,624 --> 01:38:13,823
Why are you reeling back to hit it?

2359
01:38:13,824 --> 01:38:15,423
- Just swing right away.
- Okay.

2360
01:38:15,424 --> 01:38:17,590
Don't hold back.
Don't twist and just hit it immediately.

2361
01:38:17,591 --> 01:38:18,357
Got it.

2362
01:38:22,191 --> 01:38:23,957
We came here to win, so we will win.

2363
01:38:24,357 --> 01:38:27,856
I really want to show everyone
just how much grit...

2364
01:38:27,857 --> 01:38:29,157
the Pohang players have.

2365
01:38:29,791 --> 01:38:31,657
Gyeong Hyeon.

2366
01:38:32,224 --> 01:38:33,124
(Nodding)

2367
01:38:33,324 --> 01:38:35,024
Hyeon Ju!

2368
01:38:35,491 --> 01:38:36,757
(Nodding)

2369
01:38:37,057 --> 01:38:39,457
Cut it off their run.

2370
01:38:42,424 --> 01:38:43,291
(Hyeon Ju sets up the ball.)

2371
01:38:45,224 --> 01:38:46,457
(Touch)

2372
01:38:46,757 --> 01:38:48,256
She goes for the spike!

2373
01:38:48,257 --> 01:38:49,390
(A block touch-out)

2374
01:38:49,391 --> 01:38:51,157
The ball goes off the block and out!

2375
01:38:52,324 --> 01:38:54,191
The Wonder Dogs need
to be careful not to let them catch up.

2376
01:38:55,124 --> 01:38:56,523
Ye Eun, go for it.

2377
01:38:56,524 --> 01:38:58,156
Take your time.

2378
01:38:58,157 --> 01:38:59,524
Let's get a little more coverage.

2379
01:39:00,257 --> 01:39:03,591
(The fired-up Wonder Dogs
vs. the Bulldogs)

2380
01:39:03,957 --> 01:39:04,824
The score is 5 to 4.

2381
01:39:05,927 --> 01:39:06,594
Go for it!

2382
01:39:07,124 --> 01:39:07,957
Great reception.

2383
01:39:08,957 --> 01:39:09,691
Ye Eun.

2384
01:39:10,891 --> 01:39:12,690
Ye Eun attacks from the left.

2385
01:39:12,691 --> 01:39:14,257
Nice!

2386
01:39:14,857 --> 01:39:15,857
I told you to go!

2387
01:39:18,657 --> 01:39:19,890
Gyeong Hyeon, you take it!

2388
01:39:19,891 --> 01:39:20,691
Okay.

2389
01:39:20,957 --> 01:39:23,024
Young In with a tip.

2390
01:39:23,291 --> 01:39:24,591
She gets low and digs it up.

2391
01:39:24,991 --> 01:39:26,557
She rushed that one.

2392
01:39:28,457 --> 01:39:29,424
(Gyeong Hyeon is up!)

2393
01:39:29,425 --> 01:39:30,491
Gyeong Hyeon, you take it.

2394
01:39:31,791 --> 01:39:33,156
She spikes it,

2395
01:39:33,157 --> 01:39:35,223
- and out off the block.
- Nice play.

2396
01:39:35,224 --> 01:39:36,590
Okay.

2397
01:39:36,591 --> 01:39:38,390
(Third set, Pohang Sports Council 4
: Wonder Dogs 6)

2398
01:39:38,391 --> 01:39:39,623
We need to put points away.

2399
01:39:39,624 --> 01:39:40,990
The gap isn't that big.

2400
01:39:40,991 --> 01:39:42,656
Young In, you need to finish this.

2401
01:39:42,657 --> 01:39:44,523
Just set it up right away.

2402
01:39:44,524 --> 01:39:46,956
- Da Sol sends a back set.
- It's a chance.

2403
01:39:46,957 --> 01:39:49,791
Young In spikes it
and it goes off the block and out!

2404
01:39:50,191 --> 01:39:53,623
She's looking much more confident today.

2405
01:39:53,624 --> 01:39:55,590
You've been hitting
down the line this whole time!

2406
01:39:55,591 --> 01:39:57,156
Hyun Ji, don't hold back.

2407
01:39:57,157 --> 01:39:58,491
Ho Bin needs to take that swing.

2408
01:39:59,957 --> 01:40:01,324
(Ho Bin is ready to attack!)

2409
01:40:01,524 --> 01:40:02,557
She attacks from the middle.

2410
01:40:03,091 --> 01:40:04,357
The score is 7 to 5, a two-point lead.

2411
01:40:04,382 --> 01:40:05,449
The gap is still small.

2412
01:40:06,891 --> 01:40:07,691
It's coming.

2413
01:40:08,791 --> 01:40:09,557
Good.

2414
01:40:10,357 --> 01:40:11,224
Point scored.

2415
01:40:11,225 --> 01:40:12,891
(Third set, Pohang Sports Council 5
: Wonder Dogs 8)

2416
01:40:14,024 --> 01:40:15,256
Come on!

2417
01:40:15,257 --> 01:40:17,390
Oh, this is driving me crazy!
I told you to go for it!

2418
01:40:17,391 --> 01:40:19,323
(A fierce back-and-forth rally)

2419
01:40:19,324 --> 01:40:21,957
Your hands are reaching back behind you.

2420
01:40:22,891 --> 01:40:24,324
We're busy!

2421
01:40:25,857 --> 01:40:27,990
(They need a decisive move.)

2422
01:40:27,991 --> 01:40:29,791
Da Sol, come out.
I'm putting Tsubaki back in.

2423
01:40:32,091 --> 01:40:34,256
Coach Kim is getting ready...

2424
01:40:34,257 --> 01:40:36,624
to take Da Sol out and put Tsubaki in.

2425
01:40:38,024 --> 01:40:42,757
(Tsubaki struggled to get
on the same page with the hitters.)

2426
01:40:43,824 --> 01:40:46,423
(Is Tsubaki coming in
at this crucial moment?)

2427
01:40:46,424 --> 01:40:50,490
A team's strength ultimately comes down
to its offense.

2428
01:40:50,491 --> 01:40:53,623
I needed to bring out even more
of Young In's attacking potential,

2429
01:40:53,624 --> 01:40:56,857
and I thought Tsubaki and Young In...

2430
01:40:57,324 --> 01:40:59,724
would work well together.

2431
01:41:00,191 --> 01:41:03,124
(Her delayed sets didn't match
the hitter's timing.)

2432
01:41:03,891 --> 01:41:08,457
(She was perfectly in sync
with Young In during practice.)

2433
01:41:10,024 --> 01:41:11,924
Tsubaki and Young In have good chemistry.

2434
01:41:14,191 --> 01:41:15,269
Since Tsubaki delays the set a bit.

2435
01:41:16,124 --> 01:41:18,390
(The Tsubaki-Young In combination
stood out.)

2436
01:41:18,391 --> 01:41:22,090
I think their timing and playing styles...

2437
01:41:22,091 --> 01:41:23,724
complement each other.

2438
01:41:24,124 --> 01:41:26,356
Rather than making a double substitution,

2439
01:41:26,357 --> 01:41:29,890
Tsubaki and Young In will
get to play together.

2440
01:41:29,891 --> 01:41:33,624
I'm curious to see how they'll do.

2441
01:41:37,991 --> 01:41:39,590
Chae Min, get ready.

2442
01:41:39,591 --> 01:41:40,757
Switch Chae Min in for Hyun Ji.

2443
01:41:41,357 --> 01:41:44,390
Pohang Sports Council has
subbed in Chae Min as well.

2444
01:41:44,391 --> 01:41:45,824
(Hyun Ji out, Chae Min in)

2445
01:41:46,157 --> 01:41:47,923
I've never seen Chae Min play before.

2446
01:41:47,924 --> 01:41:50,191
But the Pohang players look
to be in better shape than I expected.

2447
01:41:50,557 --> 01:41:53,557
(An unfamiliar player
they know little about)

2448
01:41:53,857 --> 01:41:56,391
(Both teams' substitutions could
decide the match.)

2449
01:41:59,891 --> 01:42:01,123
Let's do it.

2450
01:42:01,124 --> 01:42:02,324
- You've got this.
- I'll serve!

2451
01:42:05,691 --> 01:42:06,756
Hit it!

2452
01:42:06,757 --> 01:42:08,524
The pass is shaky.
She sends the ball to the middle.

2453
01:42:09,157 --> 01:42:10,124
Yu Kyung.

2454
01:42:10,124 --> 01:42:11,057
Good.

2455
01:42:11,257 --> 01:42:12,890
Tsubaki keeps the ball alive.

2456
01:42:12,891 --> 01:42:14,391
(The set goes to Young In.)

2457
01:42:14,557 --> 01:42:16,124
(Chae Min goes up for a solo block.)

2458
01:42:16,857 --> 01:42:17,791
She targets the back right.

2459
01:42:18,424 --> 01:42:19,424
She covers it herself again.

2460
01:42:21,291 --> 01:42:22,157
The ball goes to the other side,

2461
01:42:23,091 --> 01:42:24,457
but they can't get it over the net.

2462
01:42:25,357 --> 01:42:27,257
- Nice work, Chae Min!
- Good job, Chae Min.

2463
01:42:27,624 --> 01:42:28,823
Good job!

2464
01:42:28,824 --> 01:42:30,457
Just watch your position, Chae Min.

2465
01:42:34,891 --> 01:42:37,023
I went in too early. Sorry.

2466
01:42:37,024 --> 01:42:38,691
We can't afford an unforced error.

2467
01:42:42,224 --> 01:42:45,457
Chae Min, take the tip.
And you, move to the back.

2468
01:42:45,824 --> 01:42:47,657
Chae Min, hit the half-cross!

2469
01:42:50,591 --> 01:42:51,791
The score is 8 to 6, a two-point lead.

2470
01:42:54,657 --> 01:42:55,991
(Tsubaki sets the ball.)

2471
01:42:59,391 --> 01:43:00,423
The ball goes to Chae Min.

2472
01:43:00,424 --> 01:43:02,291
Just hit it from up high.

2473
01:43:03,491 --> 01:43:04,491
She spikes it!

2474
01:43:04,824 --> 01:43:05,857
- Min Kyeong digs it.
- Cover her!

2475
01:43:07,857 --> 01:43:09,424
Yu Kyung, you should've covered that!

2476
01:43:14,124 --> 01:43:14,991
Hey!

2477
01:43:18,824 --> 01:43:21,556
The Wonder Dogs are
really rattled right now.

2478
01:43:21,557 --> 01:43:23,091
Let's get one point back.

2479
01:43:23,324 --> 01:43:26,590
Chae Min had so much potential...

2480
01:43:26,591 --> 01:43:29,256
that she was even picked
in the first round.

2481
01:43:29,257 --> 01:43:31,856
We had no information about Chae Min,

2482
01:43:31,857 --> 01:43:34,890
so we were even more caught off guard.

2483
01:43:34,891 --> 01:43:39,223
I found her attacks pretty threatening.

2484
01:43:39,224 --> 01:43:41,191
We hadn't been able to scout her,

2485
01:43:41,824 --> 01:43:45,624
so we were all a little thrown off.

2486
01:43:46,724 --> 01:43:48,357
The score is 8 to 7.
Now it's just a one-point difference.

2487
01:43:50,191 --> 01:43:52,391
Chae Min, get the ones in front.

2488
01:43:53,691 --> 01:43:55,291
Hyeon Ju, keep it inside.

2489
01:44:01,657 --> 01:44:02,657
Min Kyeong receives.

2490
01:44:03,924 --> 01:44:04,657
Spike!

2491
01:44:05,079 --> 01:44:06,046
Seon Ah digs it.

2492
01:44:06,580 --> 01:44:07,480
Send it this way!

2493
01:44:08,116 --> 01:44:09,448
Hyeon Ju on the attack this time.

2494
01:44:09,950 --> 01:44:11,651
(Hyeon Ju pushes it over.)

2495
01:44:12,686 --> 01:44:14,420
She scores! It's tied at eight.

2496
01:44:14,421 --> 01:44:15,855
(Third set, Pohang Sports Council 8
: Wonder Dogs 8)

2497
01:44:15,856 --> 01:44:18,224
Okay!

2498
01:44:20,961 --> 01:44:22,895
- It's a tip!
- Get in there!

2499
01:44:24,999 --> 01:44:27,201
Pohang has been closing the gap,

2500
01:44:27,202 --> 01:44:30,270
- but this is the first time it's tied.
- Right.

2501
01:44:32,506 --> 01:44:34,207
All right, reset. Take it slow!

2502
01:44:34,208 --> 01:44:35,808
Look at the score!

2503
01:44:41,248 --> 01:44:44,083
I was nervous. I wondered
if I should take Tsubaki out.

2504
01:44:44,084 --> 01:44:46,085
I really did consider it,

2505
01:44:46,320 --> 01:44:48,387
but I decided to trust her.

2506
01:44:49,156 --> 01:44:49,989
Tsubaki!

2507
01:44:51,759 --> 01:44:54,227
I was nervous, but I told myself
I could do this.

2508
01:44:54,361 --> 01:44:57,163
As the youngest player,

2509
01:44:57,231 --> 01:45:00,099
I wanted to give it my all
and play fearlessly.

2510
01:45:00,935 --> 01:45:01,935
Zero.

2511
01:45:01,936 --> 01:45:03,203
(Zero: right-side back attack)

2512
01:45:03,370 --> 01:45:05,338
Let's run it now!

2513
01:45:07,275 --> 01:45:09,543
Chae Min, hands up. Watch the inside.

2514
01:45:09,544 --> 01:45:10,510
Got it.

2515
01:45:11,179 --> 01:45:12,178
They're sending it over.

2516
01:45:13,647 --> 01:45:16,249
(Pohang comes charging back.)

2517
01:45:16,583 --> 01:45:18,217
They're tied at eight.

2518
01:45:21,922 --> 01:45:22,722
Here!

2519
01:45:22,923 --> 01:45:25,091
- Tsubaki.
- Watch the inside attack!

2520
01:45:25,227 --> 01:45:27,193
Right-side back attack. She scores!

2521
01:45:27,828 --> 01:45:29,595
- Chae Min, stay on it to the end.
- Yes.

2522
01:45:30,290 --> 01:45:31,998
(They're finally in sync.)

2523
01:45:31,999 --> 01:45:33,433
Great job, Young In.

2524
01:45:34,435 --> 01:45:36,669
- Nice!
- Good one, Young In.

2525
01:45:38,038 --> 01:45:39,739
If Tsubaki keeps delivering sets...

2526
01:45:39,740 --> 01:45:42,274
with that kind of speed,

2527
01:45:42,275 --> 01:45:45,411
her timing with the hitters
will keep getting better.

2528
01:45:46,081 --> 01:45:48,748
Young In's timing is best with Tsubaki.

2529
01:45:49,017 --> 01:45:50,917
- Right-handers get time to wind up.
- Right.

2530
01:45:50,918 --> 01:45:52,352
Come on, let's keep pushing!

2531
01:45:53,387 --> 01:45:54,287
Let's get up there!

2532
01:45:54,288 --> 01:45:55,388
The Wonder Dogs lead 9 to 8.

2533
01:45:56,223 --> 01:45:58,358
(Trusting their instincts)

2534
01:45:58,726 --> 01:46:01,194
If you move up, the pipe is an option too.

2535
01:46:02,329 --> 01:46:03,597
(Another shot at the pipe attack)

2536
01:46:03,598 --> 01:46:06,299
I'd love to see them hammer one home.

2537
01:46:06,300 --> 01:46:09,134
Exactly. When a pipe attack clicks,

2538
01:46:09,135 --> 01:46:11,370
it's so clean and satisfying to watch.

2539
01:46:11,705 --> 01:46:15,195
(Coach Kim's long-awaited play)

2540
01:46:20,314 --> 01:46:21,180
Serve!

2541
01:46:21,515 --> 01:46:23,816
Se Yeon, cover the short ones.

2542
01:46:24,518 --> 01:46:25,218
Mine!

2543
01:46:25,219 --> 01:46:26,719
There we go!

2544
01:46:26,720 --> 01:46:27,553
Give it to me!

2545
01:46:28,222 --> 01:46:29,155
A tip up the middle.

2546
01:46:29,156 --> 01:46:30,256
Young In digs it up.

2547
01:46:30,257 --> 01:46:31,958
- Come on!
- No, that's not it!

2548
01:46:31,959 --> 01:46:32,959
- Good!
- Nice!

2549
01:46:34,094 --> 01:46:35,061
Middle! I'm here!

2550
01:46:35,362 --> 01:46:36,195
- Mine!
- I'm here!

2551
01:46:36,464 --> 01:46:37,564
Nice, Tsubaki!

2552
01:46:37,798 --> 01:46:39,299
(Just like they practiced)

2553
01:46:40,048 --> 01:46:41,007
Let's do this.

2554
01:46:42,070 --> 01:46:43,970
Nice set.

2555
01:46:44,305 --> 01:46:45,605
Be ready!

2556
01:46:45,973 --> 01:46:46,973
There it is!

2557
01:46:47,174 --> 01:46:47,707
(Whoosh)

2558
01:46:47,808 --> 01:46:48,575
Hit it!

2559
01:46:49,777 --> 01:46:51,010
A pipe attack!

2560
01:46:51,011 --> 01:46:52,945
It drops in!

2561
01:46:52,946 --> 01:46:54,046
(The pipe attack pays off.)

2562
01:46:54,548 --> 01:46:57,350
(Finally!)

2563
01:46:57,351 --> 01:46:58,545
Not a single blocker.

2564
01:46:58,546 --> 01:46:59,719
(Even the national players are surprised.)

2565
01:46:59,720 --> 01:47:01,888
Nice one!

2566
01:47:02,157 --> 01:47:03,890
- Good.
- Nice!

2567
01:47:03,891 --> 01:47:05,826
- Good job.
- Nice set!

2568
01:47:05,827 --> 01:47:07,961
Nice set, Tsubaki. Keep it up.

2569
01:47:07,962 --> 01:47:08,896
Nice work.

2570
01:47:08,897 --> 01:47:10,964
In all the matches they've played,

2571
01:47:11,098 --> 01:47:12,799
that was their smoothest pipe attack yet.

2572
01:47:12,800 --> 01:47:13,833
That's right.

2573
01:47:14,301 --> 01:47:16,903
(Hyo Rim couldn't pull it off.)

2574
01:47:16,904 --> 01:47:18,905
She digs it back up.

2575
01:47:18,906 --> 01:47:19,672
Enkhsoyol!

2576
01:47:19,673 --> 01:47:22,175
(Da Sol couldn't pull it off either.)

2577
01:47:22,176 --> 01:47:24,410
A back-row attack!
It fails to clear the net.

2578
01:47:25,312 --> 01:47:27,046
(Tsubaki, 19)

2579
01:47:27,648 --> 01:47:29,210
(The youngest got it done.)

2580
01:47:29,211 --> 01:47:32,452
Ye Eun really let it rip
on that pipe attack.

2581
01:47:32,720 --> 01:47:35,655
That's the attack Coach Kim
has been waiting for.

2582
01:47:35,656 --> 01:47:36,589
Absolutely.

2583
01:47:36,891 --> 01:47:38,891
How does she do that with her hands?
That's amazing.

2584
01:47:39,860 --> 01:47:41,260
(Like this)

2585
01:47:41,929 --> 01:47:43,296
(Meanwhile)

2586
01:47:44,865 --> 01:47:45,831
Se Yeon!

2587
01:47:46,301 --> 01:47:47,634
I'm telling you to hit it!

2588
01:47:50,037 --> 01:47:50,937
No, hold on.

2589
01:47:50,938 --> 01:47:52,505
(The lost point fires up the coach.)

2590
01:47:52,506 --> 01:47:53,873
Hyeon Ju, where's your position?

2591
01:47:55,909 --> 01:47:58,611
(Checking opposite hitter Hyeon Ju)

2592
01:47:59,279 --> 01:48:00,246
Yeong Hye!

2593
01:48:04,485 --> 01:48:05,351
Hyeon Ju.

2594
01:48:06,687 --> 01:48:09,156
(Relaying the coach's signal)

2595
01:48:09,157 --> 01:48:10,590
It's 10 to 8, a two-point lead.

2596
01:48:12,893 --> 01:48:13,759
Come on!

2597
01:48:14,928 --> 01:48:16,428
Easy on the pass.

2598
01:48:16,597 --> 01:48:17,497
Mine!

2599
01:48:18,298 --> 01:48:19,198
Over here!

2600
01:48:19,766 --> 01:48:20,766
(Quick attack through the middle)

2601
01:48:21,002 --> 01:48:22,635
Jump sooner!

2602
01:48:23,371 --> 01:48:25,538
That's it. Hit it quick!

2603
01:48:27,007 --> 01:48:28,240
A delayed attack.

2604
01:48:28,241 --> 01:48:29,275
(Hyeon Ju's tempo attack)

2605
01:48:29,510 --> 01:48:30,443
Other side!

2606
01:48:30,444 --> 01:48:32,378
Hey!

2607
01:48:32,379 --> 01:48:33,413
Pohang scores.

2608
01:48:34,047 --> 01:48:35,948
(A point lost in the blink of an eye)

2609
01:48:36,917 --> 01:48:37,783
Nice.

2610
01:48:38,152 --> 01:48:39,586
- Nice job!
- Nice.

2611
01:48:40,788 --> 01:48:44,424
Earlier today, Coach Kim mentioned
this kind of delayed attack...

2612
01:48:44,425 --> 01:48:47,094
- and said the Wonder Dogs might try it.
- Right.

2613
01:48:47,095 --> 01:48:49,262
- But we haven't seen it yet.
- Exactly.

2614
01:48:49,763 --> 01:48:52,098
Winning today matters, of course,

2615
01:48:52,099 --> 01:48:54,734
but they also need
to sharpen their plays...

2616
01:48:54,735 --> 01:48:56,435
and try patterns they don't usually run.

2617
01:48:57,971 --> 01:48:59,271
Let's turn this around.

2618
01:48:59,272 --> 01:49:02,141
(The Bulldogs aren't letting up.)

2619
01:49:03,977 --> 01:49:04,944
Serve!

2620
01:49:05,579 --> 01:49:07,146
She's got a fast serve.

2621
01:49:07,147 --> 01:49:07,914
Got it.

2622
01:49:08,248 --> 01:49:09,715
(Chae Min serves.)

2623
01:49:10,818 --> 01:49:12,619
Send it to C!

2624
01:49:12,620 --> 01:49:14,254
Stay right where you are.

2625
01:49:14,321 --> 01:49:15,621
- Mine!
- The pass is short.

2626
01:49:16,990 --> 01:49:18,324
Min Kyeong powers it over.

2627
01:49:19,226 --> 01:49:21,007
(Stepping out of the way)

2628
01:49:21,328 --> 01:49:22,928
- Mine!
- Get over here!

2629
01:49:23,030 --> 01:49:25,531
- Free ball!
- We've got a chance!

2630
01:49:25,532 --> 01:49:26,632
They can't get an attack off.

2631
01:49:26,633 --> 01:49:27,967
(A free-ball opportunity)

2632
01:49:27,968 --> 01:49:28,835
Ye Eun.

2633
01:49:28,836 --> 01:49:30,002
Zero!

2634
01:49:30,938 --> 01:49:33,172
Tsubaki with the back set.
Right-side back attack!

2635
01:49:33,474 --> 01:49:34,340
Get it!

2636
01:49:34,341 --> 01:49:35,608
(Stepping back again)

2637
01:49:35,943 --> 01:49:36,876
Seon Ah digs it.

2638
01:49:37,611 --> 01:49:38,411
Hurry!

2639
01:49:38,713 --> 01:49:40,613
- Dink!
- Watch the dink!

2640
01:49:41,748 --> 01:49:43,248
Yu Kyung gets under it.

2641
01:49:43,750 --> 01:49:45,050
- It's a B!
- B!

2642
01:49:48,589 --> 01:49:49,956
They mistime the B-quick.

2643
01:49:49,957 --> 01:49:52,358
Okay, good job!

2644
01:49:52,826 --> 01:49:54,160
We got the point. That's what matters.

2645
01:49:54,595 --> 01:49:56,829
Ye Dam, you should've been ready.

2646
01:49:57,164 --> 01:49:58,631
Don't just touch it, Ye Dam.

2647
01:49:59,066 --> 01:50:01,067
Is it hot? Hit it!

2648
01:50:01,235 --> 01:50:02,602
- The ball isn't hot.
- Yes.

2649
01:50:02,603 --> 01:50:04,170
(The Bulldogs are on fire.)

2650
01:50:04,605 --> 01:50:06,606
(Leaning forward)

2651
01:50:09,309 --> 01:50:10,476
Get ready.

2652
01:50:10,777 --> 01:50:11,744
Just swing at everything!

2653
01:50:13,981 --> 01:50:14,914
Now!

2654
01:50:15,582 --> 01:50:17,716
- Cross-court, inside!
- Time your block!

2655
01:50:17,717 --> 01:50:19,718
They go left to Gyeong Hyeon.
She hits cross-court.

2656
01:50:19,920 --> 01:50:21,486
- It gets blocked.
- Cover that!

2657
01:50:21,487 --> 01:50:23,422
- Another attack is coming.
- Push it!

2658
01:50:25,993 --> 01:50:27,560
She tries to score off the block.

2659
01:50:27,561 --> 01:50:30,096
(She sends over the same cross.)

2660
01:50:31,398 --> 01:50:33,332
Nicely done!

2661
01:50:33,634 --> 01:50:34,500
Damn it.

2662
01:50:35,369 --> 01:50:36,569
(Pulling her hair)

2663
01:50:38,038 --> 01:50:40,706
This is killing me.

2664
01:50:40,909 --> 01:50:42,809
Gyeong Hyeon just keeps...

2665
01:50:42,810 --> 01:50:47,046
going cross-court, again and again.

2666
01:50:47,047 --> 01:50:47,981
I told you to hit it.

2667
01:50:47,982 --> 01:50:48,881
(That's it!)

2668
01:50:49,450 --> 01:50:50,583
It's tied at 11.

2669
01:50:50,584 --> 01:50:52,151
(Pohang Sports Council 11
: Wonder Dogs 11)

2670
01:50:52,753 --> 01:50:54,387
(A quick glance)

2671
01:50:55,289 --> 01:50:56,122
No.

2672
01:50:56,123 --> 01:50:57,924
(Last game's starters)

2673
01:50:58,158 --> 01:51:01,160
As a coach, I could get nervous
and make a substitution.

2674
01:51:01,562 --> 01:51:05,331
But I wanted the players out there
to fight through it...

2675
01:51:05,566 --> 01:51:06,666
and win.

2676
01:51:07,100 --> 01:51:08,233
That's what I wanted to see.

2677
01:51:09,136 --> 01:51:10,436
Let's run a good play right away.

2678
01:51:10,938 --> 01:51:11,871
Right now!

2679
01:51:11,872 --> 01:51:13,940
(No substitutions)

2680
01:51:14,274 --> 01:51:17,843
I didn't want to let my chance
on that court slip away.

2681
01:51:19,279 --> 01:51:20,079
C.

2682
01:51:20,681 --> 01:51:23,149
Watch for a short serve. Move up.

2683
01:51:24,852 --> 01:51:28,187
(Can they pull through without a sub?)

2684
01:51:28,588 --> 01:51:30,155
(Se Yeon serves.)

2685
01:51:31,692 --> 01:51:32,492
Mine!

2686
01:51:33,226 --> 01:51:34,092
Tsubaki, set me up!

2687
01:51:34,394 --> 01:51:35,627
Move your feet!

2688
01:51:35,862 --> 01:51:37,329
Close the gap in the block!

2689
01:51:37,898 --> 01:51:38,731
Tsubaki.

2690
01:51:38,732 --> 01:51:39,432
(Tsubaki sets it up.)

2691
01:51:39,933 --> 01:51:40,967
Tip!

2692
01:51:42,036 --> 01:51:43,903
Young In finds the gap with a tip.

2693
01:51:44,304 --> 01:51:45,170
Nice!

2694
01:51:45,939 --> 01:51:46,972
Nice one!

2695
01:51:47,374 --> 01:51:48,174
Good job.

2696
01:51:48,175 --> 01:51:49,742
(The Tsubaki-Young In duo clicks again.)

2697
01:51:50,444 --> 01:51:52,778
Tsubaki and Young In work well together.

2698
01:51:53,014 --> 01:51:56,549
This match should really boost
Young In's confidence.

2699
01:51:56,550 --> 01:51:59,218
And when Tsubaki sets,

2700
01:51:59,219 --> 01:52:02,055
Young In gets her timing just right.

2701
01:52:02,689 --> 01:52:03,622
Nice set.

2702
01:52:07,094 --> 01:52:10,229
(A quiet thumbs-up for Tsubaki)

2703
01:52:10,797 --> 01:52:12,398
(Rubbing her nose)

2704
01:52:13,400 --> 01:52:17,003
Actually, I was given instructions.

2705
01:52:17,004 --> 01:52:18,504
Nice serve!

2706
01:52:18,638 --> 01:52:21,306
(Tsubaki gets whisked away in Set 2.)

2707
01:52:22,609 --> 01:52:23,509
The "Room Of Truth."

2708
01:52:24,745 --> 01:52:26,346
(Off to Hyo Hee's "Room Of Truth")

2709
01:52:26,347 --> 01:52:28,849
You might go in with Young In
in the next set.

2710
01:52:28,850 --> 01:52:31,584
Remember the kind of sets she likes,

2711
01:52:31,585 --> 01:52:33,219
and be ready. You're going in.

2712
01:52:34,187 --> 01:52:37,823
(Young In's secret ally,
planted on the court)

2713
01:52:37,824 --> 01:52:39,358
(Got it.)

2714
01:52:39,926 --> 01:52:43,295
(A perfect set, just for her)

2715
01:52:44,197 --> 01:52:46,265
She'll set to you again.

2716
01:52:48,702 --> 01:52:53,406
(The coaching staff's secret-partner plan)

2717
01:52:53,407 --> 01:52:55,709
(More right-side attacks for Young In)

2718
01:52:55,710 --> 01:52:58,077
Tsubaki kept setting to me.

2719
01:52:58,211 --> 01:52:59,511
That made me want to do even better.

2720
01:53:01,615 --> 01:53:02,815
(Exhaling)

2721
01:53:03,717 --> 01:53:04,717
(Min Kyeong serves.)

2722
01:53:04,718 --> 01:53:05,518
Mine!

2723
01:53:06,219 --> 01:53:07,152
A shaky reception.

2724
01:53:09,589 --> 01:53:10,889
Chance!

2725
01:53:11,091 --> 01:53:12,158
Mine!

2726
01:53:12,225 --> 01:53:14,460
(The ball finds
Young In's secret partner.)

2727
01:53:14,795 --> 01:53:15,628
Tsubaki!

2728
01:53:15,762 --> 01:53:16,596
Tsubaki!

2729
01:53:16,597 --> 01:53:17,396
Tsubaki!

2730
01:53:18,032 --> 01:53:19,332
Take your time.

2731
01:53:19,333 --> 01:53:20,633
Nice footwork!

2732
01:53:20,634 --> 01:53:21,801
Come on!

2733
01:53:21,802 --> 01:53:22,869
You have to swing!

2734
01:53:22,870 --> 01:53:24,939
(Screaming)

2735
01:53:24,940 --> 01:53:26,506
Young In puts it down!

2736
01:53:32,512 --> 01:53:34,379
- Nice teamwork!
- Nice play!

2737
01:53:34,380 --> 01:53:35,881
Well done!

2738
01:53:37,350 --> 01:53:38,885
(Way to go, Young In!)

2739
01:53:38,886 --> 01:53:40,819
- Nice one, Young In!
- Nice!

2740
01:53:42,355 --> 01:53:43,355
You're doing great, Young In!

2741
01:53:44,324 --> 01:53:45,391
Nice. Thank you!

2742
01:53:54,367 --> 01:53:55,300
She's finally smiling.

2743
01:53:57,204 --> 01:53:59,272
(Smiling)

2744
01:53:59,306 --> 01:54:01,240
Let's go, Mom.

2745
01:54:01,808 --> 01:54:04,678
(Her dream shattered twice.)

2746
01:54:06,146 --> 01:54:07,413
Young In gets stuffed.

2747
01:54:07,414 --> 01:54:10,282
(A frustrating match)

2748
01:54:10,851 --> 01:54:13,286
You haven't watched tape
of your own attacks yet, have you?

2749
01:54:13,831 --> 01:54:15,675
I couldn't bear to watch myself play.

2750
01:54:16,038 --> 01:54:20,147
I wouldn't blame Coach Kim
if she benched me.

2751
01:54:20,838 --> 01:54:22,505
(Getting Young In back on track)

2752
01:54:22,506 --> 01:54:24,808
(It takes a village to help Young In.)

2753
01:54:25,543 --> 01:54:28,345
(Helping her break out of her slump)

2754
01:54:28,346 --> 01:54:29,413
Keep your feet moving.

2755
01:54:29,781 --> 01:54:32,316
(Wherever the ball goes,)

2756
01:54:32,317 --> 01:54:34,918
(we've got it covered.)

2757
01:54:34,919 --> 01:54:37,221
(Off you go!)

2758
01:54:37,989 --> 01:54:40,090
(With everyone pitching in...)

2759
01:54:40,558 --> 01:54:44,394
(to get their opposite hitter
back on track)

2760
01:54:44,796 --> 01:54:46,030
(When you score,)

2761
01:54:46,031 --> 01:54:48,899
(I'll cheer louder than anyone.)

2762
01:54:49,200 --> 01:54:52,669
(Way to go, Young In!)

2763
01:54:53,037 --> 01:54:54,771
(To help her turn things around,)

2764
01:54:55,540 --> 01:54:57,508
(Coach Kim weighs her options.)

2765
01:54:57,842 --> 01:54:59,519
Young In and Tsubaki click.

2766
01:55:00,020 --> 01:55:03,656
Whether it's a back-row attack
or a swing from the right pin,

2767
01:55:03,681 --> 01:55:05,515
their timing is dialed in.

2768
01:55:06,784 --> 01:55:09,953
(Tsubaki helps Young In bounce back.)

2769
01:55:10,120 --> 01:55:11,020
(Young In's secret weapon)

2770
01:55:11,021 --> 01:55:13,066
You and Young In have great chemistry.
Keep building on that.

2771
01:55:13,191 --> 01:55:14,389
I told her to set for Young In,

2772
01:55:14,413 --> 01:55:16,103
and now she's setting only to the right.

2773
01:55:17,628 --> 01:55:19,563
It's 15 to 13. Gyeong Hyeon serves.

2774
01:55:19,564 --> 01:55:20,296
Mine!

2775
01:55:20,737 --> 01:55:21,796
Yoon Ha passes the serve.

2776
01:55:21,820 --> 01:55:22,709
Just like that.

2777
01:55:23,434 --> 01:55:24,367
Tsubaki.

2778
01:55:25,336 --> 01:55:27,214
I want to keep getting better.

2779
01:55:28,205 --> 01:55:29,038
Swing!

2780
01:55:29,407 --> 01:55:30,307
Young In.

2781
01:55:30,508 --> 01:55:31,408
There you go!

2782
01:55:33,077 --> 01:55:34,744
The timing on that set is
right on the money.

2783
01:55:34,745 --> 01:55:36,546
They've unlocked a new offensive duo.

2784
01:55:36,547 --> 01:55:39,349
(Young In, a hitter they can count on)

2785
01:55:39,350 --> 01:55:41,518
Nice kill, Young In!

2786
01:55:42,887 --> 01:55:44,921
Nice! Great swing!

2787
01:55:44,922 --> 01:55:48,024
They put a lot of thought
into helping Young In bounce back,

2788
01:55:48,025 --> 01:55:50,060
and the key
to Young In's resurgence was...

2789
01:55:50,061 --> 01:55:51,962
(The key to Young In's comeback)

2790
01:55:51,963 --> 01:55:53,029
(Tsubaki)

2791
01:55:53,030 --> 01:55:53,964
Tsubaki.

2792
01:55:55,466 --> 01:55:56,676
A Tsubaki keychain, then?

2793
01:55:58,603 --> 01:56:00,647
She'd probably want
to keep Tsubaki close by.

2794
01:56:00,839 --> 01:56:02,749
"You're not going anywhere
while I'm still here."

2795
01:56:03,341 --> 01:56:06,843
Now that I'm getting more chances
to put the ball away,

2796
01:56:06,844 --> 01:56:08,722
I'm having so much more fun
playing volleyball.

2797
01:56:10,014 --> 01:56:14,117
(A year ago or today,)

2798
01:56:14,452 --> 01:56:15,996
I still want to play volleyball.

2799
01:56:16,278 --> 01:56:19,666
I need to keep my eyes
on the ball after I swing.

2800
01:56:20,725 --> 01:56:21,892
(Smiling)

2801
01:56:22,179 --> 01:56:24,614
(Pohang Sports Council
claws its way back.)

2802
01:56:24,615 --> 01:56:25,805
Just swing away!

2803
01:56:26,684 --> 01:56:30,086
(Hanging on like a bulldog)

2804
01:56:30,621 --> 01:56:33,122
(The Wonder Dogs stare
down their first loss.)

2805
01:56:33,123 --> 01:56:34,924
(And in the next match...)

2806
01:56:35,559 --> 01:56:37,059
(Season Two's first overseas trip)

2807
01:56:37,060 --> 01:56:38,761
(Vietnam)

2808
01:56:38,786 --> 01:56:40,415
It's impossible to predict.

2809
01:56:40,798 --> 01:56:43,166
(An unfamiliar volleyball powerhouse)

2810
01:56:43,167 --> 01:56:43,900
What was that?

2811
01:56:43,901 --> 01:56:45,335
(A whole new world,
even for a world-class superstar)

2812
01:56:45,536 --> 01:56:46,559
(Their next opponents)

2813
01:56:47,137 --> 01:56:49,005
(Lao Cai, a top-tier Vietnamese pro club)

2814
01:56:49,600 --> 01:56:52,602
Vietnam brings a different style
from traditional volleyball powerhouses.

2815
01:56:55,646 --> 01:56:57,447
(Their first clash against a 195 cm wall)

2816
01:56:58,616 --> 01:57:00,217
(National team star...)

2817
01:57:00,218 --> 01:57:01,718
(vs. national team star)

2818
01:57:01,952 --> 01:57:03,454
(An even taller wall to overcome)

2819
01:57:03,988 --> 01:57:05,522
(A top-tier overseas pro team)

2820
01:57:05,523 --> 01:57:06,223
Who's going to take the swing?

2821
01:57:06,224 --> 01:57:08,157
If you don't hit it, who will?

2822
01:57:08,158 --> 01:57:09,493
You want me to swing?

2823
01:57:09,494 --> 01:57:11,561
When you get the opening, rip it!

2824
01:57:12,603 --> 01:57:14,341
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)

2825
01:57:14,365 --> 01:57:17,034
(The Wonder Coach 2)
